test of 'case insensitive equals' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\20250728_120549\\SQLEXPRESS\\SqlSupport_Cpu64_1.log': 'SYSTEM' failed test of 'case insensitive equals' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\20250728_120549\\SQLEXPRESS\\SqlSupport_Cpu64_1.log': 'SYSTEM' failed test of 'case insensitive equals' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\20250728_120549\\SQLEXPRESS\\SqlWriter_Cpu64_1.log': 'SYSTEM' failed test of 'case insensitive equals' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\20250728_120549\\SQLEXPRESS\\sql_common_core_Cpu64_1.log': 'SYSTEM' failed test of 'case insensitive equals' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\20250728_120549\\SQLEXPRESS\\sql_engine_core_inst_Cpu64_1.log': 'SYSTEM' failed test of 'case insensitive equals' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\20250728_120549\\SQLEXPRESS\\sql_engine_core_shared_Cpu64_1.log': 'SYSTEM' failed test of 'case insensitive equals' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\20250728_120549\\SQLEXPRESS\\sql_xevent_Cpu64_1.log': 'SYSTEM' failed test of 'case insensitive equals' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\20251019_102839\\SQLEXPRESS\\AdvancedAnalytics_Cpu64_1.log': 'SYSTEM' failed test of 'case insensitive equals' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\20251019_102839\\SQLEXPRESS\\SqlBrowser_Cpu32_1.log': 'SYSTEM' failed test of 'case insensitive equals' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\20251019_102839\\SQLEXPRESS\\SqlSupport_Cpu64_1.log': 'SYSTEM' failed test of 'case insensitive equals' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\20251019_102839\\SQLEXPRESS\\SqlSupport_Cpu64_1.log': 'SYSTEM' failed test of 'case insensitive equals' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\20251019_102839\\SQLEXPRESS\\SqlWriter_Cpu64_1.log': 'SYSTEM' failed test of 'case insensitive equals' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\20251019_102839\\SQLEXPRESS\\sql_common_core_Cpu64_1.log': 'SYSTEM' failed test of 'case insensitive equals' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\20251019_102839\\SQLEXPRESS\\sql_engine_core_inst_Cpu64_1.log': 'SYSTEM' failed test of 'case insensitive equals' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\20251019_102839\\SQLEXPRESS\\sql_engine_core_shared_Cpu64_1.log': 'SYSTEM' failed test of 'case insensitive equals' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\20251019_102839\\SQLEXPRESS\\sql_xevent_Cpu64_1.log': 'SYSTEM' failed test of 'case insensitive equals' compared to ''\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27128608 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Verify SQL Instance is SQL 2022\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27128612 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'engine' must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27128605 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : Instance is SQL 2022\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'version' must be equal to '2022'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals ''\n","group_tree":{"id":"V-271286","title":"SRG-APP-000133-DB-000198"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-006700","weight":"10.0","status":"open","ia_controls":"","false_positives":"","fix_text":"From a command prompt, open lusrmgr.msc. Navigate to \"Users\" and right-click \"Individual User\". Select \"Properties\", then \"Member Of\". \n \nConfigure SQL Server and OS settings and access controls to restrict user access to objects and data that the user is authorized to view/use.","group_id":"V-271286","check_content":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:var:27128602;;Instance;;user_name;;Array","rule_title":"SQL Server software installation account must be restricted to authorized users.","group_id_src":"V-271286","mitigation_control":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271286","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"potential_impacts":""},{"ia_controls":"","fix_text":"Reinstall SQL Server application components using dedicated directories that are separate from the operating system. \n \nRelocate or reinstall other application software that currently shares directories with SQL Server components separate from the operating system and/or temporary storage.","false_positives":"","rule_version":"SQLI-22-006800","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000133-DB-000199","id":"V-271287"},"status":"not_reviewed","weight":"10.0","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271287, SV-271287r1108843, SRG-APP-000133-DB-000199)\n","mitigation_control":"","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:3501"},"group_id_src":"V-271287","rule_title":"Database software, including DBMS configuration files, must be stored in dedicated directories, separate from the host OS and other applications.","group_id":"V-271287","check_content":"Determine the directory in which SQL Server has been installed:\n\nUsing SQL Server Management Studio's Object Explorer, right-click [SQL Server Instance], select \"Facets\", then record the value of RootDirectory.\n\nDetermine the Operating System directory:\n1. Click \"Start\".\n2. Type \"Run\".\n3. Press \"Enter\".\n4. Type \"%windir%\".\n5. Click \"Ok\".\n6. Record the value in the address bar.\n\nVerify the SQL Server RootDirectory is not in the Operating System directory.\n\nCompare the SQL RootDirectory and the Operating System directory. If the SQL RootDirectory is in the same directory as the Operating System, this is a finding.\n\nVerify the SQL Server RootDirectory is not in another application's directory.\n\nNavigate to the SQL RootDirectory using Windows Explorer.\n\nExamine each directory for evidence another application is stored in it.\n\nIf evidence exists the SQL RootDirectory is in another application's directory, this is a finding.\n\nIf the SQL RootDirectory is not in the Operating System directory or another application's directory, this is not a finding.\n\nExamples:\n1. The Operating System directory is \"C:\\Windows\". The SQL RootDirectory is \"D:\\Program Files\\MSSQLSERVER\\MSSQL\". The MSSQLSERVER directory is not living in the Operating System directory or the directory of another application. This is not a finding.\n\n2. The Operating System directory is \"C:\\Windows\". The SQL RootDirectory is \"C:\\Windows\\MSSQLSERVER\\MSSQL\". This is a finding.\n\n3. The Operating System directory is \"C:\\Windows\". The SQL RootDirectory is \"D:\\Program Files\\Microsoft Office\\MSSQLSERVER\\MSSQL\". The MSSQLSERVER directory is in the Microsoft Office directory, which indicates Microsoft Office is installed here. This is a finding.","rule_id":"SV-271287r1108843","ccis":["CCI-001499"],"uuid":"F201632E-6BF8-1014-B9CB-F41DFC5C203D","mitigations":"","comments":null,"documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"group_title":"SRG-APP-000133-DB-000199","discussion":"When dealing with change control issues, it should be noted any changes to the hardware, software, and/or firmware components of the information system and/or application can potentially have significant effects on the overall security of the system. \n \nMultiple applications can provide a cumulative negative effect. A vulnerability and subsequent exploit to one application can lead to an exploit of other applications sharing the same security context. For example, an exploit to a web server process that leads to unauthorized administrative access to host system directories can most likely lead to a compromise of all applications hosted by the same system. Database software not installed using dedicated directories both threatens and is threatened by other hosted applications. Access controls defined for one application may by default provide access to the other application's database objects or directories. Any method that provides any level of separation of security context assists in the protection between applications.","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","security_override_guidance":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271287r1108843_rule"},{"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_id":"SV-271290r1109112","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","uuid":"F2016A03-6BF8-1014-BF3A-ED810F359358","mitigations":"","comments":null,"reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","discussion":"Information systems are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the default functions and services may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n \nIt is detrimental for software products to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. Examples include, but are not limited to, installing advertising software, demonstrations, or browser plugins not related to requirements or providing a wide array of functionality, not required for every mission, that cannot be disabled. \n \nDBMSs must adhere to the principles of least functionality by providing only essential capabilities. \n \nDemonstration and sample database objects and applications present publicly known attack points for malicious users. These demonstration and sample objects are meant to provide simple examples of coding specific functions and are not developed to prevent vulnerabilities from being introduced to SQL Server and host system.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000090","rule_id_src":"SV-271290r1109112_rule","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","security_override_guidance":"","fix_text":"Remove all demonstration or sample databases from production instances.","false_positives":"","ia_controls":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Check if pubs, Northwinds, AdventureWorks, or WorldwideImporter databases are present.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27129001 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Check if pubs, Northwinds, AdventureWorks, or WorldwideImporter databases are present.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27129001 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name FROM sysdatabases WHERE name LIKE 'Northwind' OR name LIKE 'AdventureWorks' OR name LIKE 'pubs' OR name LIKE 'WorldwideImporters';'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql does not exist\n","weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","group_tree":{"id":"V-271290","title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000090"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-006900","group_id_src":"V-271290","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271290","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"mitigation_control":"","check_content":"Review vendor documentation and vendor websites to identify vendor-provided demonstration or sample databases, database applications, objects, and files. Review the SQL Server to determine if any of the demonstration and sample databases, database applications, or files are installed in the database or included with the SQL Server Instance. \n\nRun the following query to check for names matching known sample databases. Sample databases may have been renamed, so this is not an exhaustive list.\n\nSELECT name\nFROM sys.databases\nWHERE name LIKE '%pubs%'\nOR name LIKE '%northwind%'\nOR name LIKE '%adventureworks%'\nOR name LIKE '%wideworldimporters%'\nOR name LIKE '%contoso%'\n\nIf any sample databases are found, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271290","rule_title":"Default demonstration and sample databases, database objects, and applications must be removed."},{"uuid":"F201799F-6BF8-1014-A536-B1FA54BC473C","comments":null,"mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","rule_id":"SV-271291r1108899","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271291r1108899_rule","discussion":"Information systems are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the default functions and services may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n \nIt is detrimental for software products to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. \n \nDBMSs must adhere to the principles of least functionality by providing only essential capabilities.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000091","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","status":"open","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-271291","title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000091"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-007000","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Verify SQL 2022 Setup Bootstrap Log must exist (run 'Installed SQL 2022 Server features discovery report' if not found))\nTest                    :   true (Verify SQL Instance is SQL 2022)\nTest                    :   false (Compare SQL 2022 Installed Features against system documentation (run 'Installed SQL 2022 Server features discovery report' if no features found))\nResult Analysis         :        For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\Summary.txt': '  SQL Server 2022      SQLEXPRESS           MSSQL16.SQLEXPRESS             Database Engine Services                 1033                 Express Edition      16.0.1140.6     No         Yes       ' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\Summary.txt': '  SQL Server 2022      SQLEXPRESS           MSSQL16.SQLEXPRESS             SQL Server Replication                   1033                 Express Edition      16.0.1140.6     No         Yes       ' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\Summary.txt': '  SQL Server 2022      SQLEXPRESS           MSSQL16.SQLEXPRESS             Full-Text and Semantic Extractions for Search 1033                 Express Edition      16.0.1000.6     No         Yes       ' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\Summary.txt': '  SQL Server 2022      SQLEXPRESS           MSSQL16.SQLEXPRESS             Machine Learning Services and Language Extensions 1033                 Express Edition      16.0.1140.6     No         Yes       ' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to ''\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27129110 (file_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Verify SQL 2022 Setup Bootstrap Log must exist (run 'Installed SQL 2022 Server features discovery report' if not found)\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27129113 (file_object)\nObject Comment          : SQL 2022 Setup Bootstrap Log must exist\nObject Requirement      : for filepath, all of the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     filepath must be equal to 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\Summary.txt'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\Summary.txt'\n                        : path equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log'\n                        : filename equals 'Summary.txt'\n                        : owner equals 'BUILTIN\\Administrators'\n                        : size equals '3759'\n                        : a_time equals '134053578100000000'\n                        : c_time equals '133513674700000000'\n                        : m_time equals '134053578100000000'\n                        : ms_checksum does not exist\n                        : version does not exist\n                        : type equals 'FILE_TYPE_DISK'\n                        : attribute equals 'FILE_ATTRIBUTE_ARCHIVE'\n                        : development_class does not exist\n                        : company does not exist\n                        : internal_name does not exist\n                        : language does not exist\n                        : original_filename does not exist\n                        : product_name does not exist\n                        : product_version does not exist\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27129112 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Verify SQL Instance is SQL 2022\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27129116 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'engine' must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27129105 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : Instance is SQL 2022\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'version' must be equal to '2022'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals ''\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27129111 (textfilecontent54_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Compare SQL 2022 Installed Features against system documentation (run 'Installed SQL 2022 Server features discovery report' if no features found)\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27129115 (textfilecontent54_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather SQL 2022 Installed Product Features\nObject Requirement      : for filepath, all of the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     filepath must be equal to 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\Summary.txt'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'pattern' must match the pattern '^  SQL Server 2022      .*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must be greater than or equal to '1'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27129101 (textfilecontent54_state)\nState Comment           : Check SQL bootstrap logs for user approved list of features/products\nState Requirement       : for alltext, at least one of the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     text must match the pattern ''\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\Summary.txt'\n                        : path equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log'\n                        : filename equals 'Summary.txt'\n                        : pattern equals '^  SQL Server 2022      .*'\n                        : instance equals '1'\n                        : text equals '  SQL Server 2022      SQLEXPRESS           MSSQL16.SQLEXPRESS             Database Engine Services                 1033                 Express Edition      16.0.1140.6     No         Yes       '\n                        : subexpression does not exist\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\Summary.txt'\n                        : path equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log'\n                        : filename equals 'Summary.txt'\n                        : pattern equals '^  SQL Server 2022      .*'\n                        : instance equals '2'\n                        : text equals '  SQL Server 2022      SQLEXPRESS           MSSQL16.SQLEXPRESS             SQL Server Replication                   1033                 Express Edition      16.0.1140.6     No         Yes       '\n                        : subexpression does not exist\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\Summary.txt'\n                        : path equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log'\n                        : filename equals 'Summary.txt'\n                        : pattern equals '^  SQL Server 2022      .*'\n                        : instance equals '3'\n                        : text equals '  SQL Server 2022      SQLEXPRESS           MSSQL16.SQLEXPRESS             Full-Text and Semantic Extractions for Search 1033                 Express Edition      16.0.1000.6     No         Yes       '\n                        : subexpression does not exist\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\Summary.txt'\n                        : path equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log'\n                        : filename equals 'Summary.txt'\n                        : pattern equals '^  SQL Server 2022      .*'\n                        : instance equals '4'\n                        : text equals '  SQL Server 2022      SQLEXPRESS           MSSQL16.SQLEXPRESS             Machine Learning Services and Language Extensions 1033                 Express Edition      16.0.1140.6     No         Yes       '\n                        : subexpression does not exist\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nResult Analysis         : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\Summary.txt': '  SQL Server 2022      SQLEXPRESS           MSSQL16.SQLEXPRESS             Database Engine Services                 1033                 Express Edition      16.0.1140.6     No         Yes       ' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\Summary.txt': '  SQL Server 2022      SQLEXPRESS           MSSQL16.SQLEXPRESS             SQL Server Replication                   1033                 Express Edition      16.0.1140.6     No         Yes       ' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\Summary.txt': '  SQL Server 2022      SQLEXPRESS           MSSQL16.SQLEXPRESS             Full-Text and Semantic Extractions for Search 1033                 Express Edition      16.0.1000.6     No         Yes       ' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to ''\n                        : For 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Log\\Summary.txt': '  SQL Server 2022      SQLEXPRESS           MSSQL16.SQLEXPRESS             Machine Learning Services and Language Extensions 1033                 Express Edition      16.0.1140.6     No         Yes       ' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to ''\n","fix_text":"Remove all features that are not required.","false_positives":"","ia_controls":"","rule_title":"Unused database components, DBMS software, and database objects must be removed.","check_content":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:var:27129102;;Instance;;feature;;Array","group_id":"V-271291","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271291","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-271291"},{"uuid":"F20183D9-6BF8-1014-93D5-88D3F9229370","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","rule_id":"SV-271292r1111143","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271292r1111143_rule","discussion":"SQL Server is capable of providing a wide range of features and services. Some of the default features and services may not be necessary and enabling them could adversely affect the security of the system.\n\nEnabling the replication Xps opens a significant attack surface area that can be used by an attacker to gather information about the system and potentially abuse the privileges of SQL Server.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000092","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","severity":"medium","weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","rule_version":"SQLI-22-017900","group_tree":{"id":"V-271292","title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000092"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (If the value of 'config_value' is '0', this is not a finding.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27129201 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If the value of 'config_value' is '0', this is not a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27129201 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'replication xps';'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27129201 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : SQL query result field 'name' = 'replication xps' and config_value = 0\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all name must be equal (case insensitive) to 'replication xps'\n                        : all value_in_use must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'replication xps';'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : value = '0'\n                        : value_in_use = '0'\n                        : name = 'Replication XPs'\n","fix_text":"Disable use of or remove any external application executable object definitions that are not approved.\n\nTo disable the use of [Replication Xps] option, from the query prompt:\nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'show advanced options', 1;  \nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE;\nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'replication xps', 0;\nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE;\nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'show advanced options', 0;  \nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE;\nGO  \nRECONFIGURE;  \nGO","false_positives":"","ia_controls":"","rule_title":"The SQL Server Replication Xps feature must be disabled unless specifically required and approved.","check_content":"To determine if [Replication Xps] is enabled, execute the following command:\nSELECT name, value, value_in_use\nFROM sys.configurations\nWHERE name = 'Replication Xps'\n \nIf [value_in_use] is a [1], review the system documentation to determine whether the use of [Replication Xps] is approved. If it is not approved, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271292","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271292","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-271292"},{"ia_controls":"","fix_text":"Disable use of or remove any external application executable object definitions that are not approved.\n\nTo disable the use of [External Scripts Enabled] option, from the query prompt:\nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'External Scripts Enabled', 0;\nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE;","false_positives":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000092","id":"V-271293"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-017700","weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (If the value of 'config_value' is '0', this is not a finding.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27129301 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If the value of 'config_value' is '0', this is not a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27129301 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'external scripts enabled'; '\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27129301 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : SQL query result field 'name' = 'external scripts enabled' and config_value = 0\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all name must be equal (case insensitive) to 'external scripts enabled'\n                        : all value_in_use must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'external scripts enabled'; '\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : name = 'external scripts enabled'\n                        : value = '0'\n                        : value_in_use = '0'\n","mitigation_control":"","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271293"},"group_id_src":"V-271293","rule_title":"The SQL Server External Scripts Enabled feature must be disabled, unless specifically required and approved.","group_id":"V-271293","check_content":" To determine if [External Scripts Enabled] is enabled, execute the following command:\nSELECT name, value, value_in_use\nFROM sys.configurations\nWHERE name = 'External Scripts Enabled'\n \nIf [value_in_use] is a [1], review the system documentation to determine whether the use of [External Scripts Enabled] is approved. If it is not approved, this is a finding.","rule_id":"SV-271293r1111138","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"uuid":"F2018E16-6BF8-1014-9BF4-A259564216C1","comments":null,"mitigations":"","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000092","discussion":"SQL Server is capable of providing a wide range of features and services. Some of the default features and services may not be necessary and enabling them could adversely affect the security of the system.\n\nThe External Scripts Enabled feature allows scripts external to SQL such as files located in an R library to be executed.","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","security_override_guidance":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271293r1111138_rule"},{"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_id":"SV-271295r1111135","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","uuid":"F2019C25-6BF8-1014-A694-A59FE0333D9C","severity":"medium","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093","discussion":"Information systems are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the default functions and services may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n\nIt is detrimental for applications to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. \n\nApplications must adhere to the principles of least functionality by providing only essential capabilities.\n\nSQL Server may spawn additional external processes to execute procedures that are defined in theÂ SQL ServerÂ but stored in external host files (external procedures). The spawned process used to execute the external procedure may operate within a different OS security context than SQL Server and provide unauthorized access to the host system.\n\nSQL Server is capable of providing a wide range of features and services. Some of the features and services, provided by default, may not be necessary, and enabling them could adversely affect the security of the system.\n\nThe Remote Data Archive feature allowsÂ an export of local SQL Server data to an Azure SQL Database. An exploit to the SQL Server instance could result in a compromise of the host system and external SQL Server resources.","rule_id_src":"SV-271295r1111135_rule","security_override_guidance":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","ia_controls":"","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Disable use of or remove any external application executable object definitions that are not approved.\n\nTo disable the use of [Remote Data Archive] option, from the query prompt: \nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'Remote Data Archive', 0;\nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE;","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (If the value of 'config_value' is '0', this is not a finding.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27129501 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If the value of 'config_value' is '0', this is not a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27129501 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'remote data archive';'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27129501 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : SQL query result field 'name' = 'remote data archive' and config_value = 0\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all name must be equal (case insensitive) to 'remote data archive'\n                        : all value_in_use must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'remote data archive';'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : value = '0'\n                        : value_in_use = '0'\n                        : name = 'remote data archive'\n","rule_version":"SQLI-22-017600","group_tree":{"id":"V-271295","title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093"},"weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","group_id_src":"V-271295","mitigation_control":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271295","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-271295","check_content":"To determine if [Remote Data Archive] is enabled, execute the following command:\nSELECT name, value, value_in_use\nFROM sys.configurations\nWHERE name = 'Remote Data Archive'\n \nIf [value_in_use] is a [1], review the system documentation to determine whether the use of [Remote Data Archive] is approved. If it is not approved, this is a finding.","rule_title":"The remote Data Archive feature must be disabled unless specifically required and approved."},{"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","severity":"medium","discussion":"Information systems are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the default functions and services may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n\nIt is detrimental for applications to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. \n\nApplications must adhere to the principles of least functionality by providing only essential capabilities.\n\nSQL Server may spawn additional external processes to execute procedures that are defined in theÂ SQL ServerÂ but stored in external host files (external procedures). The spawned process used to execute the external procedure may operate within a different OS security context than SQL Server and provide unauthorized access to the host system.\n\nThe Allow Polybase Export feature allows an export of data to an external data source such as Hadoop File System or Azure Data Lake. An exploit to the SQL Server instance could result in a compromise of the host system and external SQL Server resources.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093","rule_id_src":"SV-271296r1111132_rule","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_id":"SV-271296r1111132","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","uuid":"F201A4E0-6BF8-1014-80E7-8BD6CF0B0CF1","mitigations":"","comments":null,"group_id_src":"V-271296","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271296","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"mitigation_control":"","check_content":"To determine if [Allow Polybase Export] is enabled, execute the following command:\nSELECT name, value, value_in_use\nFROM sys.configurations\nWHERE name = 'Allow Polybase Export'\n \nIf [value_in_use] is a [1], review the system documentation to determine whether the use of [Allow Polybase Export] is approved. If it is not approved, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271296","rule_title":"The \"Allow Polybase Export\" feature must be disabled, unless specifically required and approved.","fix_text":"Disable use of or remove any external application executable object definitions that are not approved.\n\nTo disable the use of [Allow Polybase Export] option, from the query prompt: \nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'Allow Polybase Export', 0;\nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE;","false_positives":"","ia_controls":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (If the value of 'config_value' is '0', this is not a finding.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27129601 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If the value of 'config_value' is '0', this is not a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27129601 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'allow polybase export';'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27129601 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : SQL query result field 'name' = 'allow polybase export' and config_value = 0\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all name must be equal (case insensitive) to 'allow polybase export'\n                        : all value_in_use must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'allow polybase export';'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : name = 'allow polybase export'\n                        : value_in_use = '0'\n                        : value = '0'\n","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-271296","title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-017500"},{"status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-271297","title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-017400","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (If the value of 'config_value' is '0', this is not a finding.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27129701 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If the value of 'config_value' is '0', this is not a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27129701 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'hadoop connectivity';'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27129701 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : SQL query result field 'name' = 'hadoop connectivity' and config_value = 0\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all name must be equal (case insensitive) to 'hadoop connectivity'\n                        : all value_in_use must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'hadoop connectivity';'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : value = '0'\n                        : value_in_use = '0'\n                        : name = 'hadoop connectivity'\n","fix_text":"Disable use of or remove any external application executable object definitions that are not approved.\n\nTo disable the use of [Hadoop Connectivity] option, from the query prompt:\nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE  'hadoop connectivity', 0;  \nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE;  ","false_positives":"","ia_controls":"","rule_title":"The \"Hadoop Connectivity\" feature must be disabled unless specifically required and approved.","check_content":"To determine if [Hadoop Connectivity] is enabled, execute the following command:\nSELECT name, value, value_in_use\nFROM sys.configurations\nWHERE name = 'Hadoop Connectivity'\n \nIf [value_in_use] is a [1], review the system documentation to determine whether the use of [Hadoop Connectivity] is approved. If it is not approved, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271297","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271297","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-271297","uuid":"F201AD6C-6BF8-1014-99C5-85D7F1E617AA","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","rule_id":"SV-271297r1111129","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271297r1111129_rule","discussion":"Information systems are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the default functions and services may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n\nIt is detrimental for applications to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. \n\nApplications must adhere to the principles of least functionality by providing only essential capabilities.\n\nSQL Server may spawn additional external processes to execute procedures that are defined in theÂ SQL ServerÂ but stored in external host files (external procedures). The spawned process used to execute the external procedure may operate within a different OS security context than SQL Server and provide unauthorized access to the host system.\n\nSQL Server is capable of providing a wide range of features and services. Some of the features and services, provided by default, may not be necessary, and enabling them could adversely affect the security of the system.\n\nThe \"Hadoop Connectivity\" feature allows multiple types of external data sources to be created and used across all sessions on the server. An exploit to the SQL Server instance could result in a compromise of the host system and external SQL Server resources.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","severity":"medium"},{"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_id":"SV-271298r1111126","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","uuid":"F201B653-6BF8-1014-9456-F55B389A8C11","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093","discussion":"Information systems are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the default functions and services may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n\nIt is detrimental for applications to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. \n\nApplications must adhere to the principles of least functionality by providing only essential capabilities.\n\nSQL Server may spawn additional external processes to execute procedures that are defined in theÂ SQL ServerÂ but stored in external host files (external procedures). The spawned process used to execute the external procedure may operate within a different OS security context than SQL Server and provide unauthorized access to the host system.\n\nThe \"Remote Access\" option controls the execution of local stored procedures on remote servers or remote stored procedures on local server. Remote access functionality can be abused to launch a denial-of-service (DoS) attack on remote servers by off-loading query processing to a target.","rule_id_src":"SV-271298r1111126_rule","security_override_guidance":"","third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Disable use of [Remote Access] if it is not authorized.\n \nTo disable the use of [Remote Access], from the query prompt: \nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'remote access', 0;\nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE;","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (If the value of 'config_value' is '0', this is not a finding.)\nResult Analysis         :        value_in_use = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27129801 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : If the value of 'config_value' is '0', this is not a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27129801 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'remote access''\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27129801 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : SQL query result field 'name' = 'remote access' and config_value = 0\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all name must be equal (case insensitive) to 'remote access'\n                        : all value_in_use must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'remote access''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : !![ value_in_use = '1' ]!!\n                        : !![ value = '1' ]!!\n                        : name = 'remote access'\n\nResult Analysis         : value_in_use = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n","rule_version":"SQLI-22-017200","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093","id":"V-271298"},"status":"open","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-271298","mitigation_control":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271298","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-271298","check_content":"To determine if [Remote Access] is enabled, execute the following command:\nSELECT name, value, value_in_use\nFROM sys.configurations\nWHERE name = 'Remote Access'\n \nIf [value_in_use] is a [1], review the system documentation to determine whether the use of [Remote Access] is approved. If it is not approved, this is a finding.","rule_title":"The \"Remote Access\" feature must be disabled unless specifically required and approved."},{"status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-271299","title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-007500","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Review the system documentation to determine whether the linked servers listed are required and approved. If it is not approved, this is a finding.)\nTest                    :   true (If a login in the list is impersonating sysadmin and system documentation does not require this, it is a finding.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27129901 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Review the system documentation to determine whether the linked servers listed are required and approved. If it is not approved, this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27129901 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT \n                        :   name as linked_server,\n                        :   provider,\n                        :   data_source\n                        : FROM sys.servers\n                        : WHERE is_linked = 1;'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27129901 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : If the value of 'linked_server' is approved and documented, then this is not a finding.\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : Field Requirement       : for at least one linked_server, at least one of the following must be true:\n                        : Field Requirement       : linked_server must be equal (case insensitive) to  the value(s) in End user provided list of required and approved linked servers\n                        : Field Requirement       :     linked_server must be equal (case insensitive) to ''\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql does not exist\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27129902 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If a login in the list is impersonating sysadmin and system documentation does not require this, it is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27129902 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT s.name as linked_server, p.principal_id, USER_NAME(p.principal_id) as user_name, l.remote_name as remote_user_name \n                        : FROM sys.servers s \n                        : JOIN sys.linked_logins l ON s.server_id = l.server_id \n                        : LEFT JOIN sys.server_principals p ON l.local_principal_id = p.principal_id \n                        : WHERE s.is_linked = 1 AND l.remote_name is not null'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql does not exist\n","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Remove any linked servers and all associated logins that are not authorized. \n \nTo remove a linked server and all associated logins run the following: \n \nsp_dropserver 'LinkedServerName', 'droplogins'; \n \nTo remove a login from a linked server run the following: \n \nEXEC sp_droplinkedsrvlogin 'LoginName', NULL;","ia_controls":"","rule_title":"Access to linked servers must be disabled or restricted, unless specifically required and approved.","check_content":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:var:27129904;;Instance;;linked_server;;Array","group_id":"V-271299","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271299"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-271299","comments":null,"mitigations":"","uuid":"F201C7E4-6BF8-1014-9F15-83EEB34CA7BC","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","rule_id":"SV-271299r1108513","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271299r1108513_rule","discussion":"Information systems are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the default functions and services may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n\nIt is detrimental for applications to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. \n\nApplications must adhere to the principles of least functionality by providing only essential capabilities. \n\nSQL Server may spawn additional external processes to execute procedures that are defined in the SQL Server but stored in external host files (external procedures). The spawned process used to execute the external procedure may operate within a different OS security context than SQL Server and provide unauthorized access to the host system. \n\nA linked server allows for access to distributed, heterogeneous queries against OLE DB data sources. After a linked server is created, distributed queries can be run against this server, and queries can join tables from more than one data source. If the linked server is defined as an instance of SQL Server, remote stored procedures can be executed. This access may be exploited by malicious users who have compromised the integrity of the SQL Server.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","severity":"medium"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (If any records are returned, review the system documentation to determine whether the use of Non-Standard extended stored procedures are required and approved.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27130001 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If any records are returned, review the system documentation to determine whether the use of Non-Standard extended stored procedures are required and approved.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27130001 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to '\n                        : DECLARE @xplist AS TABLE\n                        : (\n                        :        xp_name sysname,\n                        :        source_dll nvarchar(255)\n                        : )\n                        : INSERT INTO @xplist\n                        : EXEC sp_helpextendedproc\n                        : \n                        : SELECT X.xp_name, X.source_dll, O.is_ms_shipped FROM @xplist X JOIN sys.all_objects O ON X.xp_name = O.name WHERE O.is_ms_shipped = 0 ORDER BY X.xp_name'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql does not exist\n","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093","id":"V-271300"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-007400","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Remove any nonstandard extended stored procedures that are not documented and approved using the following:\n \nsp_dropextendedproc 'proc name'","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Extended stored procedures are DLLs that an instance of SQL Server can dynamically load and run. Extended stored procedures run directly in the address space of an instance of SQL Server and are programmed by using the SQL Server Extended Stored Procedure API.  \n \nNonstandard extended stored procedures can compromise the integrity of the SQL Server process. This feature will be removed in a future version of SQL Server. Do not use this feature in new development work and modify applications that currently use this feature as soon as possible. \n \nTo determine if nonstandard extended stored procedures exist, run the following:\n\nUSE [master]\nGO\nDECLARE @xplist AS TABLE\n(\n       xp_name sysname,\n       source_dll nvarchar(255)\n)\nINSERT INTO @xplist\nEXEC sp_helpextendedproc\n\nSELECT X.xp_name, X.source_dll, O.is_ms_shipped FROM @xplist X JOIN sys.all_objects O ON X.xp_name = O.name WHERE O.is_ms_shipped = 0 ORDER BY X.xp_name\n \nIf any records are returned, review the system documentation to determine whether the use of nonstandard extended stored procedures are required and approved.\n\nIf it is not approved, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271300","rule_title":"Access to nonstandard, extended stored procedures must be disabled or restricted, unless specifically required and approved.","group_id_src":"V-271300","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271300"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":"","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","comments":null,"mitigations":"","uuid":"F201D42B-6BF8-1014-B1B2-A16F1557AF26","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_id":"SV-271300r1109264","rule_id_src":"SV-271300r1109264_rule","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","severity":"medium","discussion":"Information systems are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the default functions and services may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n \nIt is detrimental for applications to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. \n \nApplications must adhere to the principles of least functionality by providing only essential capabilities. \n \nSQL Server may spawn additional external processes to execute procedures that are defined in the SQL Server but stored in external host files (external procedures). The spawned process used to execute the external procedure may operate within a different OS security context than SQL Server and provide unauthorized access to the host system. \n \nExtended stored procedures are DLLs that an instance of SQL Server can dynamically load and run. Extended stored procedures run directly in the address space of an instance of SQL Server and are programmed by using the SQL Server Extended Stored Procedure API. Nonstandard extended stored procedures can compromise the integrity of the SQL Server process. This feature will be removed in a future version of Microsoft SQL Server. Do not use this feature in new development work and modify applications that currently use this feature as soon as possible.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093"},{"ia_controls":"","fix_text":"Disable use of or remove any CLR code that is not authorized.\n\nTo disable the use of CLR, from the query prompt:  \n \nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'clr enabled', 0;\nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE;\n\nFor any approved CLR code with Unsafe or External permissions, use the ALTER ASSEMBLY to change the permission set for the assembly and ensure a certificate is configured.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Check CLR is disabled.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27130101 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Check CLR is disabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27130101 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'clr enabled''\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27130101 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : If the value of 'value_in_use' is '0', this is not a finding.\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all name must be equal (case insensitive) to 'clr enabled'\n                        : all value_in_use must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'clr enabled''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : name = 'clr enabled'\n                        : value_in_use = '0'\n                        : value = '0'\n","rule_version":"SQLI-22-007300","group_tree":{"id":"V-271301","title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093"},"status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-271301","mitigation_control":"","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271301"},"group_id":"V-271301","check_content":"To determine if [CLR] is enabled, execute the following command:  \n\nSELECT name, value, value_in_use\nFROM sys.configurations\nWHERE name = 'clr enabled'\n \nIf [value_in_use] is a [1], review the system documentation to determine whether the use of [CLR] is approved. If it is not approved, this is a finding.","rule_title":"Access to common language runtime (CLR) code must be disabled or restricted unless specifically required and approved.","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_id":"SV-271301r1109114","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"uuid":"F201DC95-6BF8-1014-BAC4-CEE3ADE4D028","mitigations":"","comments":null,"severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093","discussion":"Information systems are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the default functions and services may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n \nIt is detrimental for applications to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. \n \nApplications must adhere to the principles of least functionality by providing only essential capabilities. \n \nSQL Server may spawn additional external processes to execute procedures that are defined in the SQL Server but stored in external host files (external procedures). The spawned process used to execute the external procedure may operate within a different OS security context than SQL Server and provide unauthorized access to the host system. \n \nThe CLR component of the .NET Framework for Microsoft Windows in SQL Server allows users to write stored procedures, triggers, user-defined types, user-defined functions, user-defined aggregates, and streaming table-valued functions, using any .NET Framework language, including Microsoft Visual Basic .NET and Microsoft Visual C#. CLR packing assemblies can access resources protected by .NET Code Access Security when it runs managed code. Specifying UNSAFE enables the code in the assembly complete freedom to perform operations in the SQL Server process space that can potentially compromise the robustness of SQL Server. UNSAFE assemblies can also potentially subvert the security system of either SQL Server or the common language runtime.","rule_id_src":"SV-271301r1109114_rule","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":""},{"discussion":"Information systems are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the default functions and services may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n \nIt is detrimental for applications to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. \n \nApplications must adhere to the principles of least functionality by providing only essential capabilities. \n \nSQL Server may spawn additional external processes to execute procedures that are defined in the SQL Server but stored in external host files (external procedures). The spawned process used to execute the external procedure may operate within a different OS security context than SQL Server and provide unauthorized access to the host system. \n \nThe xp_cmdshell extended stored procedure allows execution of host executables outside the controls of database access permissions. This access may be exploited by malicious users who have compromised the integrity of the SQL Server database process to control the host operating system to perpetrate additional malicious activity.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271302r1109113_rule","rule_id":"SV-271302r1109113","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"mitigations":"","comments":null,"uuid":"F201E76B-6BF8-1014-9081-A4BF11CADEA0","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271302","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-271302","rule_title":"Access to xp_cmdshell must be disabled unless specifically required and approved.","check_content":"To determine if [xp_cmdshell] is enabled, execute the following command:  \n\nSELECT name, value, value_in_use\nFROM sys.configurations\nWHERE name = 'xp_cmdshell'\n \nIf [value_in_use] is a [1], review the system documentation to determine whether the use of [xp_cmdshell] is approved. If it is not approved, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271302","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Disable use of or remove any external application executable object definitions that are not approved.\n\nTo disable the use of xp_cmdshell, from the query prompt: \n\nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'show advanced options', 1;  \nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE;\nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'xp_cmdshell', 0;\nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE;\nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'show advanced options', 0;  \nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE;","ia_controls":"","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093","id":"V-271302"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-007200","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Check if xp_cmdshell is disabled.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27130201 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Check if xp_cmdshell is disabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27130201 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'xp_cmdshell''\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27130201 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : SQL query result name=xp_cmdshell and value_in_use = 0\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all name must be equal (case insensitive) to 'xp_cmdshell'\n                        : all value_in_use must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'xp_cmdshell''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : value = '0'\n                        : value_in_use = '0'\n                        : name = 'xp_cmdshell'\n"},{"rule_title":"SQL Server must be configured to prohibit or restrict the use of organization-defined ports, as defined in the Ports, Protocols, and Services Management (PPSM) Category Assurance List (CAL) and vulnerability assessments.","check_content":"Review SQL Server Configuration for the ports used by SQL Server. \n \nTo determine whether SQL Server is configured to use a fixed port or dynamic ports, in the right-side pane, double-click on the TCP/IP entry to open the Properties dialog. (The default fixed port is 1433.) \n\nAlternatively, run the following SQL query to determine the port used by SQL Server:\n\nSELECT ISNULL(CONVERT(VARCHAR(25),local_tcp_port),'Dynamic Ports are Enabled')\nFROM   sys.dm_exec_connections\nWHERE  session_id = @@SPID\n \nIf any ports in use are in conflict with PPSM guidance and not explained and approved in the system documentation, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271303","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:6101"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-271303","weight":"10.0","status":"not_reviewed","rule_version":"SQLI-22-007700","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000142-DB-000094","id":"V-271303"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271303, SV-271303r1109116, SRG-APP-000142-DB-000094)\n","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Use SQL Server Configuration to change the ports used by SQL Server to comply with PPSM guidance, or document the need for other ports, and obtain written approval. Close ports no longer needed.","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271303r1109116_rule","discussion":"To prevent unauthorized connection of devices, unauthorized transfer of information, or unauthorized tunneling (i.e., embedding of data types within data types), organizations must disable or restrict unused or unnecessary physical and logical ports on information systems. \n \nApplications are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the functions and services provided by default may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations. Additionally, it is sometimes convenient to provide multiple services from a single component (e.g., email and web services); however, doing so increases risk over limiting the services provided by any one component. \n \nTo support the requirements and principles of least functionality, the application must support the organizational requirements providing only essential capabilities and limiting the use of ports to only those required, authorized, and approved to conduct official business or to address authorized quality of life issues. \n \nSQL Server using ports deemed unsafe is open to attack through those ports. This can allow unauthorized access to the database and through the database to other components of the information system.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000142-DB-000094","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","comments":null,"mitigations":"","uuid":"F201F439-6BF8-1014-A15C-94A9C22525D2","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","rule_id":"SV-271303r1109116","ccis":["CCI-000382"]},{"ccis":["CCI-000382"],"rule_id":"SV-271304r1109265","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","mitigations":"","comments":null,"uuid":"F201FADF-6BF8-1014-89C5-C3DE8C8FB43A","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","severity":"medium","discussion":"To prevent unauthorized connection of devices, unauthorized transfer of information, or unauthorized tunneling (i.e., embedding of data types within data types), organizations must disable or restrict unused or unnecessary protocols on information systems. \n \nApplications are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the functions and services provided by default may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations. Additionally, it is sometimes convenient to provide multiple services from a single component (e.g., email and web services); however, doing so increases risk over limiting the services provided by any one component. \n \nTo support the requirements and principles of least functionality, the application must support the organizational requirements providing only essential capabilities and limiting the use of protocols to only those required, authorized, and approved to conduct official business or to address authorized quality of life issues. \n \nSQL Server using protocols deemed unsafe is open to attack through those protocols. This can allow unauthorized access to the database and through the database to other components of the information system.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-APP-000142-DB-000094, SRG-APP-000383-DB-000364","group_title":"SRG-APP-000142-DB-000094","rule_id_src":"SV-271304r1109265_rule","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","security_override_guidance":"","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Navigate to SQL Server Configuration Manager &gt;&gt; SQL Server Network Configuration &gt;&gt; Protocols, then right-click on each listed protocol that is enabled but not authorized and select \"Disable\".","ia_controls":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271304, SV-271304r1109265, SRG-APP-000142-DB-000094)\n","weight":"10.0","status":"not_reviewed","rule_version":"SQLI-22-007600","group_tree":{"id":"V-271304","title":"SRG-APP-000142-DB-000094"},"group_id_src":"V-271304","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:6301","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":"","check_content":"To determine the protocol(s) enabled for SQL Server, open SQL Server Configuration Manager. In the left pane, expand SQL Server Network Configuration. Click on the entry for the SQL Server instance under review: \"Protocols for\". The right-side pane displays the protocols enabled for the instance. \n\nAlternatively, run the following SQL Script and review the registry_key for enabled protocols.\n\nSELECT \n*\nFROM sys.dm_server_registry\nWHERE registry_key like 'HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\%\\MSSQLServer\\SuperSocketNetLib\\%'\n   AND value_name = 'enabled'\n   AND value_data = 1\n \nIf any listed protocols are enabled but not documented and authorized, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271304","rule_title":"SQL Server must be configured to prohibit or restrict the use of organization-defined protocols as defined in the Ports, Protocols, and Services Management (PPSM) Category Assurance List (CAL) and vulnerability assessments."},{"rule_id_src":"SV-271305r1109239_rule","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","severity":"medium","discussion":"To ensure accountability and prevent unauthenticated access, organizational users must be identified and authenticated to prevent potential misuse and compromise of the system. \n \nOrganizational users include organizational employees or individuals the organization deems to have equivalent status of employees (e.g., contractors). Organizational users (and any processes acting on behalf of users) must be uniquely identified and authenticated for all accesses, except the following: \n \n(i) Accesses explicitly identified and documented by the organization. Organizations document specific user actions that can be performed on the information system without identification or authentication; and  \n(ii) Accesses that occur through authorized use of group authenticators without individual authentication. Organizations may require unique identification of individuals using shared accounts for detailed accountability of individual activity.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-APP-000148-DB-000103, SRG-APP-000180-DB-000115","group_title":"SRG-APP-000148-DB-000103","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","comments":null,"mitigations":"","uuid":"F20210BB-6BF8-1014-8C10-E288E53B19D6","ccis":["CCI-000764","CCI-000804"],"rule_id":"SV-271305r1109239","check_content":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:var:27126904;;Instance;;user_name;;Array","group_id":"V-271305","rule_title":"SQL Server must uniquely identify and authenticate users (or processes acting on behalf of organizational users).","group_id_src":"V-271305","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271269","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (If shared identifiers are found, and not accompanied by individual identifiers, this is a finding.)\nResult Analysis         :        Collected Item did not meet the state requirement.\nTest                    :   true (If logins are links to computer accounts this is a finding.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27126901 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : If shared identifiers are found, and not accompanied by individual identifiers, this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27126901 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : Non-computer accounts\nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name AS user_name, type_desc AS account_type, is_disabled\n                        : FROM sys.server_principals\n                        : WHERE type in ('U','S','E')\n                        : and is_disabled = 0\n                        : AND name NOT LIKE '%$'\n                        : ORDER BY name, type_desc'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27126901 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : SQL Server account logins match documenatation, and are confirmed to not be shared.\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : Field Requirement       : for at least one user_name, at least one of the following must be true:\n                        : Field Requirement       : user_name must be equal (case insensitive) to  the value(s) in End user provided list of database user names documented and approved to authenticate to SQL Server and verified to not be shared accounts.\n                        : Field Requirement       :     user_name must be equal (case insensitive) to ''\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT name AS user_name, type_desc AS account_type, is_disabled\n                        : FROM sys.server_principals\n                        : WHERE type in ('U','S','E')\n                        : and is_disabled = 0\n                        : AND name NOT LIKE '%$'\n                        : ORDER BY name, type_desc'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : !![ user_name = 'sa' ]!!\n\nResult Analysis         : Collected Item did not meet the state requirement.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27126902 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If logins are links to computer accounts this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27126902 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Check to see if any logins are computer accounts\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      : for command, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     command must be equal to 'try{ ([ADSISearcher]\"(&amp;(ObjectCategory=Computer)(Name=))\").FindAll() | foreach-object{ write-host($_.Properties.adspath + \", OS:\" + $_.Properties.operatingsystem)}} catch{}'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'pattern' must be equal to '^(?!$|----|Path Properties).*'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27126902 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : System Full, Administrators ReadPermission and ChangePermissions \n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals 'try{ ([ADSISearcher]\"(&amp;(ObjectCategory=Computer)(Name=))\").FindAll() | foreach-object{ write-host($_.Properties.adspath + \", OS:\" + $_.Properties.operatingsystem)}} catch{}'\n                        : pattern equals '^(?!$|----|Path Properties).*'\n                        : exit_status equals ''\n","weight":"10.0","status":"open","rule_version":"SQLI-22-007800","group_tree":{"id":"V-271305","title":"SRG-APP-000148-DB-000103"},"false_positives":"","fix_text":"Remove all shared accounts and computer accounts.\n\nTo remove users, run the following command for each user:\n\nDROP USER [ IF EXISTS ] &lt;user_name&gt;;","ia_controls":""},{"rule_id_src":"SV-271306r1109119_rule","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","security_override_guidance":"","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"high","discussion":"OS/enterprise authentication and identification must be used (SRG-APP-000023-DB-000001). Native DBMS authentication may be used only when circumstances make it unavoidable and must be documented and authorizing official (AO)-approved.\n \nThe DOD standard for authentication is DOD-approved PKI certificates. Authentication based on User ID and Password may be used only when it is not possible to employ a PKI certificate and requires AO approval.\n \nIn such cases, the DOD standards for password complexity and lifetime must be implemented. DBMS products that can inherit the rules for these from the operating system or access control program (e.g., Microsoft Active Directory) must be configured to do so. For other DBMSs, the rules must be enforced using available configuration parameters or custom code.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000164-DB-000401","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","comments":null,"mitigations":"","uuid":"F2022D6C-6BF8-1014-AD4B-DBB50CC82F00","ccis":["CCI-004066"],"rule_id":"SV-271306r1109119","check_content":"Execute the following query to determine if Contained Databases are used: \n\nSELECT * FROM sys.databases WHERE containment = 1\n\nIf any records are returned, check the server documentation for a list of authorized contained database users. \n\nExecute the following query to ensure contained database users are not using SQL Authentication:\n\nEXEC sp_MSforeachdb 'USE [?]; SELECT DB_NAME() AS DatabaseName, *\nFROM sys.database_principals dp\ninner join sys.databases d on d.name = dp.name\nWHERE dp.authentication_type = 2\nand d.containment = 1'\n\nIf any records are returned, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271306","rule_title":"Contained databases must use Windows principals.","group_id_src":"V-271306","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271306","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :   true (If no contained databases are found, this is not a finding)\nTest                    :   not applicable (Ensure contained database users are not using SQL Authentication.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27130601 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If no contained databases are found, this is not a finding\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27130601 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather list of contained database names\nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name FROM sys.databases WHERE containment = 1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql does not exist\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27130602 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : not applicable\nTest Title              : Ensure contained database users are not using SQL Authentication.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27130602 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      : for database, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'select name, type, type_desc, authentication_type, authentication_type_desc\n                        : from sys.database_principals\n                        : where authentication_type =2'\n\n","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000164-DB-000401","id":"V-271306"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-008000","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Configure SQL Server contained databases to have users originating from Microsoft Entra (Azure Active Directory) principals. Remove any users not created from Microsoft Entra principals. \n\nReference Contained Databases: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/relational-databases/databases/contained-databases?","ia_controls":""},{"group_id_src":"V-271307","mitigation_control":"","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271307","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"group_id":"V-271307","check_content":"Check for use of SQL Authentication:\n\nSELECT CASE SERVERPROPERTY('IsIntegratedSecurityOnly')\nWHEN 1 THEN 'Windows Authentication' WHEN 0 THEN 'SQL Authentication' \nEND as [Authentication Mode]\n\nIf the returned value in the \"Authentication Mode\" column is \"Windows Authentication\", this is not a finding.  \n\nSQL Server should be configured to inherit password complexity and password lifetime rules from the operating system. Review the SQL Server Instance to ensure logons are created with respect to the complexity settings and password lifetime rules by running the following statement:\n\nSELECT\n[name],\nis_expiration_checked,\nis_policy_checked,*\nFROM\nsys.sql_logins\nWHERE\nis_disabled = 0\nAND name NOT IN ('##MS_PolicyTsqlExecutionLogin##','##MS_PolicyEventProcessingLogin##')\nAND sid &lt;&gt; 1\n \nIf any account does not have both \"is_expiration_checked\" and \"is_policy_checked\" equal to \"1\", this is a finding. ","rule_title":"If DBMS authentication using passwords is employed, SQL Server must enforce the DOD standards for password complexity and lifetime.","ia_controls":"","fix_text":"Ensure check of policy and expiration are enforced when SQL logins are created. \n\nUse the command below to set CHECK_EXPIRATION and CHECK_POLICY  for any login found to be noncompliant:\n\nALTER LOGIN [LoginnameHere] WITH CHECK_EXPIRATION=ON;\nALTER LOGIN [LoginNameHere] WITH CHECK_POLICY=ON;\n\nNew SQL authenticated logins must be created with CHECK_EXPIRATION and CHECK_POLICY set to ON.\n\nCREATE LOGIN [LoginNameHere]  WITH PASSWORD = 'ComplexPasswordHere', CHECK_EXPIRATION = ON, CHECK_POLICY = ON;","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (DBMS authentication is using local SQL passwords)\nTest                    :     true (If any account does not have both 'is_expiration_checked' and 'is_policy_checked' equal to '1', this is a finding.)\nTest                    :     true (Ensure the DISA Windows Password Policy is set on the SQL Server member server.)\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false (DBMS authentication using Windows Authentication)\nTest                    :     true (Ensure the DISA Windows Password Policy is set on the SQL Server member server.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27130701 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : DBMS authentication is using local SQL passwords\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27130701 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT CASE SERVERPROPERTY('IsIntegratedSecurityOnly')    \n                        : \t\tWHEN 1 THEN 'Windows Authentication'    \n                        : \t\tWHEN 0 THEN 'Windows and SQL Server Authentication'    \n                        : \t\tEND as [authentication_mode]'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27130701 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : If the returned value in the 'authentication_mode' column is 'SQL Server Authentication', verify DBMS password settings.\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all authentication_mode must be equal to 'Windows and SQL Server Authentication'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT CASE SERVERPROPERTY('IsIntegratedSecurityOnly')    \n                        : \t\tWHEN 1 THEN 'Windows Authentication'    \n                        : \t\tWHEN 0 THEN 'Windows and SQL Server Authentication'    \n                        : \t\tEND as [authentication_mode]'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : authentication_mode = 'Windows and SQL Server Authentication'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27130702 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If any account does not have both 'is_expiration_checked' and 'is_policy_checked' equal to '1', this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27130702 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT [name], is_expiration_checked, is_policy_checked\n                        : FROM sys.sql_logins where \n                        :     name not in ('sa', '##MS_PolicyTsqlExecutionLogin##', '##MS_PolicyEventProcessingLogin##', '##MS_SSISServerCleanupJobLogin##')\n                        : and name NOT LIKE '%##MS%'\n                        : AND principal_id !=1'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27130702 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : If any account does not have both 'is_expiration_checked' and 'is_policy_checked' equal to '1', this is a finding.\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all is_expiration_checked must be equal to '1'\n                        : all is_policy_checked must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql does not exist\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27130705 (passwordpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Ensure the DISA Windows Password Policy is set on the SQL Server member server.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : All item-state comparisons must be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27130703 (passwordpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : Retrieves a passwordpolicy_object.\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27130703 (passwordpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : All DISA STIG OS Password Policy Settings must be applied\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'max_passwd_age' must be less than or equal to '5184000'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'min_passwd_age' must be greater than or equal to '86400'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'min_passwd_len' must be greater than or equal to '14'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'password_hist_len' must be greater than or equal to '24'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'password_complexity' must be equal to '1'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'reversible_encryption' must be equal to '0'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'anonymous_name_lookup' must be equal to '0'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27130704 (passwordpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : All DISA STIG OS Password Policy Settings must be applied\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'max_passwd_age' must be greater than '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : max_passwd_age equals '5184000'\n                        : min_passwd_age equals '86400'\n                        : min_passwd_len equals '14'\n                        : password_hist_len equals '24'\n                        : password_complexity equals '1'\n                        : reversible_encryption equals '0'\n                        : anonymous_name_lookup equals '0'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27130704 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : DBMS authentication using Windows Authentication\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27130701 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT CASE SERVERPROPERTY('IsIntegratedSecurityOnly')    \n                        : \t\tWHEN 1 THEN 'Windows Authentication'    \n                        : \t\tWHEN 0 THEN 'Windows and SQL Server Authentication'    \n                        : \t\tEND as [authentication_mode]'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27130705 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : If the returned value in the 'authentication_mode' column is 'Windows Authentication', this is not a finding.\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all authentication_mode must be equal to 'Windows Authentication'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT CASE SERVERPROPERTY('IsIntegratedSecurityOnly')    \n                        : \t\tWHEN 1 THEN 'Windows Authentication'    \n                        : \t\tWHEN 0 THEN 'Windows and SQL Server Authentication'    \n                        : \t\tEND as [authentication_mode]'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : authentication_mode = 'Windows and SQL Server Authentication'\n\n","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000164-DB-000401","id":"V-271307"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-007900","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","severity":"high","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","group_title":"SRG-APP-000164-DB-000401","discussion":"Windows Authentication is the default authentication mode and is much more secure than SQL Server Authentication. Windows Authentication uses Kerberos security protocol, provides password policy enforcement regarding complexity validation for strong passwords, provides support for account lockout, and supports password expiration. A connection made using Windows Authentication is sometimes called a trusted connection, because SQL Server trusts the credentials provided by Windows.\n\nBy using Windows Authentication, Windows groups can be created at the domain level, and a login can be created on SQL Server for the entire group. Managing access at the domain level can simplify account administration.\n\nOS/enterprise authentication and identification must be used (SRG-APP-000023-DB-000001). Native SQL Server authentication may be used only when circumstances make it unavoidable and must be documented and authorizing official (AO)-approved. \n \nThe DOD standard for authentication is DOD-approved PKI certificates. Authentication based on User ID and Password may be used only when it is not possible to employ a PKI certificate and requires AO approval. \n \nIn such cases, the DOD standards for password complexity and lifetime must be implemented. DBMS products that can inherit the rules for these from the operating system or access control program (e.g., Microsoft Active Directory) must be configured to do so. For other DBMSs, the rules must be enforced using available configuration parameters or custom code.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-APP-000164-DB-000401, SRG-APP-000700-DB-000100","rule_id_src":"SV-271307r1109241_rule","security_override_guidance":"","third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-004066","CCI-003627"],"rule_id":"SV-271307r1109241","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"uuid":"F20256AF-6BF8-1014-8136-939C5F08EB26","mitigations":"","comments":null},{"rule_id":"SV-271309r1109243","ccis":["CCI-000197"],"uuid":"F202710C-6BF8-1014-8ECB-ABF9576A53BD","mitigations":"","comments":null,"documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"group_title":"SRG-APP-000172-DB-000075","discussion":"The DOD standard for authentication is DOD-approved PKI certificates.\n\nAuthentication based on User ID and Password may be used only when it is not possible to employ a PKI certificate, and requires authorizing official (AO) approval.\n\nIn such cases, passwords need to be protected at all times, and encryption is the standard method for protecting passwords during transmission.\n\nDBMS passwords sent in clear text format across the network are vulnerable to discovery by unauthorized users. Disclosure of passwords may easily lead to unauthorized access to the database.","severity":"high","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","security_override_guidance":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271309r1109243_rule","ia_controls":"","fix_text":"Configure SQL Server to encrypt authentication data for remote connections using DOD-approved cryptography.\n\nDeploy encryption to the SQL Server Network Connections.\n\nFrom the search bar, open SQL Server Configuration Manager by typing \"SQL Server 2022 Configuration Manager\" and pressing \"ENTER\".\n\nNavigate to SQL Server Configuration Manager &gt;&gt; SQL Server Network Configuration. Right-click on \"Protocols for\", where there is a placeholder for the SQL Server instance name, and click on \"Properties\".\n\nIn the \"Protocols for Properties\" dialog box, on the \"Certificate\" tab, select the DOD certificate from the drop down for the Certificate box, and then click \"OK\". On the \"Flags\" tab, in the \"ForceEncryption\" box, select \"Yes\", and then click \"OK\" to close the dialog box. Then restart the SQL Server service.\n\nFor clustered instances install the certificate after setting \"Force Encryption\" to \"Yes\" in SQL Server Configuration Manager.\n\n1. Navigate to the certificate store where the FQDN certificate is stored, by typing \"Manage computer certificates\" in the search bar and pressing \"ENTER\".\n2. On the \"Properties\" page for the certificate, go to the \"Details\" tab and copy the \"thumbprint\" value of the certificate to a \"Notepad\" window.\n3. Remove the spaces between the hex characters in the \"thumbprint\" value in Notepad.\n4. Start regedit, navigate to the following registry key, and copy the value from step 2: HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\&lt;instance&gt;\\MSSQLServer\\SuperSocketNetLib\\Certificate.\n5. If the SQL virtual server is currently on this node, failover to another node in the cluster, and then reboot the node where the registry change occurred.\n6. Repeat this procedure on all the nodes. Configure SQL Server to encrypt authentication data for remote connections using DOD-approved cryptography.\n\nDeploy encryption to the SQL Server Network Connections.","false_positives":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-271309","title":"SRG-APP-000172-DB-000075"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-008200","status":"open","weight":"10.0","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       true (Check to see if SQL Instance is part of a cluster) (negated)\nTest                    :       false (Verify an DOD encryption cerificate is being used (Non-Clustered))\nResult Analysis         :            .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nCriteria                :     false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       false (Check to see if SQL Instance is part of a cluster)\nResult Analysis         :            is_clustered = '0' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \nTest                    :       false (Verify an DOD encryption cerificate is being used (Clustered))\nResult Analysis         :            .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false (Verify Force Encryption is set to Yes)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\\\MSSQLServer\\SuperSocketNetLib\\ForceEncryption'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nError Information       : Unable to retrieve any data with SQL transaction \"EXECUTE xp_regread @rootkey='HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE',\n                        :                    @key='SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\Instance Names\\SQl',\n                        :                    @value_name=@@servicename from DBMS instance \"SQLEXPRESS\" on server \"SOT-WIN2K22-SQL\" Error: [Microsoft][ODBC Driver 17 for SQL Server][SQL Server]xp_regread() returned error 5, 'Access is denied.' (SQL-42000)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27130904 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Check to see if SQL Instance is part of a cluster\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27130903 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT\n                        :     SERVERPROPERTY('isClustered') AS [is_clustered]'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27130902 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : Verify if is_clustered returns 1\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all is_clustered must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT\n                        :     SERVERPROPERTY('isClustered') AS [is_clustered]'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : !![ is_clustered = '0' ]!!\n\nResult Analysis         : is_clustered = '0' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27130903 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verify an DOD encryption cerificate is being used (Non-Clustered)\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27130904 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather certifates in 'Personal'.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'Microsoft.Powershell.Management'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'ChildItem'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : path must be equal to 'Cert:\\LocalMachine\\my'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : property must be equal to 'issuer,thumbprint'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27130903 (cmdlet_state)\nState Comment           : Cert issuer is DOD Root CA (if non-clustered)\nState Requirement       : for at least one 'value' the following must be true:\n                        : all issuer must match the pattern '^CN=DoD Root CA'\n                        : Field Requirement       : for at least one thumbprint, at least one of the following must be true:\n\nResult Analysis         : .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27130905 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verify an DOD encryption cerificate is being used (Clustered)\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27130904 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather certifates in 'Personal'.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'Microsoft.Powershell.Management'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'ChildItem'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : path must be equal to 'Cert:\\LocalMachine\\my'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : property must be equal to 'issuer,thumbprint'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27130904 (cmdlet_state)\nState Comment           : Cert issuer is DOD Root CA (if clustered)\nState Requirement       : for at least one 'value' the following must be true:\n                        : all issuer must match the pattern '^CN=DoD Root CA'\n                        : Field Requirement       : for at least one thumbprint, at least one of the following must be true:\n\nResult Analysis         : .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27130901 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verify Force Encryption is set to Yes\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27130901 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Value of Force Encryption\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      : for key, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     key must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\\\MSSQLServer\\SuperSocketNetLib'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'ForceEncryption'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27130901 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry key dword value equals 1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\\\MSSQLServer\\SuperSocketNetLib\\ForceEncryption'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nError Information       : Unable to retrieve any data with SQL transaction \"EXECUTE xp_regread @rootkey='HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE',\n                        :                    @key='SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\Instance Names\\SQl',\n                        :                    @value_name=@@servicename from DBMS instance \"SQLEXPRESS\" on server \"SOT-WIN2K22-SQL\" Error: [Microsoft][ODBC Driver 17 for SQL Server][SQL Server]xp_regread() returned error 5, 'Access is denied.' (SQL-42000)\n","mitigation_control":"","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271309","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"group_id_src":"V-271309","rule_title":"If passwords are used for authentication, SQL Server must transmit only encrypted representations of passwords.","group_id":"V-271309","check_content":"If SQL Server is using \"Windows Authentication mode\" this requirement can be marked as Not Applicable.\n\nOpen SQL Server Configuration Manager by typing \"SQL Server 2022 Configuration Manager\" in the search bar and pressing \"Enter\".\n\nNavigate to SQL Server Configuration Manager &gt;&gt; SQL Server Network Configuration. Right-click on \"Protocols\", where there is a placeholder for the SQL Server instance name and click on \"Properties\". \n\nOn the \"Flags\" tab, if \"Force Encryption\" is set to \"NO\", this is a finding.\n\nOn the \"Flags\" tab, if \"Force Encryption\" is set to \"YES\", examine the certificate used on the \"Certificate\" tab.\n\nIf it is not a DOD approved certificate, or if no certificate is listed, this is a finding.\n\nFor clustered instances, the Certificate will NOT be shown in the SQL Server Configuration Manager.\n\n1. From a command prompt, navigate to the certificate store where the Full Qualified Domain Name (FQDN) certificate is stored, by typing \"Manage computer certificates\" in the search bar and pressing \"Enter\".\n2. In the left side of the window, expand the \"Personal\" folder, and click \"Certificates\".\n3. Verify the Certificate with the FQDN name is issued by the DOD. Double-click the certificate, click the \"Details\" tab, and note the value for the Thumbprint.\n4. Ensure the value for the \"Thumbprint\" field matches the value in the registry by running regedit and looking at \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\&lt;instance&gt;\\MSSQLServer\\SuperSocketNetLib\\Certificate\".\n5. Run this on each node of the cluster.\n\nIf any nodes have a certificate in use by SQL that is not issued or approved by DOD, this is a finding."},{"rule_id":"SV-271310r1111062","ccis":["CCI-000197"],"uuid":"F2028D0D-6BF8-1014-B97D-F71F03657FDA","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","discussion":"Transport Layer Security (TLS) encryption is a required security setting as a number of known vulnerabilities have been reported against Secure Sockets Layer (SSL) and earlier versions of TLS. Encryption of private information is essential to ensuring data confidentiality. If private information is not encrypted, it can be intercepted and easily read by an unauthorized party. SQL Server must use a FIPS-approved minimum TLS version 1.2, and all non-FIPS-approved SSL and TLS versions must be disabled. NIST SP 800-52 Rev. 2 specifies the preferred configurations for government systems.\n\nReferences:\nTLS Support 1.2 for SQL Server: https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/kb/3135244 \nTLS Registry Settings:  https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/security/tls/tls-registry-settings","group_title":"SRG-APP-000175-DB-000067","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"high","third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271310r1111062_rule","fix_text":"Important Note: Incorrectly modifying the Windows Registry can result in serious system errors. Before making any modifications, ensure there is a recent backup of the system and registry settings.\n\nAccess the SQL Server.\nAccess an administrator command prompt. \nType \"regedit\" to launch the Registry Editor.\n \nEnable TLS 1.2:\n  \n1. Navigate to the path HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols.\n    a. If the \"TLS 1.2\" key does not exist, right-click \"Protocols\".\n    b. Click \"New\".\n    c. Click \"Key\".\n    d. Type the name \"TLS 1.2\".\n\n2. Navigate to the \"TLS 1.2\" subkey.\n    a. If the subkey \"Client\" does not exist, right-click \"TLS 1.2\".\n    b. Click \"New\".\n    c. Click \"Key\".\n    d. Type the name \"Client\".\n    e. Repeat steps A-D for the \"Server\" subkey.\n\n3. Navigate to the \"Client\" subkey.\n    a. If the value \"Enabled\" does not exist, right-click on \"Client\".\n    b. Click \"New\".\n    c. Click \"DWORD\".\n    d. Enter \"Enabled\" as the name.\n    e. Repeat steps A-D for the value \"DisabledByDefault\".\n\n4. Double-click \"Enabled\".\n\n5. In Value Data, enter \"1\".\n\n6. Click \"OK\".\n\n7. Double-click \"DisabledByDefault\".\n\n8. In Value Data, enter \"0\".\n\n9. Click \"OK\".\n\n10. Repeat steps 3-9 for the \"Server\" subkey.\n \nDisable unwanted SSL/TLS protocol versions:\n\n1. Navigate to the path HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols.\n    a. If the \"TLS 1.0\" key does not exist, right-click \"Protocols\".\n    b. Click \"New\".\n    c. Click \"Key\".\n    d. Type the name \"TLS 1.0\".\n\n2. Navigate to the \"TLS 1.0\" subkey.\n    a. If the subkey \"Client\" does not exist, right-click \"TLS 1.0\".\n    b. Click \"New\".\n    c. Click \"Key\".\n    d. Type the name \"Client\".\n    e. Repeat steps A-D for the \"Server\" subkey.\n\n3. Navigate to the \"Client\" subkey.\n   a. If the value \"Enabled\" does not exist, right-click on \"Client\".\n   b. Click \"New\".\n   c. Click \"DWORD\".\n   d. Enter \"Enabled\" as the name.\n   e. Repeat steps A-D for the value \"DisabledByDefault\".\n\n4. Double-click \"Enabled\".\n\n5. In Value Data, enter \"0\".\n\n6. Click \"OK\".\n\n7. Double-click \"DisabledByDefault\".\n\n8. In Value Data, enter \"1\".\n\n9. Click \"OK\".\n\n10. Repeat steps 3-9 for the \"Server\" subkey.\n\n11. Repeat steps 1-10 for \"TLS 1.1\", \"SSL 2.0\", and \"SSL 3.0\".","false_positives":"","ia_controls":"","weight":"10.0","status":"open","group_tree":{"id":"V-271310","title":"SRG-APP-000175-DB-000067"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-008300","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false (TLS 1.2 Enabled = 1 for Client)\nResult Analysis         :          Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.2\\Client\\Enabled'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :     false (TLS 1.2 DisabledByDefault = 0 for Client)\nResult Analysis         :          Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.2\\Client\\DisabledByDefault'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :     false (TLS 1.2 Enabled = 1 for Server)\nResult Analysis         :          Regis