d items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27131015 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : SSL 2.0 Server Enabled\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 2.0\\Server'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Enabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27131002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry key dword value equals 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 2.0\\Server\\Enabled'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27131016 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : SSL 2.0 DisabledByDefault = 1 for Server\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27131016 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : SSL 2.0 Server DisabledByDefault\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 2.0\\Server'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisabledByDefault'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27131001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry key dword value equals 1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 2.0\\Server\\DisabledByDefault'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27131017 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : SSL 3.0 Enabled = 0 for Client\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27131017 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : SSL 3.0 Client Enabled\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Client'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Enabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27131002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry key dword value equals 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Client\\Enabled'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27131018 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : SSL 3.0 Enabled = 0 for Server\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27131018 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : SSL 3.0 Server Enabled\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Server'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Enabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27131002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry key dword value equals 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Server\\Enabled'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27131019 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : SSL 3.0 DisabledByDefault = 1 for Client\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27131019 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : SSL 3.0 Client DisabledByDefault\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Client'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisabledByDefault'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27131001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry key dword value equals 1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Client\\DisabledByDefault'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27131020 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : SSL 3.0 DisabledByDefault = 1 for Server\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27131020 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : SSL 3.0 Server DisabledByDefault\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Server'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisabledByDefault'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27131001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry key dword value equals 1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\\Server\\DisabledByDefault'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271310","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-271310","rule_title":"Confidentiality of information during transmission must be controlled through the use of an approved TLS version.","check_content":"Access the SQL Server.\nAccess an administrator command prompt.\nType \"regedit\" to launch the Registry Editor.\n \nNavigate to:\nHKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.2\n\nIf this key does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nVerify a REG_DWORD value of \"0\" for \"DisabledByDefault\" and a value of \"1\" for \"Enabled\" for both Client and Server.\n \nNavigate to:\nHKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.0\nHKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\TLS 1.1\nHKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 2.0\nHKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\SCHANNEL\\Protocols\\SSL 3.0\n\nUnder each key, verify a REG_DWORD value of \"1\" for \"DisabledByDefault\" and a value of \"0\" for \"Enabled\" for both Client and Server subkeys.\n \nIf any of the respective registry paths are non-existent or contain values other than specified above, this is a finding. If Vendor documentation supporting the configuration is provided, reduce this finding to a CAT III.","group_id":"V-271310"},{"legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","uuid":"F202BB60-6BF8-1014-B0C5-9CAA0D6BDCB2","comments":null,"mitigations":"","ccis":["CCI-000206"],"rule_id":"SV-271313r1111146","rule_id_src":"SV-271313r1111146_rule","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","security_override_guidance":"","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"high","discussion":"To prevent the compromise of authentication information, such as passwords and PINs, during the authentication process, the feedback from the information system must not provide any information that would allow an unauthorized user to compromise the authentication mechanism.\n\nObfuscation of user-provided information when typed into the system is a method used in addressing this risk.\n\nFor example, displaying asterisks when a user types in a password or PIN is an example of obscuring feedback of authentication information.\n\nThis requirement is applicable when mixed-mode authentication is enabled. When this is the case, password-authenticated accounts can be created in and authenticated by SQL Server. Other STIG requirements prohibit the use of mixed-mode authentication except when justified and approved. This deals with the exceptions.\n\nSQLCMD and other command-line tools are part of any SQL Server installation. These tools can accept a plain text password but do offer alternative techniques. Since the typical user of these tools is a database administrator, the consequences of password compromise are particularly serious. Therefore, the use of plain-text passwords must be prohibited, as a matter of practice and procedure.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000178-DB-000083","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: errorRule Result             : Error\nCriteria                : error (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   error (If the config_value returned is 'Windows NT Authentication', this is not a finding.)\nError Information       : Unable to retrieve any data with SQL transaction \"EXEC master.sys.xp_loginconfig 'login mode'; from DBMS instance \"SQLEXPRESS\" on server \"SOT-WIN2K22-SQL\" Error: [Microsoft][ODBC Driver 17 for SQL Server][SQL Server]The EXECUTE permission was denied on the object 'xp_loginconfig', database 'mssqlsystemresource', schema 'sys'. (SQL-42000)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27131301 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : error\nTest Title              : If the config_value returned is 'Windows NT Authentication', this is not a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27131301 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'EXEC master.sys.xp_loginconfig 'login mode';'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27131301 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : SQL query result field 'name' = 'login mode' and config_value = 'Windows NT Authentication'\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all name must be equal (case insensitive) to 'login mode'\n                        : all config_value must be equal to 'Windows NT Authentication'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : error\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'EXEC master.sys.xp_loginconfig 'login mode';'\n\nError Information       : Unable to retrieve any data with SQL transaction \"EXEC master.sys.xp_loginconfig 'login mode'; from DBMS instance \"SQLEXPRESS\" on server \"SOT-WIN2K22-SQL\" Error: [Microsoft][ODBC Driver 17 for SQL Server][SQL Server]The EXECUTE permission was denied on the object 'xp_loginconfig', database 'mssqlsystemresource', schema 'sys'. (SQL-42000)\n","status":"open","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"SQLI-22-018100","group_tree":{"id":"V-271313","title":"SRG-APP-000178-DB-000083"},"fix_text":"Where possible, change the login mode to Windows-only:\nUSE [master]\nGO\nEXEC xp_instance_regwrite N'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE', N'Software\\Microsoft\\MSSQLServer\\MSSQLServer', N'LoginMode', REG_DWORD, 1;\nGO\n\nIf mixed-mode authentication is necessary, then for SQLCMD, which cannot be configured not to accept a plain-text password when mixed-mode authentication is enabled, and any other essential tool with the same limitation:\n1. Document the need for it, who uses it, and any relevant mitigations, and obtain AO approval.\n2. Train all users of the tool in the importance of not using the plain-text password option and in how to keep the password hidden.","false_positives":"","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Run this query to determine whether SQL Server authentication is enabled:\nEXEC master.sys.xp_loginconfig 'login mode'; \n\nIf the config_value returned is \"Windows NT Authentication\", this is not a finding.\n\nFor SQLCMD, which cannot be configured not to accept a plain-text password, and any other essential tool with the same limitation, verify that the system documentation explains the need for the tool, who uses it, and any relevant mitigations; and that authorizing approval (AO) approval has been obtained; if not, this is a finding.\n\nRequest evidence that all users of the tool are trained on the importance of not using the plain-text password option, how to keep the password hidden, and that they adhere to this practice; if not, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271313","rule_title":"When using command-line tools such as SQLCMD in a mixed-mode authentication environment, users must use a logon method that does not expose the password.","group_id_src":"V-271313","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271313"},"mitigation_control":""},{"rule_title":"SQL Server must use NIST FIPS 140-2 or 140-3 validated cryptographic operations for encryption, hashing, and signing.","check_content":"Verify that Windows is configured to require the use of FIPS compliant algorithms. \n \n1. Click \"Start\".\n2. Type \"Local Security Policy\".\n3. Press \"Enter\".\n4. Expand \"Local Policies\".\n5. Select \"Security Options\".\n6. Review the Security Setting for \"System Cryptography:  Use FIPS compliant algorithms for encryption, hashing, and signing\". \n \nIf the Security Setting for this option is \"Disabled\", this is a finding.\n\nAlternatively, run the following code in PowerShell:\n\nGet-ItemProperty -Path HKLM:\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\FipsAlgorithmPolicy | Select Enabled\n\nIf the returned value is \"0\", this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271314","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271314","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-271314","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000179-DB-000114","id":"V-271314"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-008700","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Check if 'FIPS compliant algorithms for encryption, hashing, and signing' is disabled.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27131401 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Check if 'FIPS compliant algorithms for encryption, hashing, and signing' is disabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27131401 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Determine via the registry that FIPS is enabled in the Local security policy\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\FipsAlgorithmPolicy'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Enabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27131401 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry key dword value equals 1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\FipsAlgorithmPolicy'\n                        : name equals 'Enabled'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055496560000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","fix_text":"Configure Windows to require the use of FIPS compliant algorithms for the unclassified information that requires it. \n \n1. Click \"Start\".\n2. Type \"Local Security Policy\".\n3. Press \"Enter\". \n4. Expand \"Local Policies\". \n5. Select \"Security Options\".\n6. Locate \"System Cryptography:  Use FIPS compliant algorithms for encryption, hashing, and signing\". \n7. Change the Setting option to \"Enabled\". \n8. Restart Windows.","false_positives":"","ia_controls":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271314r1109121_rule","discussion":"Use of weak or not validated cryptographic algorithms undermines the purposes of using encryption and digital signatures to protect data. Weak algorithms can be easily broken, and not validated cryptographic modules may not implement algorithms correctly. Unapproved cryptographic modules or algorithms should not be relied on for authentication, confidentiality, or integrity. Weak cryptography could allow an attacker to gain access to, and modify data stored in, the database as well as the administration settings of SQL Server. \n \nApplications, including DBMSs, using cryptography are required to use approved NIST FIPS 140-2 or 140-3 validated cryptographic modules that meet the requirements of applicable federal laws, Executive Orders, directives, policies, regulations, standards, and guidance.  \n \nNSA Type- (where =1, 2, 3, 4) products are NSA-certified, hardware-based encryption modules.\n\nThe standard for validating cryptographic modules will transition to the NIST FIPS 140-3 publication.\n\nFIPS 140-2 modules can remain active for up to five years after validation or until September 21, 2026, when the FIPS 140-2 validations will be moved to the historical list. Even on the historical list, CMVP supports the purchase and use of these modules for existing systems. While Federal Agencies decide when they move to FIPS 140-3 only modules, purchasers are reminded that for several years there may be a limited selection of FIPS 140-3 modules from which to choose. CMVP recommends purchasers consider all modules that appear on the Validated Modules Search Page:\nhttps://csrc.nist.gov/projects/cryptographic-module-validation-program/validated-modules\n\nMore information on the FIPS 140-3 transition can be found here: \nhttps://csrc.nist.gov/Projects/fips-140-3-transition-effort/.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-APP-000179-DB-000114, SRG-APP-000176-DB-000068, SRG-APP-000224-DB-000384, SRG-APP-000514-DB-000381, SRG-APP-000514-DB-000382, SRG-APP-000514-DB-000383","group_title":"SRG-APP-000179-DB-000114","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","severity":"high","uuid":"F202C958-6BF8-1014-8FC3-F4648AB1F26D","comments":null,"mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","rule_id":"SV-271314r1109121","ccis":["CCI-000803","CCI-000186","CCI-001188","CCI-002450"]},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT I, V-271322, SV-271322r1108582, SRG-APP-000231-DB-000154)\n","status":"not_reviewed","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"SQLI-22-009700","group_tree":{"id":"V-271322","title":"SRG-APP-000231-DB-000154"},"fix_text":"Document and implement procedures to safely back up and store the Master Key in a secure location that is not on the SQL Server. Include in the procedures methods to establish evidence of backup and storage, and careful, restricted access and restoration of the Master Key.\n\nBACKUP MASTER KEY TO FILE = 'path_to_file'  \nENCRYPTION BY PASSWORD = 'password';  \n \nAs this requires a password, take care to ensure it is not exposed to unauthorized persons or stored as plain text.","false_positives":"","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the application owner and authorizing official have determined that encryption of data at rest is not required, this is not a finding. \n \nReview procedures for and evidence of backup of the Master Key in the System Security Plan. \n \nIf the procedures or evidence does not exist, this is a finding. \n \nIf the procedures do not indicate that a backup of the Master Key is stored in a secure location that is not on the SQL Server, this is a finding.\n\nIf procedures do not indicate access restrictions to the Master Key backup, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271322","rule_title":"The Master Key must be backed up and stored in a secure location that is not on the SQL Server.","group_id_src":"V-271322","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:7901"},"mitigation_control":"","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","uuid":"F202D388-6BF8-1014-A379-9E6A89CABDA4","mitigations":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001199"],"rule_id":"SV-271322r1108582","rule_id_src":"SV-271322r1108582_rule","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","severity":"high","discussion":"Backup and recovery of the Master Key may be critical to the complete recovery of the database. Not having this key can lead to loss of data during recovery.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000231-DB-000154"},{"rule_id":"SV-271323r1108585","ccis":["CCI-001199"],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","uuid":"F202DC9C-6BF8-1014-98BD-E7B1294C3257","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"group_title":"SRG-APP-000231-DB-000154","discussion":"Backup and recovery of the Service Master Key may be critical to the complete recovery of the database. Creating this backup should be one of the first administrative actions performed on the server. Not having this key can lead to loss of data during recovery.","severity":"high","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","security_override_guidance":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271323r1108585_rule","ia_controls":"","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Document and implement procedures to safely back up and store the Service Master Key in a secure location that is not on the SQL Server. In the procedures, include methods to establish evidence of backup and storage, and careful, restricted access and restoration of the Service Master Key.\n \nBACKUP SERVICE MASTER KEY TO FILE = 'path_to_file'  \nENCRYPTION BY PASSWORD = 'password';  \n \nAs this requires a password, take care to ensure it is not exposed to unauthorized persons or stored as plain text.","rule_version":"SQLI-22-009600","group_tree":{"id":"V-271323","title":"SRG-APP-000231-DB-000154"},"weight":"10.0","status":"not_reviewed","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT I, V-271323, SV-271323r1108585, SRG-APP-000231-DB-000154)\n","mitigation_control":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:8101","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-271323","rule_title":"The Service Master Key must be backed up and stored in a secure location that is not on the SQL Server.","group_id":"V-271323","check_content":"Review procedures for and evidence of backup of the Server Service Master Key in the System Security Plan. \n \nIf the procedures or evidence does not exist, this is a finding.\n \nIf the procedures do not indicate that a backup of the Service Master Key is stored in a secure location that is not on the SQL Server, this is a finding. \n\nIf procedures do not indicate access restrictions to the Service Master Key backup, this is a finding."},{"false_positives":"","fix_text":"Apply appropriate controls to protect the confidentiality and integrity of data on a secondary device.Â Where encryption is required, this can be done by full-disk encryption or by database encryption. \n\nTo enable database encryption, create a master key, create a database encryption key, protect it by using mechanisms tied to the master key, and then turn encryption on.\n\nImplement physical security measures, operating system access control lists, and organizational controls appropriate to the sensitivity level of the data in the database(s).","ia_controls":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: errorRule Result             : Error\nCriteria                : error (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :   false (BitLocker must be enabled on all fixed drives.)\nResult Analysis         :        .  Existence requirement is 'all_exist' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   error (If the database 'encryption_state' returns 'Encrypted', this is not a finding.)\nTest                    :   error (If the database 'encryption_state' matches end user provided documentation', this is not a finding.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27132401 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : BitLocker must be enabled on all fixed drives.\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27132401 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : BitLocker status\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2\\security\\microsoftvolumeencryption'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT protectionstatus FROM win32_encryptablevolume'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27132401 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : BitLocker status is Protected\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all protectionstatus must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : .  Existence requirement is 'all_exist' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27132402 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : error\nTest Title              : If the database 'encryption_state' returns 'Encrypted', this is not a finding.\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27132402 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to '\n                        : SELECT\n                        : db.name AS [database_name], db.is_encrypted, CASE encryption_state \n                        : WHEN 0 THEN CONCAT(db.name,':','NoDatabaseEncryptionKey' ) \n                        : WHEN 1 THEN CONCAT(db.name,':','Unencrypted')\n                        : WHEN 2 THEN 'Encryption in progress'  \n                        : WHEN 3 THEN CONCAT(db.name,':','Encrypted' )\n                        : WHEN 4 THEN 'Key change in progress'  \n                        : WHEN 5 THEN 'Decryption in progress'  \n                        : WHEN 6 THEN 'Protection change in progress' \n                        : ELSE CONCAT(db.name,':','NoDatabaseEncryptionKey' ) \n                        : END AS [encryption_state]  \n                        : \n                        : FROM sys.dm_database_encryption_keys e  \n                        : RIGHT JOIN sys.databases db ON DB_NAME(e.database_id) = db.name  \n                        : WHERE db.database_id &gt; 4\n                        : ORDER BY [database_name] ;    \n                        : \t\t '\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27132402 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : 'encryption_state' must be equal to 'Encrypted'\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all encryption_state must match the pattern '.*\\:Encrypted'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : error\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals '\n                        : SELECT\n                        : db.name AS [database_name], db.is_encrypted, CASE encryption_state \n                        : WHEN 0 THEN CONCAT(db.name,':','NoDatabaseEncryptionKey' ) \n                        : WHEN 1 THEN CONCAT(db.name,':','Unencrypted')\n                        : WHEN 2 THEN 'Encryption in progress'  \n                        : WHEN 3 THEN CONCAT(db.name,':','Encrypted' )\n                        : WHEN 4 THEN 'Key change in progress'  \n                        : WHEN 5 THEN 'Decryption in progress'  \n                        : WHEN 6 THEN 'Protection change in progress' \n                        : ELSE CONCAT(db.name,':','NoDatabaseEncryptionKey' ) \n                        : END AS [encryption_state]  \n                        : \n                        : FROM sys.dm_database_encryption_keys e  \n                        : RIGHT JOIN sys.databases db ON DB_NAME(e.database_id) = db.name  \n                        : WHERE db.database_id &gt; 4\n                        : ORDER BY [database_name] ;    \n                        : \t\t '\n\nError Information       : Unable to retrieve any data with SQL transaction \"\n                        : SELECT\n                        : db.name AS [database_name], db.is_encrypted, CASE encryption_state \n                        : WHEN 0 THEN CONCAT(db.name,':','NoDatabaseEncryptionKey' ) \n                        : WHEN 1 THEN CONCAT(db.name,':','Unencrypted')\n                        : WHEN 2 THEN 'Encryption in progress'  \n                        : WHEN 3 THEN CONCAT(db.name,':','Encrypted' )\n                        : WHEN 4 THEN 'Key change in progress'  \n                        : WHEN 5 THEN 'Decryption in progress'  \n                        : WHEN 6 THEN 'Protection change in progress' \n                        : ELSE CONCAT(db.name,':','NoDatabaseEncryptionKey' ) \n                        : END AS [encryption_state]  \n                        : \n                        : FROM sys.dm_database_encryption_keys e  \n                        : RIGHT JOIN sys.databases db ON DB_NAME(e.database_id) = db.name  \n                        : WHERE db.database_id &gt; 4\n                        : ORDER BY [database_name] ;    \n                        : \t\t  from DBMS instance \"SQLEXPRESS\" on server \"SOT-WIN2K22-SQL\" Error: [Microsoft][ODBC Driver 17 for SQL Server][SQL Server]VIEW SERVER SECURITY STATE permission was denied on object 'server', database 'master'. (SQL-42000)\n                        : [Microsoft][ODBC Driver 17 for SQL Server][SQL Server]The user does not have permission to perform this action. (SQL-42000)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27132403 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : error\nTest Title              : If the database 'encryption_state' matches end user provided documentation', this is not a finding.\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27132402 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to '\n                        : SELECT\n                        : db.name AS [database_name], db.is_encrypted, CASE encryption_state \n                        : WHEN 0 THEN CONCAT(db.name,':','NoDatabaseEncryptionKey' ) \n                        : WHEN 1 THEN CONCAT(db.name,':','Unencrypted')\n                        : WHEN 2 THEN 'Encryption in progress'  \n                        : WHEN 3 THEN CONCAT(db.name,':','Encrypted' )\n                        : WHEN 4 THEN 'Key change in progress'  \n                        : WHEN 5 THEN 'Decryption in progress'  \n                        : WHEN 6 THEN 'Protection change in progress' \n                        : ELSE CONCAT(db.name,':','NoDatabaseEncryptionKey' ) \n                        : END AS [encryption_state]  \n                        : \n                        : FROM sys.dm_database_encryption_keys e  \n                        : RIGHT JOIN sys.databases db ON DB_NAME(e.database_id) = db.name  \n                        : WHERE db.database_id &gt; 4\n                        : ORDER BY [database_name] ;    \n                        : \t\t '\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27132403 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : 'encryption_state' must be equal to End User provided authorized/documented requirement for database level encryption\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : Field Requirement       : for at least one encryption_state, at least one of the following must be true:\n                        : Field Requirement       : encryption_state must be equal (case insensitive) to  the value(s) in End user provided information on authorized/documented database level encryption requirement\n                        : Field Requirement       :     encryption_state must be equal (case insensitive) to ''\n\nCollected Item/State Result : error\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals '\n                        : SELECT\n                        : db.name AS [database_name], db.is_encrypted, CASE encryption_state \n                        : WHEN 0 THEN CONCAT(db.name,':','NoDatabaseEncryptionKey' ) \n                        : WHEN 1 THEN CONCAT(db.name,':','Unencrypted')\n                        : WHEN 2 THEN 'Encryption in progress'  \n                        : WHEN 3 THEN CONCAT(db.name,':','Encrypted' )\n                        : WHEN 4 THEN 'Key change in progress'  \n                        : WHEN 5 THEN 'Decryption in progress'  \n                        : WHEN 6 THEN 'Protection change in progress' \n                        : ELSE CONCAT(db.name,':','NoDatabaseEncryptionKey' ) \n                        : END AS [encryption_state]  \n                        : \n                        : FROM sys.dm_database_encryption_keys e  \n                        : RIGHT JOIN sys.databases db ON DB_NAME(e.database_id) = db.name  \n                        : WHERE db.database_id &gt; 4\n                        : ORDER BY [database_name] ;    \n                        : \t\t '\n\n","weight":"10.0","status":"open","rule_version":"SQLI-22-009500","group_tree":{"id":"V-271324","title":"SRG-APP-000231-DB-000154"},"group_id_src":"V-271324","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271324","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":"","check_content":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:var:27132404;;Instance;;encryption_state;;Array","group_id":"V-271324","rule_title":"SQL Server must protect the confidentiality and integrity of all information at rest.","ccis":["CCI-001199"],"rule_id":"SV-271324r1192911","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","mitigations":"","comments":null,"uuid":"F202EB7C-6BF8-1014-A06E-CBC527C503F5","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"high","discussion":"This control is intended to address the confidentiality and integrity of information at rest in nonmobile devices and covers user information and system information. Information at rest refers to the state of information when it is located on a secondary storage device (e.g., disk drive, tape drive) within an organizational information system. Applications and application users generate information throughout the course of their application use. \n \nUser data generated, as well as application-specific configuration data, needs to be protected. Organizations may choose to employ different mechanisms to achieve confidentiality and integrity protections, as appropriate. \n \nIf the confidentiality and integrity of SQL Server data is not protected, the data will be open to compromise and unauthorized modification.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000231-DB-000154","rule_id_src":"SV-271324r1192911_rule","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","security_override_guidance":""},{"rule_id_src":"SV-271327r1137657_rule","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000243-DB-000373","discussion":"The purpose of this control is to prevent information, including encrypted representations of information, produced by the actions of a prior user/role (or the actions of a process acting on behalf of a prior user/role) from being available to any current user/role (or current process) that obtains access to a shared system resource (e.g., registers, main memory, secondary storage) after the resource has been released back to the information system. Control of information in shared resources is also referred to as object reuse.\n\nWhen IFI is in use, the deleted disk content is overwritten only as new data is written to the files. For this reason, the deleted content might be accessed by an unauthorized principal until some other data writes on that specific area of the data file.\n\nHistorically, transaction log files couldn't be initialized instantaneously. However, starting with SQL Server 2022 (16.x) (all editions), transaction log autogrowth events up to 64 MB can benefit from instant file initialization. The default auto growth size increment for new databases is 64 MB. Transaction log file autogrowth events larger than 64 MB can't benefit from instant file initialization.\n\nInstant file initialization is allowed for transaction log growth on databases that have transparent data encryption (TDE) enabled, due to the nature of how the transaction log file is expanded, and the fact that the transaction log is written into in a serial fashion.","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"uuid":"F202FA0F-6BF8-1014-A8D4-B8EFA17FE1F6","mitigations":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001090"],"rule_id":"SV-271327r1137657","group_id":"V-271327","check_content":"Review system configuration to determine whether IFI support has been enabled (IFI is enabled by default).\n\nRun the following query in SSMS:\n\nSELECT\n\tservicename\n\t,instant_file_initialization_enabled\nFROM sys.dm_server_services \n\nIf the column instant_file_initialization_enabled returns a value of \"Y\", then IFI is enabled.\n\nAlternatively, navigate to Start &gt;&gt; Control Panel &gt;&gt; System and Security &gt;&gt; Administrative Tools &gt;&gt; Local Security Policy &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Perform volume maintenance tasks.\n\nThe default SQL service account for a default instance is NT SERVICE\\MSSQLSERVER or for a named instance is NT SERVICE\\MSSQL$InstanceName.\n\nIf the SQL service account or SQL service SID has been granted \"Perform volume maintenance tasks\" Local Rights Assignment, this means that IFI is enabled.\n\nReview the system documentation to determine if IFI is required.\n\nIf IFI is enabled but not documented as required, this is a finding.\n\nIf IFI is not enabled, this is not a finding.","rule_title":"SQL Server must prevent unauthorized and unintended information transfer via Instant File Initialization (IFI).","group_id_src":"V-271327","mitigation_control":"","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:8501"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271327, SV-271327r1137657, SRG-APP-000243-DB-000373)\n","rule_version":"SQLI-22-009900","group_tree":{"id":"V-271327","title":"SRG-APP-000243-DB-000373"},"status":"not_reviewed","weight":"10.0","ia_controls":"","fix_text":"If IFI is not documented as being required, disable instant file initialization for the instance of SQL Server by removing the SQL Service SID and/or service account from the \"Perform volume maintenance tasks\" local rights assignment.\n\nTo grant an account the \"Perform volume maintenance tasks\" permission:\n\n1. On the computer where the data file will be created, open the Local Security Policy application (secpol.msc).\n2. In the left pane, expand \"Local Policies\" then select \"User Rights Assignment\".\n3. In the right pane, double-click \"Perform volume maintenance tasks\".\n4. Select \"Add User or Group\" and add the SQL Server service account.\n5. Select \"Apply\", then close all Local Security Policy dialog boxes.\n6. Restart the SQL Server service.\n7. Check the SQL Server error log at startup.","false_positives":""},{"check_content":"Review system documentation to determine whether common criteria compliance is required due to potential impact on system performance. \n\nSQL Server Residual Information Protection (RIP) requires a memory allocation to be overwritten with a known pattern of bits before memory is reallocated to a new resource. Meeting the RIP standard can contribute to improved security; however, overwriting the memory allocation can slow performance. After the common criteria compliance enabled option is enabled, the overwriting occurs. \n\nReview the Instance configuration: \n\nSELECT value_in_use\nFROM sys.configurations\nWHERE name = 'common criteria compliance enabled'\n\nIf \"value_in_use\" is set to \"1\" this is not a finding.\n\nIf \"value_in_use\" is set to \"0\" this is a finding. \n\nIf no results are returned, common criteria compliance is not available in the installed version of SQL Server, this is a finding. Common criteria compliance is only supported in Enterprise and Developer editions of SQL Server.\n\nNote: Enabling this feature may impact performance on highly active SQL Server instances. If an exception justifying setting SQL Server RIP to disabled (value_in_use set to \"0\") has been documented and approved, then this is downgraded to a CAT III finding.","group_id":"V-271328","rule_title":"SQL Server must prevent unauthorized and unintended information transfer via shared system resources.","group_id_src":"V-271328","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271328"},"mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Check if 'common criteria compliance enabled' returns 'value_in_use' = 1)\nResult Analysis         :        .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n                        :         .  \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27132801 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Check if 'common criteria compliance enabled' returns 'value_in_use' = 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27132801 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT value_in_use\n                        : FROM sys.configurations\n                        : WHERE name = 'common criteria compliance enabled''\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27132801 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : SQL query result field 'value_in_use' = 1\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all value_in_use must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : !![ sql does not exist ]!!\n\nResult Analysis         : .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nResult Analysis         :  .  \n","status":"open","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"SQLI-22-009800","group_tree":{"id":"V-271328","title":"SRG-APP-000243-DB-000373"},"fix_text":"Configure SQL Server to effectively protect the private resources of one process or user from unauthorized access by another process or user. \n\nTo enable the use of [Common Criteria Compliance], from the query prompt:  \n \nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'show advanced options', 1;  \nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE;\nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'common criteria compliance enabled', 1;\nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE;\nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'show advanced options', 0;  \nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE;","false_positives":"","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271328r1137657_rule","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","security_override_guidance":"","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","discussion":"The purpose of this control is to prevent information, including encrypted representations of information, produced by the actions of a prior user/role (or the actions of a process acting on behalf of a prior user/role) from being available to any current user/role (or current process) that obtains access to a shared system resource (e.g., registers, main memory, secondary storage) after the resource has been released back to the information system. Control of information in shared resources is also referred to as object reuse.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000243-DB-000373","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","uuid":"F20303E7-6BF8-1014-AF63-9B7016C1D603","mitigations":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001090"],"rule_id":"SV-271328r1137657"},{"false_positives":"","fix_text":"Remove any unauthorized permission grants from SQL Server data, log, and backup directories.\n\n1. On the \"Security\" tab, highlight the user entry.\n2. Click \"Remove\".","ia_controls":"","weight":"10.0","status":"not_reviewed","rule_version":"SQLI-22-010000","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000243-DB-000374","id":"V-271329"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271329, SV-271329r1137658, SRG-APP-000243-DB-000374)\n","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:8901","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-271329","rule_title":"Access to database files must be limited to relevant processes and to authorized, administrative users.","check_content":"Review the permissions granted to users by the operating system/file system on the database files, database log files, and database backup files. \n\nTo obtain the location of SQL Server data, transaction log, and backup files, open and execute the supplemental file \"Get SQL Data and Backup Directories.sql\".\n\nFor each of the directories returned by the above script, verify whether the correct permissions have been applied.\n\n1. Launch Windows Explorer.\n2. Navigate to the folder.\n3. Right-click the folder and click \"Properties\".\n4. Navigate to the \"Security\" tab.\n5. Review the listing of principals and permissions.\n\nAccount Type Directory Type Permission\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDatabase Administrators      ALL                   Full Control\nSQL Server Service SID       Data; Log; Backup;    Full Control\nSQL Server Agent Service SID Backup                Full Control\nSYSTEM                       ALL                   Full Control\nCREATOR OWNER                ALL                   Full Control\n\nFor information on how to determine a \"Service SID\", refer to https://aka.ms/sql-service-sids.\n\nAdditional permission requirements, including full directory permissions and operating system rights for SQL Server, are documented at https://aka.ms/sqlservicepermissions.\n\nIf any additional permissions are granted but not documented as authorized, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271329","rule_id":"SV-271329r1137658","ccis":["CCI-001090"],"mitigations":"","comments":null,"uuid":"F2030BFF-6BF8-1014-81DE-9221E0336478","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","discussion":"Applications, including SQL Server, must prevent unauthorized and unintended information transfer via shared system resources. Permitting only DBMS processes and authorized, administrative users to have access to the files where the database resides helps ensure that those files are not shared inappropriately and are not open to backdoor access and manipulation.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000243-DB-000374","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271329r1137658_rule"},{"rule_id":"SV-271331r1108609","ccis":["CCI-001310"],"uuid":"F2031500-6BF8-1014-87A6-F512FB9E2A8C","mitigations":"","comments":null,"documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"group_title":"SRG-APP-000251-DB-000391","discussion":"With respect to database management systems, one class of threat is known as SQL Injection, or more generally, code injection. It takes advantage of the dynamic execution capabilities of various programming languages, including dialects of SQL. In such cases, the attacker deduces the manner in which SQL statements are being processed, either from inside knowledge or by observing system behavior in response to invalid inputs. When the attacker identifies scenarios where SQL queries are being assembled by application code (which may be within the database or separate from it) and executed dynamically, the attacker is then able to craft input strings that subvert the intent of the query. Potentially, the attacker can gain unauthorized access to data, including security settings, and severely corrupt or destroy the database.\n\nThe principal protection against code injection is not to use dynamic execution except where it provides necessary functionality that cannot be used otherwise. Use strongly typed data items rather than general-purpose strings as input parameters to task-specific, precompiled stored procedures and functions (and triggers).\n\nThis calls for inspection of application source code, which will require collaboration with the application developers. It is recognized that in many cases, the database administrator (DBA) is organizationally separate from the application developers, and may have limited, if any, access to source code. Nevertheless, protections of this type are so important to the secure operation of databases that they must not be ignored. At a minimum, the DBA must attempt to obtain assurances from the development organization that this issue has been addressed and must document what has been discovered.","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","security_override_guidance":"","third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271331r1108609_rule","ia_controls":"","fix_text":"Where dynamic code execution is employed in circumstances where the objective could practically be satisfied by static execution with strongly typed parameters, modify the code to do so.","false_positives":"","rule_version":"SQLI-22-010010","group_tree":{"id":"V-271331","title":"SRG-APP-000251-DB-000391"},"weight":"10.0","status":"not_reviewed","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271331, SV-271331r1108609, SRG-APP-000251-DB-000391)\n","mitigation_control":"","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:9101"},"group_id_src":"V-271331","rule_title":"SQL Server and associated applications must reserve the use of dynamic code execution for situations that require it.","group_id":"V-271331","check_content":"Review DBMS source code (stored procedures, functions, triggers) and application source code, to identify cases of dynamic code execution.\n\nIf dynamic code execution is employed in circumstances where the objective could practically be satisfied by static execution with strongly typed parameters, this is a finding."},{"ccis":["CCI-001310"],"rule_id":"SV-271332r1108612","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"uuid":"F2031E92-6BF8-1014-AF98-D7F00BEBC8A9","comments":null,"mitigations":"","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000251-DB-000392","discussion":"With respect to database management systems, one class of threat is known as SQL Injection, or more generally, code injection. It takes advantage of the dynamic execution capabilities of various programming languages, including dialects of SQL. In such cases, the attacker deduces the manner in which SQL statements are being processed, either from inside knowledge or by observing system behavior in response to invalid inputs. When the attacker identifies scenarios where SQL queries are being assembled by application code (which may be within the database or separate from it) and executed dynamically, the attacker is then able to craft input strings that subvert the intent of the query. Potentially, the attacker can gain unauthorized access to data, including security settings, and severely corrupt or destroy the database.\n\nThe principal protection against code injection is not to use dynamic execution except where it provides necessary functionality that cannot be used otherwise. Use strongly typed data items rather than general-purpose strings as input parameters to task-specific, precompiled stored procedures and functions (and triggers).\n\nWhen dynamic execution is necessary, ways to mitigate the risk include the following, which should be implemented both in the on-screen application and at the database level, in the stored procedures:\n- Allow strings as input only when necessary. \n- Rely on data typing to validate numbers, dates, etc. Do not accept invalid values. If substituting other values for them, think carefully about whether this could be subverted.\n- Limit the size of input strings to what is truly necessary.\n- If single quotes/apostrophes, double quotes, semicolons, equals signs, angle brackets, or square brackets will never be valid as input, reject them.\n- If comment markers will never be valid as input, reject them. In SQL, these are -- or /* */ \n- If HTML and XML tags, entities, comments, etc., will never be valid, reject them.\n- If wildcards are present, reject them unless truly necessary. In SQL these are the underscore and the percentage sign, and the word ESCAPE is also a clue that wildcards are in use.\n- If SQL key words, such as SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, CREATE, ALTER, DROP, ESCAPE, UNION, GRANT, REVOKE, DENY, MODIFY will never be valid, reject them. Use case-insensitive comparisons when searching for these. Bear in mind that some of these words, particularly Grant (as a person's name), could also be valid input. \n- If there are range limits on the values that may be entered, enforce those limits.\n- Institute procedures for inspection of programs for correct use of dynamic coding, by a party other than the developer.\n- Conduct rigorous testing of program modules that use dynamic coding, searching for ways to subvert the intended use.\n- Record the inspection and testing in the system documentation.\n- Bear in mind that all this applies not only to screen input, but also to the values in an incoming message to a web service or to a stored procedure called by a software component that has not itself been hardened in these ways. Not only can the caller be subject to such vulnerabilities; it may itself be the attacker.\n\nThis calls for inspection of application source code, which will require collaboration with the application developers. It is recognized that in many cases, the database administrator (DBA) is organizationally separate from the application developers, and may have limited, if any, access to source code. Nevertheless, protections of this type are so important to the secure operation of databases that they must not be ignored. At a minimum, the DBA must attempt to obtain assurances from the development organization that this issue has been addressed and must document what has been discovered.","rule_id_src":"SV-271332r1108612_rule","security_override_guidance":"","third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","fix_text":"Where dynamic code execution is used, modify the code to implement protections against code injection.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271332, SV-271332r1108612, SRG-APP-000251-DB-000392)\n","group_tree":{"id":"V-271332","title":"SRG-APP-000251-DB-000392"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-010020","weight":"10.0","status":"not_reviewed","group_id_src":"V-271332","mitigation_control":"","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:9301"},"group_id":"V-271332","check_content":"Review DBMS source code (stored procedures, functions, triggers) and application source code to identify cases of dynamic code execution.\n\nIf dynamic code execution is employed without protective measures against code injection, this is a finding.","rule_title":"SQL Server and associated applications, when making use of dynamic code execution, must scan input data for invalid values that may indicate a code injection attack."},{"security_override_guidance":"","third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271334r1109125_rule","group_title":"SRG-APP-000267-DB-000163","discussion":"If SQL Server provides too much information in error logs and administrative messages to the screen, this could lead to compromise. The structure and content of error messages need to be carefully considered by the organization and development team. The extent to which the information system is able to identify and handle error conditions is guided by organizational policy and operational requirements. \n \nSome default DBMS error messages can contain information that could aid an attacker in, among other things, identifying the database type, host address, or state of the database. Custom errors may contain sensitive customer information. \n \nIt is important that detailed error messages be visible only to those who are authorized to view them; that general users receive only generalized acknowledgment that errors have occurred; and that these generalized messages appear only when relevant to the user's task. For example, a message along the lines of, \"An error has occurred. Unable to save your changes. If this problem persists, please contact your help desk.\" would be relevant. A message such as \"Warning: your transaction generated a large number of page splits\" would likely not be relevant. \"ABGQ is not a valid widget code.\" would be appropriate; but \"The INSERT statement conflicted with the FOREIGN KEY constraint \"WidgetTransactionFK\". The conflict occurred in database \"DB7\", table \"dbo.WidgetMaster\", column 'WidgetCode'\" would not, as it reveals too much about the database structure.","severity":"medium","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","uuid":"F20327B3-6BF8-1014-B915-BDA68D5AEAEF","comments":null,"mitigations":"","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"rule_id":"SV-271334r1109125","ccis":["CCI-001314"],"rule_title":"SQL Server must reveal detailed error messages only to documented and approved individuals or roles.","group_id":"V-271334","check_content":"Error messages within applications, custom database code (stored procedures, triggers) must be enforced by guidelines and code review practices.  \n\nSQL Server generates certain system events and user-defined events to the SQL Server error log. The SQL Server error log can be viewed using SQL Server Management Studio GUI. All users granted the security admin or sysadmin level of permission are able to view the logs. Review the users returned in the following script: \n\nUSE master \nGO\nSELECT Name \nFROM syslogins \nWHERE (sysadmin = 1 or securityadmin = 1) \nand hasaccess = 1; \n\nIf any nonauthorized users have access to the SQL Server Error Log located at Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\MSSQL.n\\MSSQL\\LOG, this is a finding. \n\nIn addition, the SQL Server Error Log is also located at Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\MSSQL.n\\MSSQL\\LOG\\. Review the permissions on this folder to ensure that only authorized users are listed.  \n\nIf any nonauthorized users have access to the SQL Server Error Log in SQL Server Management Studio or if documentation does not exist stating that full error messages must be returned, this is a finding.\n\nOtherwise, verify if trace flag 3625 is enabled to mask certain system-level error information returned to nonadministrative users. \n \nLaunch SQL Server Configuration Manager &gt;&gt; select SQL Server Services &gt;&gt; select the SQL Server &gt;&gt; right-click and select Properties &gt;&gt; select Startup Parameters tab &gt;&gt; verify -T3625 exists in the dialogue window.\n\nOR\n\nRun the query:\nDBCC TRACESTATUS;\n\nIf TraceFlag 3625 does not return with Status = 1, and if documentation does not exist stating that full error messages must be returned, this is a finding.","mitigation_control":"","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:9501"},"group_id_src":"V-271334","group_tree":{"id":"V-271334","title":"SRG-APP-000267-DB-000163"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-010100","status":"not_reviewed","weight":"10.0","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271334, SV-271334r1109125, SRG-APP-000267-DB-000163)\n","ia_controls":"","fix_text":"Configure audit logging, tracing, and/or custom code in the database or application to record detailed error messages generated by SQL Server for review by authorized personnel. \n \nIf any nonauthorized users have access to the SQL Server Error Log in SQL Server Management Studio, use the REVOKE or DENY commands to remove them from the security admin or sysadmin roles.\n \nIf any nonauthorized users have access to the SQL Server Error Log located at Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\MSSQL.n\\MSSQL\\LOG, remove their permissions. \n \nConsider enabling trace flag 3625 to mask certain system-level error information returned to nonadministrative users. \n\nConfigure audit logging, tracing and/or custom code in the database or application to record detailed error messages generated by SQL Server, for review by authorized personnel. \n \nIf any nonauthorized users have access to the SQL Server Error Log in SQL Server Management Studio, use the REVOKE or DENY commands to remove them from the security admin or sysadmin roles.  \n\nIf any nonauthorized users have access to the SQL Server Error Log located at Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\MSSQL.n\\MSSQL\\LOG, remove their permissions. \n \nEnable trace flag 3625 to mask certain system-level error information returned to nonadministrative users. \n \nTo launch SQL Server Configuration Manager, select SQL Server Services, select the SQL Server, then right-click and select \"Properties\". Select the \"Startup Parameters\" tab, enter \"-T3625\", and then click \"Add\". Click \"OK\", then restart SQL instance.","false_positives":""},{"false_positives":"","fix_text":"Restrict the granting of permissions to server-level securables to only those authorized, most notably: members of sysadmin and securityadmin built-in instance-level roles, CONTROL SERVER permission, and use of the GRANT with GRANT permission.","ia_controls":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271341, SV-271341r1111081, SRG-APP-000340-DB-000304)\n","weight":"10.0","status":"not_reviewed","rule_version":"SQLI-22-010400","group_tree":{"id":"V-271341","title":"SRG-APP-000340-DB-000304"},"group_id_src":"V-271341","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:9701"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":"","check_content":"Review server-level securables and built-in role membership to ensure only authorized users have privileged access and the ability to create server-level objects and grant permissions to themselves or others. \n \nReview the system documentation to determine the required levels of protection for DBMS server securables by type of login. \n \nReview the permissions in place on the server. If the actual permissions do not match the documented requirements, this is a finding. \n \nGet all permission assignments to logins and roles: \n \nSELECT DISTINCT \n    CASE \n        WHEN SP.class_desc IS NOT NULL THEN \n            CASE \n                WHEN SP.class_desc = 'SERVER' AND S.is_linked = 0 THEN 'SERVER' \n                WHEN SP.class_desc = 'SERVER' AND S.is_linked = 1 THEN 'SERVER (linked)' \n                ELSE SP.class_desc \n            END \n        WHEN E.name IS NOT NULL THEN 'ENDPOINT' \n        WHEN S.name IS NOT NULL AND S.is_linked = 0 THEN 'SERVER' \n        WHEN S.name IS NOT NULL AND S.is_linked = 1 THEN 'SERVER (linked)' \n        WHEN P.name IS NOT NULL THEN 'SERVER_PRINCIPAL' \n        ELSE '???' \n    END                    AS [Securable Class], \n    CASE \n        WHEN E.name IS NOT NULL THEN E.name \n        WHEN S.name IS NOT NULL THEN S.name \n        WHEN P.name IS NOT NULL THEN P.name \n        ELSE '???' \n    END                    AS [Securable], \n    P1.name                AS [Grantee], \n    P1.type_desc           AS [Grantee Type], \n    sp.permission_name     AS [Permission], \n    sp.state_desc          AS [State], \n    P2.name                AS [Grantor], \n    P2.type_desc           AS [Grantor Type] \nFROM \n    sys.server_permissions SP \n    INNER JOIN sys.server_principals P1 \n        ON P1.principal_id = SP.grantee_principal_id \n    INNER JOIN sys.server_principals P2 \n        ON P2.principal_id = SP.grantor_principal_id \n \n    FULL OUTER JOIN sys.servers S \n        ON  SP.class_desc = 'SERVER' \n        AND S.server_id = SP.major_id \n \n    FULL OUTER JOIN sys.endpoints E \n        ON  SP.class_desc = 'ENDPOINT' \n        AND E.endpoint_id = SP.major_id \n \n    FULL OUTER JOIN sys.server_principals P \n        ON  SP.class_desc = 'SERVER_PRINCIPAL'        \n        AND P.principal_id = SP.major_id \n \nGet all server role memberships: \n \nSELECT \n    R.name    AS [Role], \n    M.name    AS [Member] \nFROM \n    sys.server_role_members X \n    INNER JOIN sys.server_principals R ON R.principal_id = X.role_principal_id \n    INNER JOIN sys.server_principals M ON M.principal_id = X.member_principal_id \n \nThe CONTROL SERVER permission is similar but not identical to the sysadmin fixed server role. Permissions do not imply role memberships, and role memberships do not grant permissions (e.g., CONTROL SERVER does not imply membership in the sysadmin fixed server role). \n \nEnsure only the documented and approved logins have privileged functions in SQL Server. \n \nIf the current configuration does not match the documented baseline, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271341","rule_title":"SQL Server must prevent nonprivileged users from executing privileged functions, to include disabling, circumventing, or altering implemented security safeguards/countermeasures.","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"rule_id":"SV-271341r1111081","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","comments":null,"mitigations":"","uuid":"F2033143-6BF8-1014-9114-8E8BC45F94DC","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","severity":"medium","discussion":"Preventing nonprivileged users from executing privileged functions mitigates the risk that unauthorized individuals or processes may gain unnecessary access to information or privileges. \n \nSystem documentation should include a definition of the functionality considered privileged. \n \nDepending on circumstances, privileged functions can include, for example, establishing accounts, performing system integrity checks, or administering cryptographic key management activities. Nonprivileged users are individuals that do not possess appropriate authorizations. Circumventing intrusion detection and prevention mechanisms or malicious code protection mechanisms are examples of privileged functions that require protection from nonprivileged users. \n \nA privileged function in SQL Server/database context is any operation that modifies the structure of the database, its built-in logic, or its security settings. This would include all Data Definition Language (DDL) statements and all security-related statements. In an SQL environment, it encompasses, but is not necessarily limited to:  \nCREATE \nALTER \nDROP \nGRANT \nREVOKE \nDENY \n \nThere may also be Data Manipulation Language (DML) statements that, subject to context, should be regarded as privileged. Possible examples include: \nTRUNCATE TABLE; \nDELETE, or \nDELETE affecting more than n rows, for some n, or \nDELETE without a WHERE clause; \n \nUPDATE or \nUPDATE affecting more than n rows, for some n, or \nUPDATE without a WHERE clause; \n \nAny SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, or DELETE to an application-defined security table executed by other than a security principal. \n \nDepending on the capabilities of SQL Server and the design of the database and associated applications, the prevention of unauthorized use of privileged functions may be achieved by means of DBMS security features, database triggers, other mechanisms, or a combination of these.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000340-DB-000304","rule_id_src":"SV-271341r1111081_rule","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","security_override_guidance":""},{"potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271342"},"mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-271342","rule_title":"Use of credentials and proxies must be restricted to necessary cases only.","check_content":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:var:27134204;;Instance;;credential_identity;;Array","group_id":"V-271342","fix_text":"Remove any SQL Agent Proxy accounts and credentials that are not authorized. \n \nDROP CREDENTIAL &lt;Credential Name&gt; \nGO \n \nUSE [msdb] \nEXEC sp_delete_proxy @proxy_name = '&lt;Proxy Name&gt;' \nGO","false_positives":"","ia_controls":"","status":"open","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000342-DB-000302","id":"V-271342"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-010500","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: errorRule Result             : Error\nCriteria                : error (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Check if any sys.credentials are not authorized and documented.)\nTest                    :   error (Check if any proxy credentials are not authorized and documented.)\nError Information       : Unable to retrieve any data with SQL transaction \"SELECT P.name AS proxy_name, C.name AS user_name, C.credential_identity \n                        : FROM sys.credentials C  \n                        : JOIN msdb.dbo.sysproxies P ON C.credential_id = P.credential_id \n                        : WHERE P.enabled = 1 from DBMS instance \"SQLEXPRESS\" on server \"SOT-WIN2K22-SQL\" Error: [Microsoft][ODBC Driver 17 for SQL Server][SQL Server]The SELECT permission was denied on the object 'sysproxies', database 'msdb', schema 'dbo'. (SQL-42000)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27134201 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Check if any sys.credentials are not authorized and documented.\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27134201 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT C.name AS credential_name, C.credential_identity as credential_identity \n                        : FROM sys.credentials C'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27134201 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : If unauthorized credentials are listed, this is a finding.\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : Field Requirement       : for at least one credential_identity, at least one of the following must be true:\n                        : Field Requirement       : credential_identity must be equal (case insensitive) to  the value(s) in End user provided list of documented and approved database user names allowed to execute external processes\n                        : Field Requirement       :     credential_identity must be equal (case insensitive) to ''\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql does not exist\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27134202 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : error\nTest Title              : Check if any proxy credentials are not authorized and documented.\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27134202 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT P.name AS proxy_name, C.name AS user_name, C.credential_identity \n                        : FROM sys.credentials C  \n                        : JOIN msdb.dbo.sysproxies P ON C.credential_id = P.credential_id \n                        : WHERE P.enabled = 1'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27134202 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : If unauthorized proxy credentials are listed, this is a finding.\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : Field Requirement       : for at least one credential_identity, at least one of the following must be true:\n                        : Field Requirement       : credential_identity must be equal (case insensitive) to  the value(s) in End user provided list of documented and approved database user names allowed to execute external processes\n                        : Field Requirement       :     credential_identity must be equal (case insensitive) to ''\n\nCollected Item/State Result : error\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT P.name AS proxy_name, C.name AS user_name, C.credential_identity \n                        : FROM sys.credentials C  \n                        : JOIN msdb.dbo.sysproxies P ON C.credential_id = P.credential_id \n                        : WHERE P.enabled = 1'\n\nError Information       : Unable to retrieve any data with SQL transaction \"SELECT P.name AS proxy_name, C.name AS user_name, C.credential_identity \n                        : FROM sys.credentials C  \n                        : JOIN msdb.dbo.sysproxies P ON C.credential_id = P.credential_id \n                        : WHERE P.enabled = 1 from DBMS instance \"SQLEXPRESS\" on server \"SOT-WIN2K22-SQL\" Error: [Microsoft][ODBC Driver 17 for SQL Server][SQL Server]The SELECT permission was denied on the object 'sysproxies', database 'msdb', schema 'dbo'. (SQL-42000)\n","discussion":"In certain situations, to provide required functionality, a DBMS needs to execute internal logic (stored procedures, functions, triggers, etc.) and/or external code modules with elevated privileges. However, if the privileges required for execution are at a higher level than the privileges assigned to organizational users invoking the functionality applications/programs, those users are indirectly provided with greater privileges than assigned by organizations. \n \nPrivilege elevation must be used only where necessary and protected from misuse.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000342-DB-000302","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271342r1108642_rule","rule_id":"SV-271342r1108642","ccis":["CCI-002233"],"uuid":"F2033A6F-6BF8-1014-8265-FAABC723BC80","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false"},{"group_id":"V-271343","check_content":"If the database is setup to write audit logs using APPLICATION or SECURITY event logs rather than writing to a file, this is Not Applicable.\n\nCheck the server documentation for the SQL Audit file size configurations. Locate the Audit file path and drive. \n \nSELECT max_file_size, max_rollover_files, log_file_path AS \"Audit Path\"  \nFROM sys.server_file_audits \n \nCalculate the space needed as the maximum file size and number of files from the SQL Audit File properties. \n \nIf the calculated product of the \"max_file_size\" times the \"max_rollover_files\" exceeds the size of the storage location, this is a finding; \n\nOR if \"max_file_size\" is set to \"0\" (Unlimited), this is a finding;\n\nOR if \"max_rollover_files\" are set to \"0\" (None) or \"2147483647\" (Unlimited), this is a finding.","rule_title":"SQL Server must allocate audit record storage capacity in accordance with organization-defined audit record storage requirements.","group_id_src":"V-271343","mitigation_control":"","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:10101"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271343, SV-271343r1108645, SRG-APP-000357-DB-000316)\n","rule_version":"SQLI-22-010900","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000357-DB-000316","id":"V-271343"},"status":"not_reviewed","weight":"10.0","ia_controls":"","fix_text":"Review the SQL Audit file location; ensure the destination has enough space available to accommodate the maximum total size of all files that could be written. \n \nConfigure the maximum number of audit log files that are to be generated, staying within the number of logs the system was sized to support. \n \nUpdate the \"max_files\" or \"max_rollover_files\" parameter of the audits to ensure the correct number of files is defined.\n\nIf writing to application event logs or security logs, space considerations are covered in the Windows Server STIGs. Be sure to reference these depending on the OS in use.","false_positives":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271343r1108645_rule","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000357-DB-000316","discussion":"Organizations are required to use a central log management system, so, under normal conditions, the audit space allocated to SQL Server on its own server will not be an issue. However, space will still be required on the server for SQL Server Audit records in transit, and, under abnormal conditions, this could fill up. Since a requirement exists to halt processing upon audit failure, a service outage would result. \n \nIf support personnel are not notified immediately upon storage volume utilization reaching 75 percent, they are unable to plan for storage capacity expansion. \n \nThe appropriate support staff include, at a minimum, the information system security officer (ISSO), the database administrator (DBA), and system administrator (SA). \n \nMonitoring of free space can be accomplished using Microsoft System Center or a third-party monitoring tool.","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"uuid":"F203522E-6BF8-1014-BE78-85A7964859D3","comments":null,"mitigations":"","ccis":["CCI-001849"],"rule_id":"SV-271343r1108645"},{"uuid":"F203630F-6BF8-1014-A65F-8F03AB87BE62","comments":null,"mitigations":"","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"rule_id":"SV-271344r1111082","ccis":["CCI-001855"],"security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271344r1111082_rule","group_title":"SRG-APP-000359-DB-000319","discussion":"Organizations are required to use a central log management system, so, under normal conditions, the audit space allocated to SQL Server on its own server will not be an issue. However, space will still be required on the server for SQL Server Audit records in transit, and, under abnormal conditions, this could fill up. Since a requirement exists to halt processing upon audit failure, a service outage would result. \n \nIf support personnel are not notified immediately upon storage volume utilization reaching 75 percent, they are unable to plan for storage capacity expansion. \n \nThe appropriate support staff include, at a minimum, the information system security officer (ISSO), the database administrator (DBA), and the system administrator (SA). \n \nMonitoring of free space can be accomplished using Microsoft System Center or a third-party monitoring tool.","severity":"medium","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000359-DB-000319","id":"V-271344"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-011000","weight":"10.0","status":"not_reviewed","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271344, SV-271344r1111082, SRG-APP-000359-DB-000319)\n","ia_controls":"","fix_text":"Use operating system alerting mechanisms, SQL Agent, Operations Management tools, and/or third-party tools to configure the system to notify appropriate support staff immediately upon storage volume utilization reaching 75 percent.","false_positives":"","rule_title":"SQL Server must provide a warning to appropriate support staff when allocated audit record storage volume reaches 75 percent of maximum audit record storage capacity.","group_id":"V-271344","check_content":"The operating system and SQL Server offer a number of methods for checking the drive or volume free space. Locate the destination drive where SQL Audits are stored and review system configuration. \n \nIf no alert exists to notify support staff in the event the SQL Audit drive reaches 75 percent, this is a finding.","mitigation_control":"","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:10301"},"group_id_src":"V-271344"},{"ia_controls":"","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Configure the system to provide immediate real-time alerts to appropriate support staff when an audit log failure occurs.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271345, SV-271345r1109254, SRG-APP-000360-DB-000320)\n","rule_version":"SQLI-22-011100","group_tree":{"id":"V-271345","title":"SRG-APP-000360-DB-000320"},"weight":"10.0","status":"not_reviewed","group_id_src":"V-271345","mitigation_control":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:10501","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-271345","check_content":"Review SQL Server settings, OS, or third-party logging software settings to determine whether a real-time alert will be sent to the appropriate personnel when auditing fails for any reason.\n\nIf real-time alerts are not sent upon auditing failure, this is a finding.","rule_title":"SQL Server must provide an immediate real-time alert to appropriate support staff of all audit log failures.","ccis":["CCI-001858"],"rule_id":"SV-271345r1109254","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","uuid":"F2036E16-6BF8-1014-B5B9-ADDFB140BFE6","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000360-DB-000320","discussion":"It is critical for the appropriate personnel to be aware if a system is at risk of failing to process audit logs as required. Without a real-time alert, security personnel may be unaware of an impending failure of the audit capability, and system operation may be adversely affected. \n\nThe appropriate support staff include, at a minimum, the information system security officer (ISSO), the database administrator (DBA), and the system administrator (SA).\n\nA failure of database auditing will result in either the database continuing to function without auditing or in a complete halt to database operations. When audit processing fails, appropriate personnel must be alerted immediately to avoid further downtime or unaudited transactions.\n\nAlerts provide organizations with urgent messages. Real-time alerts provide these messages immediately (i.e., the time from event detection to alert occurs in seconds or less). Alerts can be generated using tools like the SQL Server Agent Alerts and Database Mail.","rule_id_src":"SV-271345r1109254_rule","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":""},{"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","severity":"medium","discussion":"If time stamps are not consistently applied and there is no common time reference, it is difficult to perform forensic analysis. \n \nTime stamps generated by SQL Server must include date and time. Time is commonly expressed in UTC, a modern continuation of GMT, or local time with an offset from UTC.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000374-DB-000322","rule_id_src":"SV-271346r1109256_rule","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-001890"],"rule_id":"SV-271346r1109256","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","uuid":"F2037C45-6BF8-1014-A02C-B7DE6716AB59","mitigations":"","comments":null,"group_id_src":"V-271346","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:10701","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml"},"mitigation_control":"","check_content":"SQL Server Audits store the timestamp in UTC time. \n \nDetermine if the computer is joined to a domain. \n \nSELECT DEFAULT_DOMAIN()[DomainName]  \n \nIf this is not NULL, this is not a finding. \n \nIf the computer is not joined to a domain, determine what the time source is. (Run the following command in an elevated PowerShell session.) \n \n     w32tm /query /source \n \nIf the results of the command return \"Local CMOS Clock\" and this is not documented with justification and authorizing official (AO) authorization, this is a finding. \n \nIf the OS does not synchronize with a time server, review the procedure for maintaining accurate time on the system. \n \nIf such a procedure does not exist, this is a finding. \n \nIf the procedure exists, review evidence that the correct time is actually maintained. \n \nIf the evidence indicates otherwise, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271346","rule_title":"SQL Server must record time stamps in audit records and application data that can be mapped to Coordinated Universal Time (UTC), formerly Greenwich Mean Time (GMT).","fix_text":"Where possible, configure the operating system to automatic synchronize with an official time server, using NTP. \n \nWhere there is reason not to implement automatic synchronization with an official time server, using NTP, document the reason, and the procedure for maintaining the correct time, and obtain AO approval. Enforce the procedure.","false_positives":"","ia_controls":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271346, SV-271346r1109256, SRG-APP-000374-DB-000322)\n","weight":"10.0","status":"not_reviewed","rule_version":"SQLI-22-011200","group_tree":{"id":"V-271346","title":"SRG-APP-000374-DB-000322"}},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Return all enabled users that are part of the local Administrators Group)\nResult Analysis         :        For 'SOT-WIN2K22-SQL\\degthat': 'SOT-WIN2K22-SQL\\degthat' failed test of 'equals' compared to ''\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27134901 (user_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Return all enabled users that are part of the local Administrators Group\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27134901 (user_object)\nObject Comment          : Enabled Local Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27134901 (user_state)\nState Comment           : End user authorized user accounts\nState Requirement       : for alluser, at least one of the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     user must be equal to ''\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : user equals 'SOT-WIN2K22-SQL\\degthat'\n                        : enabled equals 'true'\n                        : group equals 'Administrators'\n                        : group equals 'Remote Desktop Users'\n                        : last_logon equals '1788628256'\n                        : full_name equals 'degthat'\n                        : comment equals ''\n                        : password_age_days equals '946'\n\nResult Analysis         : For 'SOT-WIN2K22-SQL\\degthat': 'SOT-WIN2K22-SQL\\degthat' failed test of 'equals' compared to ''\n","group_tree":{"id":"V-271349","title":"SRG-APP-000380-DB-000360"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-011500","status":"open","weight":"10.0","ia_controls":"","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Remove users from the local Administrators group who are not authorized.","group_id":"V-271349","check_content":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:var:27134902;;Instance;;user_name;;Array","rule_title":"Windows must enforce access restrictions associated with changes to the configuration of the SQL Server instance.","group_id_src":"V-271349","mitigation_control":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271349"},"potential_impacts":"","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","comments":null,"uuid":"F203886D-6BF8-1014-8E3F-CF491958C2FE","ccis":["CCI-001813"],"rule_id":"SV-271349r1108938","rule_id_src":"SV-271349r1108938_rule","security_override_guidance":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","severity":"medium","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","group_title":"SRG-APP-000380-DB-000360","discussion":"Failure to provide logical access restrictions associated with changes to configuration may have significant effects on the overall security of the system. \n \nWhen dealing with access restrictions pertaining to change control, it should be noted that any changes to the hardware, software, and/or firmware components of the information system can potentially have significant effects on the overall security of the system. \n \nAccordingly, only qualified and authorized individuals should be allowed to obtain access to system components for the purposes of initiating changes, including upgrades and modifications."},{"rule_id_src":"SV-271350r1111084_rule","third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","discussion":"Failure to provide logical access restrictions associated with changes to configuration may have significant effects on the overall security of the system. \n \nWhen dealing with access restrictions pertaining to change control, it should be noted that any changes to the hardware, software, and/or firmware components of the information system can potentially have significant effects on the overall security of the system. \n \nAccordingly, only qualified and authorized individuals should be allowed to obtain access to system components for the purposes of initiating changes, including upgrades and modifications.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000380-DB-000360","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","mitigations":"","comments":null,"uuid":"F20393D2-6BF8-1014-96F0-A593B49FA69F","ccis":["CCI-001813"],"rule_id":"SV-271350r1111084","check_content":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:var:27135004;;Instance;;user_name;;Array","group_id":"V-271350","rule_title":"SQL Server must enforce access restrictions associated with changes to the configuration of the instance.","group_id_src":"V-271350","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271350"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Check if users with 'CONTROL SERVER' are authorized and documented.)\nTest                    :   false (Check if users with 'sysadmin','securityadmin','serveradmin' are authorized and documented.)\nResult Analysis         :        Collected Item did not meet the state requirement.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27135001 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Check if users with 'CONTROL SERVER' are authorized and documented.\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27135001 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT p.name AS user_name, \n                        : p.type_desc AS Type, \n                        : sp.permission_name AS Permission,  \n                        : sp.state_desc AS State \n                        : FROM sys.server_principals p \n                        : INNER JOIN sys.server_permissions sp ON p.principal_id = sp.grantee_principal_id \n                        : WHERE sp.permission_name = 'CONTROL SERVER' \n                        : OR sp.state = 'W''\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27135001 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : If 'user_name' matches user entered authorized/documented values, this is not a finding.\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : Field Requirement       : for at least one user_name, at least one of the following must be true:\n                        : Field Requirement       : user_name must be equal (case insensitive) to  the value(s) in End user provided list of documented and approved database user names allowed to have 'CONTROL SERVER' or be a member of 'syadmin','securityadmin','serveradmin'\n                        : Field Requirement       :     user_name must be equal (case insensitive) to ''\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql does not exist\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27135002 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Check if users with 'sysadmin','securityadmin','serveradmin' are authorized and documented.\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27135002 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT m.name AS user_name, \n                        : m.type_desc AS Type, \n                        : r.name AS Role \n                        : FROM sys.server_principals m \n                        : INNER JOIN sys.server_role_members rm ON m.principal_id = rm.member_principal_id \n                        : INNER JOIN sys.server_principals r ON rm.role_principal_id = r.principal_id \n                        : WHERE r.name IN ('sysadmin','securityadmin','serveradmin') \n                        :  '\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27135001 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : If 'user_name' matches user entered authorized/documented values, this is not a finding.\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : Field Requirement       : for at least one user_name, at least one of the following must be true:\n                        : Field Requirement       : user_name must be equal (case insensitive) to  the value(s) in End user provided list of documented and approved database user names allowed to have 'CONTROL SERVER' or be a member of 'syadmin','securityadmin','serveradmin'\n                        : Field Requirement       :     user_name must be equal (case insensitive) to ''\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT m.name AS user_name, \n                        : m.type_desc AS Type, \n                        : r.name AS Role \n                        : FROM sys.server_principals m \n                        : INNER JOIN sys.server_role_members rm ON m.principal_id = rm.member_principal_id \n                        : INNER JOIN sys.server_principals r ON rm.role_principal_id = r.principal_id \n                        : WHERE r.name IN ('sysadmin','securityadmin','serveradmin') \n                        :  '\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : !![ user_name = 'sa' ]!!\n                        : type = 'SQL_LOGIN'\n                        : role = 'sysadmin'\n\nResult Analysis         : Collected Item did not meet the state requirement.\n","status":"open","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000380-DB-000360","id":"V-271350"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-011400","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Revoke unauthorized permissions from principals. \n \nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/t-sql/statements/revoke-server-permissions-transact-sql?\n \nRemove unauthorized logins from roles. \n \nALTER SERVER ROLE DROP MEMBER login; \n \nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/t-sql/statements/alter-server-role-transact-sql?","ia_controls":""},{"reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","discussion":"Without auditing the enforcement of access restrictions against changes to configuration, it would be difficult to identify attempted attacks, and an audit trail would not be available for forensic investigation for after-the-fact actions.\n \nEnforcement actions are the methods or mechanisms used to prevent unauthorized changes to configuration settings. Enforcement action methods may be as simple as denying access to a file based on the application of file permissions (access restriction). Audit items may consist of lists of actions blocked by access restrictions or changes identified after the fact.\n\nChanges in the permissions, privileges, and roles granted to users and roles, as well as privileged activity, must be tracked. Without an audit trail, unauthorized elevation or restriction of privileges could go undetected. Elevated privileges give users access to information and functionality that they should not have; restricted privileges wrongly deny access to authorized users.\n \nA privileged function in this context is any operation that modifies the structure of the database, its built-in logic, or its security settings. This would include all Data Definition Language (DDL) statements and all security-related statements. In a SQL environment, it encompasses, but is not necessarily limited to, CREATE, ALTER, DROP, GRANT, REVOKE, and DENY. \n \nThere may also be Data Manipulation Language (DML) statements that, subject to context, should be regarded as privileged. Possible examples in SQL include TRUNCATE TABLE, SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, or DELETE (to a security table executed by a user other than a security principal).\n \nDepending on the capabilities of SQL Server and the design of the database and associated applications, audit logging may be achieved by means of DBMS auditing features, database triggers, other mechanisms, or a combination of these. \n \nNote that it is particularly important to audit, and tightly control, any action that weakens the implementation of this requirement, since the objective is to have a complete audit trail of all administrative activity.\n \nTo aid in diagnosis, it is necessary to track failed attempts in addition to the successful ones.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-APP-000381-DB-000361, SRG-APP-000495-DB-000326, SRG-APP-000495-DB-000327, SRG-APP-000495-DB-000328, SRG-APP-000495-DB-000329, SRG-APP-000499-DB-000330, SRG-APP-000499-DB-000331, SRG-APP-000504-DB-000354, SRG-APP-000504-DB-000355","group_title":"SRG-APP-000381-DB-000361","rule_id_src":"SV-271351r1167494_rule","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-003938","CCI-000172"],"rule_id":"SV-271351r1167494","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","comments":null,"mitigations":"","uuid":"F203A176-6BF8-1014-B292-CE5145582CE3","group_id_src":"V-271351","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271351"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":"","check_content":"Review the SQL configuration to verify that audit records are produced when denied actions occur.\n\nTo determine if an audit is configured, execute the following script:\n\nSELECT name AS 'Audit Name',\nstatus_desc AS 'Audit Status',\naudit_file_path AS 'Current Audit File'\nFROM sys.dm_server_audit_status\n\nIf no records are returned, this is a finding.\n\nExecute the following to verify the following events are included in the server audit specification:\n\nAPPLICATION_ROLE_CHANGE_PASSWORD_GROUP,\nAUDIT_CHANGE_GROUP,\nBACKUP_RESTORE_GROUP,\nDATABASE_CHANGE_GROUP,\nDATABASE_OBJECT_ACCESS_GROUP,\nDATABASE_OBJECT_CHANGE_GROUP,\nDATABASE_OBJECT_OWNERSHIP_CHANGE_GROUP,\nDATABASE_OBJECT_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP,\nDATABASE_OWNERSHIP_CHANGE_GROUP,\nDATABASE_OPERATION_GROUP,\nDATABASE_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP,\nDATABASE_PRINCIPAL_CHANGE_GROUP,\nDATABASE_PRINCIPAL_IMPERSONATION_GROUP,\nDATABASE_ROLE_MEMBER_CHANGE_GROUP,\nDBCC_GROUP,\nLOGIN_CHANGE_PASSWORD_GROUP,\nLOGOUT_GROUP,\nSCHEMA_OBJECT_OWNERSHIP_CHANGE_GROUP,\nSCHEMA_OBJECT_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP,\nSERVER_OBJECT_CHANGE_GROUP,\nSERVER_OBJECT_OWNERSHIP_CHANGE_GROUP,\nSERVER_OBJECT_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP,\nSERVER_OPERATION_GROUP,\nSERVER_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP,\nSERVER_PRINCIPAL_CHANGE_GROUP,\nSERVER_PRINCIPAL_IMPERSONATION_GROUP,\nSERVER_ROLE_MEMBER_CHANGE_GROUP,\nSERVER_STATE_CHANGE_GROUP,\nTRACE_CHANGE_GROUP,\nUSER_CHANGE_PASSWORD_GROUP\n\nSELECT a.name AS 'AuditName',\ns.name AS 'SpecName',\nd.audit_action_name AS 'ActionName',\nd.audited_result AS 'Result'\nFROM sys.server_audit_specifications s\nJOIN sys.server_audits a ON s.audit_guid = a.audit_guid\nJOIN sys.server_audit_specification_details d ON s.server_specification_id = d.server_specification_id\nWHERE a.is_state_enabled = 1\nAND d.audit_action_name IN (\n'APPLICATION_ROLE_CHANGE_PASSWORD_GROUP',\n'AUDIT_CHANGE_GROUP',\n'BACKUP_RESTORE_GROUP',\n'DATABASE_CHANGE_GROUP',\n'DATABASE_OBJECT_ACCESS_GROUP',\n'DATABASE_OBJECT_CHANGE_GROUP',\n'DATABASE_OBJECT_OWNERSHIP_CHANGE_GROUP',\n'DATABASE_OBJECT_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP',\n'DATABASE_OWNERSHIP_CHANGE_GROUP',\n'DATABASE_OPERATION_GROUP',\n'DATABASE_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP',\n'DATABASE_PRINCIPAL_CHANGE_GROUP',\n'DATABASE_PRINCIPAL_IMPERSONATION_GROUP',\n'DATABASE_ROLE_MEMBER_CHANGE_GROUP', \n'DBCC_GROUP',\n'LOGIN_CHANGE_PASSWORD_GROUP',\n'LOGOUT_GROUP',\n'SCHEMA_OBJECT_OWNERSHIP_CHANGE_GROUP',\n'SCHEMA_OBJECT_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP',\n'SERVER_OBJECT_CHANGE_GROUP',\n'SERVER_OBJECT_OWNERSHIP_CHANGE_GROUP',\n'SERVER_OBJECT_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP',\n'SERVER_OPERATION_GROUP',\n'SERVER_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP',\n'SERVER_PRINCIPAL_CHANGE_GROUP',\n'SERVER_PRINCIPAL_IMPERSONATION_GROUP',\n'SERVER_ROLE_MEMBER_CHANGE_GROUP',\n'SERVER_STATE_CHANGE_GROUP',\n'TRACE_CHANGE_GROUP',\n'USER_CHANGE_PASSWORD_GROUP'\n)\nOrder by d.audit_action_name\n\nIf the identified groups are not returned, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271351","rule_title":"SQL Server must produce audit records when attempts to modify SQL Server configuration and privileges occur within the database(s).","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Add the required events to the server audit specification to audit denied actions.\n\nRefer to the supplemental file \"SQL2022Audit.sql\" script.\n\nReference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/relational-databases/security/auditing/sql-server-audit-database-engine?","ia_controls":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   error (Determine if an audit is configured and started)\nTest                    :   false (Determine if an audit is configured to capture denied actions. This query will return only items that are missing. No results = pass.)\nResult Analysis         :        Existence requirement is 'none_exists' and 1 collected item exists, so result is false\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27135101 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : error\nTest Title              : Determine if an audit is configured and started\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27135101 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name AS 'audit_name',\n                        : \t\t\t\tstatus_desc AS 'audit_status',\n                        : \t\t\t\taudit_file_path AS 'current_audit_file'\n                        : \t\t\t\tFROM sys.dm_server_audit_status'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27135101 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : If an audit is not STARTED this is a finding.\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all audit_status must be equal to 'STARTED'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : error\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT name AS 'audit_name',\n                        : \t\t\t\tstatus_desc AS 'audit_status',\n                        : \t\t\t\taudit_file_path AS 'current_audit_file'\n                        : \t\t\t\tFROM sys.dm_server_audit_status'\n\nError Information       : Unable to retrieve any data with SQL transaction \"SELECT name AS 'audit_name',\n                        : \t\t\t\tstatus_desc AS 'audit_status',\n                        : \t\t\t\taudit_file_path AS 'current_audit_file'\n                        : \t\t\t\tFROM sys.dm_server_audit_status from DBMS instance \"SQLEXPRESS\" on server \"SOT-WIN2K22-SQL\" Error: [Microsoft][ODBC Driver 17 for SQL Server][SQL Server]VIEW SERVER SECURITY STATE permission was denied on object 'server', database 'master'. (SQL-42000)\n                        : [Microsoft][ODBC Driver 17 for SQL Server][SQL Server]The user does not have permission to perform this action. (SQL-42000)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27135102 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Determine if an audit is configured to capture denied actions. This query will return only items that are missing. No results = pass.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27135102 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'select 'APPLICATION_ROLE_CHANGE_PASSWORD_GROUP' as audit_action_name\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'AUDIT_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'BACKUP_RESTORE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_OBJECT_ACCESS_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_OBJECT_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_OBJECT_OWNERSHIP_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_OBJECT_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_OPERATION_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_OWNERSHIP_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_PRINCIPAL_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_PRINCIPAL_IMPERSONATION_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_ROLE_MEMBER_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DBCC_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'LOGIN_CHANGE_PASSWORD_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SCHEMA_OBJECT_OWNERSHIP_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SCHEMA_OBJECT_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SERVER_OBJECT_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SERVER_OBJECT_OWNERSHIP_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SERVER_OBJECT_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SERVER_OPERATION_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SERVER_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SERVER_PRINCIPAL_IMPERSONATION_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SERVER_ROLE_MEMBER_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SERVER_STATE_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'TRACE_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\texcept\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tSELECT d.audit_action_name AS 'ActionName'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFROM sys.server_audit_specifications s\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tJOIN sys.server_audits a ON s.audit_guid = a.audit_guid\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tJOIN sys.server_audit_specification_details d ON s.server_specification_id = d.server_specification_id\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tWHERE a.is_state_enabled = 1\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tand s.is_state_enabled = 1\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tand d.audited_result like '%FAILURE%'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tand d.audited_result like '%FAILURE%''\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'select 'APPLICATION_ROLE_CHANGE_PASSWORD_GROUP' as audit_action_name\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'AUDIT_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'BACKUP_RESTORE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_OBJECT_ACCESS_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_OBJECT_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_OBJECT_OWNERSHIP_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_OBJECT_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_OPERATION_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_OWNERSHIP_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_PRINCIPAL_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_PRINCIPAL_IMPERSONATION_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DATABASE_ROLE_MEMBER_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'DBCC_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'LOGIN_CHANGE_PASSWORD_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SCHEMA_OBJECT_OWNERSHIP_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SCHEMA_OBJECT_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SERVER_OBJECT_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SERVER_OBJECT_OWNERSHIP_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SERVER_OBJECT_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SERVER_OPERATION_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SERVER_PERMISSION_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SERVER_PRINCIPAL_IMPERSONATION_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SERVER_ROLE_MEMBER_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'SERVER_STATE_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\tunion select 'TRACE_CHANGE_GROUP'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\texcept\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tSELECT d.audit_action_name AS 'ActionName'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFROM sys.server_audit_specifications s\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tJOIN sys.server_audits a ON s.audit_guid = a.audit_guid\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tJOIN sys.server_audit_specification_details d ON s.server_specification_id = d.server_specification_id\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tWHERE a.is_state_enabled = 1\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tand s.is_state_enabled = 1\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tand d.audited_result like '%FAILURE%'\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tand d.audited_result like '%FAILURE%''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : collected 'result' result: \n\nResult Analysis         : Existence requirement is 'none_exists' and 1 collected item exists, so result is false\n","weight":"10.0","status":"open","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000381-DB-000361","id":"V-271351"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-011800"},{"rule_id":"SV-271358r1137659","ccis":["CCI-002530"],"uuid":"F203AE51-6BF8-1014-B33C-D87CCB420CC7","mitigations":"","comments":null,"documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"group_title":"SRG-APP-000431-DB-000388","discussion":"Database management systems can maintain separate execution domains for each executing process by assigning each process a separate address space. Each process has a distinct address space so that communication between processes is controlled through the security functions, and one process cannot modify the executing code of another process. Maintaining separate execution domains for executing processes can be achieved, for example, by implementing separate address spaces.","severity":"medium","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271358r1137659_rule","ia_controls":"","fix_text":"Configure SQL Server services to have a documented, dedicated account. \n \nFor nondomain servers, consider using virtual service accounts (VSAs). \nFor more information, refer to: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/database-engine/configure-windows/configure-windows-service-accounts-and-permissions? \n \nFor standalone domain-joined servers, consider using managed service accounts. \nFor more information, refer to: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/database-engine/configure-windows/configure-windows-service-accounts-and-permissions?\n \nFor clustered instances, consider using group managed service accounts. \nFor more information, refer to: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/database-engine/configure-windows/configure-windows-service-accounts-and-permissions? \nor \nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/archive/blogs/markweberblog/group-managed-service-accounts-gmsa-and-sql-server-2016","false_positives":"","rule_version":"SQLI-22-012400","group_tree":{"id":"V-271358","title":"SRG-APP-000431-DB-000388"},"weight":"10.0","status":"not_reviewed","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271358, SV-271358r1137659, SRG-APP-000431-DB-000388)\n","mitigation_control":"","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:11501"},"group_id_src":"V-271358","rule_title":"SQL Server services must be configured to run under unique dedicated user accounts.","group_id":"V-271358","check_content":"Review the server documentation to obtain a listing of required service accounts. Review the accounts configured for all SQL Server services installed on the server. \n \nRun the following query in SSMS:\n\nSELECT servicename,service_account FROM sys.dm_server_services\n \nReview the returned results. If any services are configured with the same service account or with an account that is not documented and authorized, this is a finding."},{"legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","mitigations":"","comments":null,"uuid":"F203BBBA-6BF8-1014-987E-FF72619D8649","ccis":["CCI-002530"],"rule_id":"SV-271359r1137659","rule_id_src":"SV-271359r1137659_rule","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","discussion":"Database management systems can maintain separate execution domains for each executing process by assigning each process a separate address space. \n \nEach process has a distinct address space so that communication between processes is controlled through the security functions, and one process cannot modify the executing code of another process. \n \nMaintaining separate execution domains for executing processes can be achieved, for example, by implementing separate address spaces.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000431-DB-000388","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (If 'value_in_use' is a '1' and CLR is not required, this is a finding)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27135901 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If 'value_in_use' is a '1' and CLR is not required, this is a finding\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27135901 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'clr enabled''\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27135901 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : If value_in_use' is a '1' and CLR is not required, this is a finding.\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all value_in_use must not be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'clr enabled''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : name = 'clr enabled'\n                        : value_in_use = '0'\n                        : value = '0'\n","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"SQLI-22-012300","group_tree":{"id":"V-271359","title":"SRG-APP-000431-DB-000388"},"false_positives":"","fix_text":"Disable use of or remove any CLR code that is not authorized.\n\nTo disable the use of CLR, from the query prompt:  \nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'clr enabled', 0;\nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE;","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Review the server documentation to determine whether use of CLR assemblies is required. Run the following query to determine whether CLR is enabled for the instance: \nSELECT name, value, value_in_use \nFROM sys.configurations \nWHERE name = 'clr enabled' \n \nIf \"value_in_use\" is a \"1\" and CLR is not required, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271359","rule_title":"SQL Server must maintain a separate execution domain for each executing process.","group_id_src":"V-271359","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271359","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":""},{"rule_title":"When invalid inputs are received, the SQL Server must behave in a predictable and documented manner that reflects organizational and system objectives.","check_content":"Review DBMS code (stored procedures, functions, triggers), application code, settings, column and field definitions, and constraints to determine whether the database is protected against invalid input. \n\nIf code exists that allows invalid data to be acted upon or input into the database, this is a finding. \n\nIf column/field definitions are not reflective of the data, this is a finding. \n\nIf columns/fields do not contain constraints and validity checking where required, this is a finding. \n\nWhere a column/field is noted in the system documentation as necessarily free form, even though its name and context suggest that it should be strongly typed and constrained, the absence of these protections is not a finding. \n\nWhere a column/field is clearly identified by name, caption or context as Notes, Comments, Description, Text, etc., the absence of these protections is not a finding.","group_id":"V-271362","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:11901","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml"},"mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-271362","weight":"10.0","status":"not_reviewed","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000447-DB-000393","id":"V-271362"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-012600","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271362, SV-271362r1108702, SRG-APP-000447-DB-000393)\n","fix_text":"Use parameterized queries, stored procedures, constraints and foreign keys to validate data input. \n\nModify SQL Server to properly use the correct column data types as required in the database.","false_positives":"","ia_controls":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271362r1108702_rule","discussion":"A common vulnerability is unplanned behavior when invalid inputs are received. This requirement guards against adverse or unintended system behavior caused by invalid inputs, where information system responses to the invalid input may be disruptive or cause the system to fail into an unsafe state.\n\nThe behavior will be derived from the organizational and system requirements and includes, but is not limited to, notification of the appropriate personnel, creating an audit record, and rejecting invalid input.\n\nThis calls for inspection of application source code, which will require collaboration with the application developers. It is recognized that in many cases, the database administrator (DBA) is organizationally separate from the application developers, and may have limited, if any, access to source code. Nevertheless, protections of this type are so important to the secure operation of databases that they must not be ignored. At a minimum, the DBA must attempt to obtain assurances from the development organization that this issue has been addressed and must document what has been discovered.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000447-DB-000393","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","uuid":"F203D450-6BF8-1014-8D26-A06915B44484","comments":null,"mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","rule_id":"SV-271362r1108702","ccis":["CCI-002754"]},{"rule_id_src":"SV-271364r1137667_rule","third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","severity":"medium","discussion":"Security flaws with software applications, including database management systems, are discovered daily. Vendors are constantly updating and patching their products to address newly discovered security vulnerabilities. Organizations (including any contractor to the organization) are required to promptly install security-relevant software updates (e.g., patches, service packs, and hot fixes). Flaws discovered during security assessments, continuous monitoring, incident response activities, or information system error handling must also be addressed expeditiously. \n \nOrganization-defined time periods for updating security-relevant software may vary based on a variety of factors including, for example, the security category of the information system or the criticality of the update (i.e., severity of the vulnerability related to the discovered flaw). \n \nThis requirement will apply to software patch management solutions that are used to install patches across the enclave and also to applications themselves that are not part of that patch management solution. For example, many browsers today provide the capability to install their own patch software. Patch criticality, as well as system criticality, will vary. Therefore, the tactical situations regarding the patch management process will also vary. This means that the time period used must be a configurable parameter. Time frames for application of security-relevant software updates may be dependent upon the Information Assurance Vulnerability Management (IAVM) process. \n \nSQL Server will be configured to check for and install security-relevant software updates within an identified time period from the availability of the update. The specific time period will be defined by an authoritative source (e.g., IAVM, CTOs, DTMs, and STIGs).","group_title":"SRG-APP-000456-DB-000390","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","uuid":"F203E4CE-6BF8-1014-B354-86E7E35D77C9","mitigations":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-002605"],"rule_id":"SV-271364r1137667","check_content":"Obtain evidence that software patches are consistently applied to SQL Server within the time frame defined for each patch. To be considered supported, Microsoft must report that the version is supported by security patches to known vulnerability. Review the Support dates at https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/troubleshoot/sql/releases/download-and-install-latest-updates.\n \nCheck the SQL Server version by running the following script: \n\nPrint @@version \n \nIf the SQL Server version is not shown as supported, this is a finding. \n \nIf such evidence cannot be obtained, or the evidence that is obtained indicates a pattern of noncompliance, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271364","rule_title":"Security-relevant software updates to SQL Server must be installed within the time period directed by an authoritative source (e.g., IAVM, CTOs, DTMs, and STIGs).","group_id_src":"V-271364","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:12101"},"mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271364, SV-271364r1137667, SRG-APP-000456-DB-000390)\n","weight":"10.0","status":"not_reviewed","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000456-DB-000390","id":"V-271364"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-012800","fix_text":"Upgrade SQL Server to the Microsoft-supported version. Institute and adhere to policies and procedures to ensure that patches are consistently applied to SQL Server within the time allowed.","false_positives":"","ia_controls":""},{"group_title":"SRG-APP-000456-DB-000400","discussion":"Unsupported commercial and database systems should not be used because fixes to newly identified bugs will not be implemented by the vendor. The lack of support can result in potential vulnerabilities.\n\nSystems at unsupported servicing levels or releases will not receive security updates for new vulnerabilities, which leaves them subject to exploitation.\n\nWhen maintenance updates and patches are no longer available, the database software is no longer considered supported and should be upgraded or decommissioned.","severity":"high","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","security_override_guidance":"","third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271365r1138543_rule","rule_id":"SV-271365r1138543","ccis":["CCI-003376"],"uuid":"F203EFCC-6BF8-1014-A007-B805F67A7C00","mitigations":"","comments":null,"documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"mitigation_control":"","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:12301"},"group_id_src":"V-271365","rule_title":"Microsoft SQL Server products must be a version supported by the vendor.","group_id":"V-271365","check_content":"Review the system documentation and interview the database administrator.\n\nIdentify all database software components.\n\nReview the version and release information.\n\nVerify the SQL Server version via one of the following methods: \n\nConnect to the server by using Object Explorer in SQL Server Management Studio. After Object Explorer is connected, it will show the version information in parentheses with the username used to connect to the specific instance of SQL Server.\n\nOr, from SQL Server Management Studio execute the following:\nSELECT @@VERSION;\n\nMore information for finding the version is available at the following link: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/troubleshoot/sql/releases/find-my-sql-version.\n\nAccess the vendor website or use other means to verify the version is still supported. Refer to https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/lifecycle/products/sql-server-2016.\n\nIf the installed version or any of the software components are not supported by the vendor, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","fix_text":"Remove or decommission all unsupported software products.\n\nUpgrade unsupported DBMS or unsupported components to a supported version of the product.","false_positives":"","rule_version":"SQLI-22-018300","group_tree":{"id":"V-271365","title":"SRG-APP-000456-DB-000400"},"status":"not_reviewed","weight":"10.0","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT I, V-271365, SV-271365r1138543, SRG-APP-000456-DB-000400)\n"},{"ccis":["CCI-000172"],"rule_id":"SV-271370r1111091","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","uuid":"F203FA21-6BF8-1014-B92F-A7FA41174715","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000496-DB-000334","discussion":"Changes and deletions of the database objects (tables, views, procedures, functions) that record and control permissions, privileges, and roles granted to users and roles must be tracked. Without an audit trail, unauthorized changes to the security subsystem could go undetected. The database could be severely compromised or rendered inoperative. \n \nTo aid in diagnosis, it is necessary to track failed attempts in addition to the successful ones.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-APP-000496-DB-000334, SRG-APP-000496-DB-000335, SRG-APP-000501-DB-000336, SRG-APP-000501-DB-000337","rule_id_src":"SV-271370r1111091_rule","security_override_guidance":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","ia_controls":"","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Add the required events to the server audit specification to audit denied actions.\n\nRefer to the supplemental file \"SQL2022Audit.sql\" script.\n\nReference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/relational-databases/security/auditing/sql-server-audit-database-engine?","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   error (Determine if an audit is configured and started)\nTest                    :   false (If 'verify the SCHEMA_OBJECT_CHANGE_GROUP is included in the server audit specification)\nResult Analysis         :        .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n                        :         .  \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27137001 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : error\nTest Title              : Determine if an audit is configured and started\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27137001 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name AS 'audit_name',\n                        : \t\t\t\tstatus_desc AS 'audit_status',\n                        : \t\t\t\taudit_file_path AS 'current_audit_file'\n                        : \t\t\t\tFROM sys.dm_server_audit_status'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27137001 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : If an audit is not STARTED this is a finding.\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all audit_status must be equal to 'STARTED'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : error\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT name AS 'audit_name',\n                        : \t\t\t\tstatus_desc AS 'audit_status',\n                        : \t\t\t\taudit_file_path AS 'current_audit_file'\n                        : \t\t\t\tFROM sys.dm_server_audit_status'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27137002 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : If 'verify the SCHEMA_OBJECT_CHANGE_GROUP is included in the server audit specification\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27137002 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT a.name AS 'AuditName', \n                        :   s.name AS 'SpecName', \n                        :   d.audit_action_name AS 'ActionName', \n                        :   d.audited_result AS 'Result' \n                        : FROM sys.server_audit_specifications s \n                        : JOIN sys.server_audits a ON s.audit_guid = a.audit_guid \n                        : JOIN sys.server_audit_specification_details d ON s.server_specification_id = d.server_specification_id \n                        : WHERE a.is_state_enabled = 1 AND d.audit_action_name = 'SCHEMA_OBJECT_CHANGE_GROUP' \n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : !![ sql does not exist ]!!\n\nResult Analysis         : .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nResult Analysis         :  .  \n","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000496-DB-000334","id":"V-271370"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-013800","weight":"10.0","status":"open","group_id_src":"V-271370","mitigation_control":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271370"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-271370","check_content":"Review the SQL configuration to verify that audit records are produced when denied actions occur.\n\nTo determine if an audit is configured, execute the following script:\nSELECT name AS 'Audit Name',\nstatus_desc AS 'Audit Status',\naudit_file_path AS 'Current Audit File'\nFROM sys.dm_server_audit_status\n\nIf no records are returned, this is a finding.\n\nExecute the following to verify the events below are included in the server audit specification:\nSCHEMA_OBJECT_CHANGE_GROUP\n\nSELECT a.name AS 'AuditName',\ns.name AS 'SpecName',\nd.audit_action_name AS 'ActionName',\nd.audited_result AS 'Result'\nFROM sys.server_audit_specifications s\nJOIN sys.server_audits a ON s.audit_guid = a.audit_guid\nJOIN sys.server_audit_specification_details d ON s.server_specification_id = d.server_specification_id\nWHERE a.is_state_enabled = 1\nAND d.audit_action_name IN (\n'SCHEMA_OBJECT_CHANGE_GROUP'\n)\nOrder by d.audit_action_name\n\nIf the identified groups are not returned, this is a finding.","rule_title":"SQL Server must generate audit records when successful and unsuccessful attempts to modify or delete security objects occur."},{"group_title":"SRG-APP-000503-DB-000350","discussion":"For completeness of forensic analysis, it is necessary to track who/what (a user or other principal) logs on to SQL Server. It is also necessary to track failed attempts to log on to SQL Server. While positive identification may not be possible in a case of failed authentication, as much information as possible about the incident must be captured.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-APP-000503-DB-000350, SRG-APP-000503-DB-000351, SRG-APP-000506-DB-000353","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271375r1111093_rule","rule_id":"SV-271375r1111093","ccis":["CCI-000172"],"mitigations":"","comments":null,"uuid":"F204048F-6BF8-1014-9925-96959F2CDC7D","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"mitigation_control":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271375"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-271375","rule_title":"SQL Server must generate audit records when successful and unsuccessful logons or connection attempts occur.","group_id":"V-271375","check_content":"Review the SQL configuration to verify that audit records are produced when denied actions occur.\n\nTo determine if an audit is configured, execute the following script:\nSELECT name AS 'Audit Name',\nstatus_desc AS 'Audit Status',\naudit_file_path AS 'Current Audit File'\nFROM sys.dm_server_audit_status\n\nIf no records are returned, this is a finding.\n\nExecute the following to verify the events below are included in the server audit specification:\nSUCCESSFUL_LOGIN_GROUP\nFAILED_LOGIN_GROUP\n\nSELECT a.name AS 'AuditName',\ns.name AS 'SpecName',\nd.audit_action_name AS 'ActionName',\nd.audited_result AS 'Result'\nFROM sys.server_audit_specifications s\nJOIN sys.server_audits a ON s.audit_guid = a.audit_guid\nJOIN sys.server_audit_specification_details d ON s.server_specification_id = d.server_specification_id\nWHERE a.is_state_enabled = 1\nAND d.audit_action_name IN (\n'SUCCESSFUL_LOGIN_GROUP',\n'FAILED_LOGIN_GROUP'\n)\nOrder by d.audit_action_name\n\nIf the identified groups are not returned, this is a finding.\n\nAlternatively: \n\n1. In SQL Management Studio, right-click on the instance.\n2. Select \"Properties\".\n3. Select \"Security\" on the left side.\n4. Check the setting for \"Login auditing\".\n \nIf \"Both failed and successful logins\" is not selected, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Add the required events to the server audit specification to audit denied actions.\n\nRefer to the supplemental file \"SQL2022Audit.sql\" script.\n\nReference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/relational-databases/security/auditing/sql-server-audit-database-engine?\n\nAlternatively, enable \"Both failed and successful logins\".\n\n1. In SQL Management Studio, right-click on the instance.\n2. Select \"Properties\".\n3.  Select \"Security\" on the left side.\n4. Select \"Both failed and successful logins\". \n5. Click \"OK\".","rule_version":"SQLI-22-014800","group_tree":{"id":"V-271375","title":"SRG-APP-000503-DB-000350"},"status":"open","weight":"10.0","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       false (FAILED_LOGIN_GROUP'SUCCESSFUL_LOGIN_GROUP'.)\nResult Analysis         :            .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n                        :             .  \nTest                    :       false (FAILED_LOGIN_GROUP 'FAILED_LOGIN_GROUP'.)\nResult Analysis         :            .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n                        :             .  \nCriteria                :     false (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :       false (Verify 'Login auditing' is set to 'both failed and successful logins' (non-Clustered))\nResult Analysis         :            Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\\\MSSQLServer\\AuditLevel'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :       false (Verify 'Login auditing' is set to 'both failed and successful logins' (Clustered))\nResult Analysis         :            Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\\\MSSQLServer\\AuditLevel'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   error (Determine if an audit is configured and started)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27137502 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : FAILED_LOGIN_GROUP'SUCCESSFUL_LOGIN_GROUP'.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27137502 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT a.name AS 'AuditName', \n                        :   s.name AS 'SpecName', \n                        :  d.audit_action_name AS 'ActionName', \n                        :   d.audited_result AS 'Result' \n                        : FROM sys.server_audit_specifications s \n                        : JOIN sys.server_audits a ON s.audit_guid = a.audit_guid \n                        : JOIN sys.server_audit_specification_details d ON s.server_specification_id = d.server_specification_id \n                        : WHERE a.is_state_enabled = 1 AND d.audit_action_name IN ('SUCCESSFUL_LOGIN_GROUP')\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t\t'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : !![ sql does not exist ]!!\n\nResult Analysis         : .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nResult Analysis         :  .  \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27137503 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : FAILED_LOGIN_GROUP 'FAILED_LOGIN_GROUP'.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27137503 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT a.name AS 'AuditName', \n                        :   s.name AS 'SpecName', \n                        :  d.audit_action_name AS 'ActionName', \n                        :   d.audited_result AS 'Result' \n                        : FROM sys.server_audit_specifications s \n                        : JOIN sys.server_audits a ON s.audit_guid = a.audit_guid \n                        : JOIN sys.server_audit_specification_details d ON s.server_specification_id = d.server_specification_id \n                        : WHERE a.is_state_enabled = 1 AND d.audit_action_name IN ('FAILED_LOGIN_GROUP')\n                        : \t\t\t\t'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : !![ sql does not exist ]!!\n\nResult Analysis         : .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nResult Analysis         :  .  \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27137504 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verify 'Login auditing' is set to 'both failed and successful logins' (non-Clustered)\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27137504 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Value of AuditLevel (Non-Clustered)\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      : for key, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     key must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\\\MSSQLServer'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AuditLevel'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27137502 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry key dword value equals 3\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '3'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\\\MSSQLServer\\AuditLevel'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27137505 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verify 'Login auditing' is set to 'both failed and successful logins' (Clustered)\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27137506 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Value of AuditLevel (Clustered)\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      : for key, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     key must be equal to '\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\\\MSSQLServer'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AuditLevel'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27137502 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry key dword value equals 3\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '3'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\\\MSSQLServer\\AuditLevel'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nError Information       : Unable to retrieve any data with SQL transaction \"SELECT NodeName as 'node_name', status, status_description, is_current_owner   \n                        : FROM sys.dm_os_cluster_nodes; from DBMS instance \"SQLEXPRESS\" on server \"SOT-WIN2K22-SQL\" Error: [Microsoft][ODBC Driver 17 for SQL Server][SQL Server]VIEW SERVER PERFORMANCE STATE permission was denied on object 'server', database 'master'. (SQL-42000)\n                        : [Microsoft][ODBC Driver 17 for SQL Server][SQL Server]The user does not have permission to perform this action. (SQL-42000)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27137501 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : error\nTest Title              : Determine if an audit is configured and started\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27137501 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name AS 'audit_name',\n                        : \t\t\t\tstatus_desc AS 'audit_status',\n                        : \t\t\t\taudit_file_path AS 'current_audit_file'\n                        : \t\t\t\tFROM sys.dm_server_audit_status'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27137501 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : If an audit is not STARTED this is a finding.\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all audit_status must be equal to 'STARTED'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : error\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT name AS 'audit_name',\n                        : \t\t\t\tstatus_desc AS 'audit_status',\n                        : \t\t\t\taudit_file_path AS 'current_audit_file'\n                        : \t\t\t\tFROM sys.dm_server_audit_status'\n\n"},{"mitigation_control":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:12901","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-271381","rule_title":"SQL Server must generate audit records for all direct access to the database(s).","group_id":"V-271381","check_content":"Determine whether any Server Audits are configured to filter records. From SQL Server Management Studio, execute the following query:\nSELECT name AS AuditName, predicate AS AuditFilter\nFROM sys.server_audits\nWHERE predicate IS NOT NULL\n\nIf any audits are returned, review the associated filters. If any direct access to the database(s) is being excluded, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Check the system documentation for required SQL Server Audits. Remove any Audit filters that exclude or reduce required auditing. Update filters to ensure direct access is not excluded.","rule_version":"SQLI-22-015500","group_tree":{"id":"V-271381","title":"SRG-APP-000508-DB-000358"},"status":"not_reviewed","weight":"10.0","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271381, SV-271381r1111095, SRG-APP-000508-DB-000358)\n","group_title":"SRG-APP-000508-DB-000358","discussion":"In this context, direct access is any query, command, or call to SQL Server that comes from any source other than the application(s) that it supports. Examples would be the command line or a database management utility program. The intent is to capture all activity from administrative and nonstandard sources.","severity":"medium","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271381r1111095_rule","rule_id":"SV-271381r1111095","ccis":["CCI-000172"],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","uuid":"F2040F08-6BF8-1014-9B66-CB2FCCB3F9B9","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[]},{"rule_id":"SV-271385r1108771","ccis":["CCI-001851"],"uuid":"F204190D-6BF8-1014-80E4-CD5FB9EFBFEF","comments":null,"mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","discussion":"Information stored in one location is vulnerable to accidental or incidental deletion or alteration. \n \nOff-loading is a common process in information systems with limited audit storage capacity. \n \nThe system SQL Server may write audit records to database tables, to files in the file system, to other kinds of local repository, or directly to a centralized log management system. Whatever the method used, it must be compatible with off-loading the records to the centralized system.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000515-DB-000318","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271385r1108771_rule","fix_text":"Configure the system or deploy and configure software tools to transfer audit records to a centralized log management system, continuously and in near-real time where a continuous network connection to the log management system exists, or at least weekly in the absence of such a connection.","false_positives":"","ia_controls":"","weight":"10.0","status":"not_reviewed","rule_version":"SQLI-22-015900","group_tree":{"id":"V-271385","title":"SRG-APP-000515-DB-000318"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271385, SV-271385r1108771, SRG-APP-000515-DB-000318)\n","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:13101","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml"},"mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-271385","rule_title":"The system SQL Server must off-load audit data to a separate log management facility; this must be continuous and in near real time for systems with a network connection to the storage facility and weekly or more often for stand-alone systems.","check_content":"Review the system documentation for a description of how audit records are off-loaded. \n \nIf the system has a continuous network connection to the centralized log management system, but the DBMS audit records are not written directly to the centralized log management system or transferred in near-real-time, this is a finding. \n \nIf the system does not have a continuous network connection to the centralized log management system, and the DBMS audit records are not transferred to the centralized log management system weekly or more often, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271385"},{"legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","uuid":"F2042483-6BF8-1014-9398-A5B2E2A29E07","mitigations":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_id":"SV-271387r1111140","rule_id_src":"SV-271387r1111140_rule","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","discussion":"The SQL Server Browser simplifies the administration of SQL Server, particularly when multiple instances of SQL Server coexist on the same computer. It avoids the need to hard-assign port numbers to the instances and to set and maintain those port numbers in client systems. It enables administrators and authorized users to discover database management system instances, and the databases they support, over the network. SQL Server uses the SQL Server Browser service to enumerate instances of the Database Engine installed on the computer. This enables client applications to browse for a server, and helps clients distinguish between multiple instances of the Database Engine on the same computer.\n\nThis convenience also presents the possibility of unauthorized individuals gaining knowledge of the available SQL Server resources. Therefore, it is necessary to consider whether the SQL Server Browser is needed. Typically, if only a single instance is installed, using the default name (MSSQLSERVER) and port assignment (1433), the Browser is not adding any value. The more complex the installation, the more likely SQL Server Browser is to be helpful. \n\nThis requirement is not intended to prohibit use of the Browser service in any circumstances. It calls for administrators and management to consider whether the benefits of its use outweigh the potential negative consequences of it being used by an attacker to browse the current infrastructure and retrieve a list of running SQL Server instances.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516-DB-000363","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (SQL Server Browser service should be Disabled if found)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27138701 (service_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : SQL Server Browser service should be Disabled if found\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27138701 (service_object)\nObject Comment          : SQL Server Browser Service\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'service_name' must be equal to 'SQLBrowser'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27138701 (service_state)\nState Comment           : SQL query result field 'name' = 'external scripts enabled' and config_value = 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'start_type' must be equal to 'SERVICE_DISABLED'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'current_state' must be equal to 'SERVICE_STOPPED'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : service_name equals 'SQLBrowser'\n                        : display_name equals 'SQL Server Browser'\n                        : description equals 'Provides SQL Server connection information to client computers.'\n                        : service_type equals 'SERVICE_WIN32_OWN_PROCESS'\n                        : start_type equals 'SERVICE_DISABLED'\n                        : current_state equals 'SERVICE_STOPPED'\n                        : start_name equals 'NT AUTHORITY\\LOCALSERVICE'\n                        : path equals '\"C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft SQL Server\\90\\Shared\\sqlbrowser.exe\"'\n                        : pid equals '0'\n                        : service_flag equals '0'\n","weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","rule_version":"SQLI-22-017800","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000516-DB-000363","id":"V-271387"},"fix_text":"If SQL Server Browser is needed, document the justification and obtain the appropriate authorization. \n\nWhere SQL Server Browser is judged unnecessary, the Service can be disabled. \n\nTo disable, in the Services tool, double-click \"SQL Server Browser\". Set \"Startup Type\" to \"Disabled\". If \"Service Status\" is \"Running\", click \"Stop\" and then click \"OK\".","false_positives":"","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Open SQL Server Configuration Manager. Select SQL Server Services. Review the Start Mode and State of SQL Server Browser.\n\nIf its Start Type is shown as \"Disabled\", this is not a finding.\n\nIf the need for the SQL Server Browser service is documented and authorized, verify the SQL Instances that do not require use of the SQL Browser Service are hidden with the following SQL script:\nDECLARE @HiddenInstance INT \nEXEC master.dbo.Xp_instance_regread \n N'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE', \n N'Software\\Microsoft\\MSSQLServer\\MSSQLServer\\SuperSocketNetLib', \n N'HideInstance', \n @HiddenInstance output \n\nSELECT CASE \n        WHEN @HiddenInstance = 0 \n             AND Serverproperty('IsClustered') = 0 THEN 'No' \n        ELSE 'Yes' \n      END AS [Hidden]\n\nIf the value of \"Hidden\" is \"Yes\", this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value of \"Hidden\" is \"No\" and the startup type of the \"SQL Server Browser\" service is not \"Disabled\", this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271387","rule_title":"The SQL Server Browser service must be disabled unless specifically required and approved.","group_id_src":"V-271387","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271387"},"mitigation_control":""},{"group_id_src":"V-271388","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:13501","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":"","check_content":"Review the server documentation to determine if auditing of the telemetry data is required. If auditing of telemetry data is not required, this is not a finding. \n \nIf auditing of telemetry data is required, determine the telemetry service username by executing the following query: \nSELECT name \nFROM sys.server_principals \nWHERE name LIKE '%SQLTELEMETRY%' \n \nReview the values of the following registry key: \nNote: InstanceId refers to the type and instance of the feature (e.g., MSSQL16.SqlInstance, MSAS16.SSASInstance, MSRS16.SSRSInstance). \n \nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\[InstanceId]\\CPE\\UserRequestedLocalAuditDirectory \n \nIf the registry key does not exist or the value is blank, this is a finding. \n \nNavigate the path defined in the \"UserRequestedLocalAuditDirectory\" registry key in file explorer. \n \nRight-click on the folder and choose \"Properties\". Open the \"Security\" tab.\n \nVerify the SQLTELEMETRY account has the following permissions: \n- List folder contents \n- Read \n- Write \n \nIf the permissions are not set properly on the folder, this is a finding. \n \nOpen services.msc and find the telemetry service. \n- For Database Engine, use SQL Server CEIP service (&lt;INSTANCENAME&gt;). \n- For Analysis Services, use SQL Server Analysis Services CEIP (&lt;INSTANCENAME&gt;). \n \nRight-click on the service and choose \"Properties\". Verify the \"Startup type\" is \"Automatic.\"  \n \nIf the service is not configured to automatically start, this is a finding. \n \nReview the processes and procedures for reviewing the telemetry data. If there is evidence that the telemetry data is periodically reviewed in accordance with the processes and procedures, this is not a finding. \n \nIf no processes and procedures exist for reviewing telemetry data, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271388","rule_title":"SQL Server must configure SQL Server Usage and Error Reporting Auditing.","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Configure the instance to audit telemetry data. More information about auditing telemetry data can be found at https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/mt743085.aspx. \n \nCreate a folder to store the telemetry audit data in. \n \nGrant the SQLTELEMETRY service the following permissions on the folder: \n- List folder contents \n- Read \n- Write \n \nCreate and configure the following registry key: \nNote: InstanceId refers to the type and instance of the feature. (e.g., MSSQL16.SqlInstance, MSAS16.SSASInstance, MSRS16.SSRSInstance) \n \nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\[InstanceId]\\CPE\\UserRequestedLocalAuditDirectory [string] \n \nSet the \"UserRequestedLocalAuditDirectory\" key value to the path of the telemetry audit folder. \n \nSet the telemetry service to start automatically. Restart the service. \n- For Database Engine, use SQL Server CEIP service (&lt;INSTANCENAME&gt;). \n- For Analysis Services, use SQL Server Analysis Services CEIP (&lt;INSTANCENAME&gt;).","ia_controls":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271388, SV-271388r1111098, SRG-APP-000516-DB-000363)\n","weight":"10.0","status":"not_reviewed","rule_version":"SQLI-22-016100","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000516-DB-000363","id":"V-271388"},"reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","discussion":"By default, Microsoft SQL Server enables participation in the customer experience improvement program (CEIP). This program collects information about how its customers are using the product. Specifically, SQL Server collects information about the installation experience, feature usage, and performance. This information helps Microsoft improve the product to better meet customer needs. The Local Audit component of SQL Server Usage Feedback collection writes data collected by the service to a designated folder, representing the data (logs) that will be sent to Microsoft. The purpose of the Local Audit is to allow customers to view all data Microsoft collects with this feature, for compliance, regulatory or privacy validation reasons.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516-DB-000363","rule_id_src":"SV-271388r1111098_rule","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_id":"SV-271388r1111098","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","mitigations":"","comments":null,"uuid":"F20434D8-6BF8-1014-BA27-D2BC58399CE0"},{"weight":"10.0","status":"open","rule_version":"SQLI-22-016000","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000516-DB-000363","id":"V-271389"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Verify if Customer Feedback is Disabled)\nResult Analysis         :        HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\CustomerFeedback\\value = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n                        : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\MSSQL16.SQLEXPRESS\\CPE\\CustomerFeedback\\value = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \nTest                    :   false (Verify if Error Reporting is Disabled)\nResult Analysis         :        HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\EnableErrorReporting\\value = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n                        : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\MSSQL16.SQLEXPRESS\\CPE\\EnableErrorReporting\\value = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27138901 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verify if Customer Feedback is Disabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27138901 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Find all of the CustomerFeedback values under HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server'.\nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  recurse_direction = down\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'CustomerFeedback'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27138901 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry key dword value equals 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160'\n                        : name equals 'CustomerFeedback'\n                        : last_write_time equals '133514425930000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\MSSQL16.SQLEXPRESS\\CPE'\n                        : name equals 'CustomerFeedback'\n                        : last_write_time equals '133513638180000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nResult Analysis         : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\CustomerFeedback\\value = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n                        : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\MSSQL16.SQLEXPRESS\\CPE\\CustomerFeedback\\value = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27138902 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verify if Error Reporting is Disabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27138902 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Find all of the EnableErrorReporting values under HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server'.\nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  recurse_direction = down\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnableErrorReporting'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27138901 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry key dword value equals 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160'\n                        : name equals 'EnableErrorReporting'\n                        : last_write_time equals '133514425930000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\MSSQL16.SQLEXPRESS\\CPE'\n                        : name equals 'EnableErrorReporting'\n                        : last_write_time equals '133513638180000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nResult Analysis         : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\EnableErrorReporting\\value = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n                        : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\MSSQL16.SQLEXPRESS\\CPE\\EnableErrorReporting\\value = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n","false_positives":"","fix_text":"To disable participation in the CEIP program, change the value of the following registry keys to \"0\". \n \nTo enable participation in the CEIP program, change the value of the following registry keys to \"1\". \n \nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\[InstanceId]\\CPE\\CustomerFeedback \nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\[InstanceId]\\CPE\\EnableErrorReporting \nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\CustomerFeedback \nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\EnableErrorReporting\n\nOr in PowerShell, run:\n\nSet-ItemProperty -Path \"HKLM:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\[InstanceId]\\CPE\" -Name CustomerFeedback -Value 0\nSet-ItemProperty -Path \"HKLM:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\[InstanceId]\\CPE\" -Name EnableErrorReporting -Value 0\nSet-ItemProperty -Path \"HKLM:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\" -Name CustomerFeedback -Value 0\nSet-ItemProperty -Path \"HKLM:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\" -Name EnableErrorReporting -Value 0 ","ia_controls":"","rule_title":"SQL Server must configure Customer Feedback and Error Reporting.","check_content":"Review the values for CustomerFeedback and EnableErrorReporting.\n\nOption 1:\nLaunch \"Registry Editor\" \n \nNavigate to:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\[InstanceId]\\CPE \nReview the following values: CustomerFeedback, EnableErrorReporting \n \nNavigate to HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160 \nReview the following values: CustomerFeedback, EnableErrorReporting \n \nOption 2:\nRun the PowerShell commands:\n\nGet-ItemProperty -Path \"HKLM:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\&lt;SqlInstanceId&gt;\\CPE\"\nGet-ItemProperty -Path \"HKLM:\\ Software\\Microsoft\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\"\n\nReview the following values: CustomerFeedback, EnableErrorReporting\n\nIf this is a classified system, and any of the above values are not \"0\", this is a finding. \n \nIf this is an unclassified system, review the server documentation to determine whether CEIP participation is authorized. \n \nIf CEIP participation is not authorized, and any of the above values are \"1\", this is a finding.","group_id":"V-271389","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:271389","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-271389","comments":null,"mitigations":"","uuid":"F2043F37-6BF8-1014-B1E9-F278FF567FE8","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","rule_id":"SV-271389r1109133","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271389r1109133_rule","discussion":"By default, Microsoft SQL Server enables participation in the customer experience improvement program (CEIP). This program collects information about how its customers are using the product. Specifically, SQL Server collects information about the installation experience, feature usage, and performance. This information helps Microsoft improve the product to better meet customer needs.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516-DB-000363","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","severity":"medium"},{"rule_id":"SV-271400r1167497","ccis":["CCI-004063"],"mitigations":"","comments":null,"uuid":"F2044C56-6BF8-1014-B206-F8B58BFB83B9","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"group_title":"SRG-APP-000855-DB-000240","discussion":"Password-based authentication applies to passwords regardless of whether they are used in single-factor or multifactor authentication. Long passwords or passphrases are preferable over shorter passwords. Enforced composition rules provide marginal security benefits while decreasing usability. However, organizations may choose to establish certain rules for password generation (e.g., minimum character length for long passwords) under certain circumstances and can enforce this requirement in IA-5(1)(h). Account recovery can occur, for example, in situations when a password is forgotten. Cryptographically protected passwords include salted one-way cryptographic hashes of passwords. The list of commonly used, compromised, or expected passwords includes passwords obtained from previous breach corpuses, dictionary words, and repetitive or sequential characters. The list includes context-specific words, such as the name of the service, username, and derivatives thereof.","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-271400r1167497_rule","ia_controls":"","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Configure the DBMS to require immediate selection of a new password for accounts using SQL login upon account recovery.\n\nEnsure all scripts, functions, triggers, and stored procedures used to create a user or reset a user's password for SQL logins include a line similar to the following password_option:\n\nMUST_CHANGE\n\nIf MUST_CHANGE is specified, CHECK_EXPIRATION and CHECK_POLICY must be set to ON. Otherwise, the statement will fail.\n\nMore information can be found at https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/t-sql/statements/alter-login-transact-sql?view=sql-server-ver16.","rule_version":"SQLI-22-019500","group_tree":{"id":"V-271400","title":"SRG-APP-000855-DB-000240"},"weight":"10.0","status":"not_reviewed","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-271400, SV-271400r1167497, SRG-APP-000855-DB-000240)\n","mitigation_control":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.sql.server:questionnaire:13901"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-271400","rule_title":"SQL Server must, for password-based authentication, require immediate selection of a new password upon account recovery.","group_id":"V-271400","check_content":"Check for use of SQL Server Authentication:\n\nSELECT CASE SERVERPROPERTY('IsIntegratedSecurityOnly') WHEN 1 THEN 'Windows Authentication' WHEN 0 THEN 'SQL Server Authentication' END as [Authentication Mode]\n\nIf the returned value in the \"Authentication Mode\" column is \"Windows Authentication\", this is not a finding.\n\nIf the returned value is not \"Windows Authentication\", verify SQL Server is configured to require immediate selection of a new password upon account recovery.\n\nAll scripts, functions, triggers, and stored procedures used to create a user or reset a user's password for SQL logins should include a line similar to the following password_option:\n\nMUST_CHANGE\n\nExample:\nCREATE LOGIN STIG_test WITH PASSWORD ='Password' MUST_CHANGE, \n     CHECK_EXPIRATION = ON,\n     CHECK_POLICY = ON;\n\nIf they do not, this is a finding.\n\nIf SQL Server is not configured to require immediate selection of a new password upon account recovery for accounts using SQL login, this is a finding."},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Check if the SQL Server default [sa] (system administrator) account has been disabled.)\nResult Analysis         :        is_disabled = '0' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27444401 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Check if the SQL Server default [sa] (system administrator) account has been disabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27444401 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name, is_disabled FROM master.sys.sql_logins WHERE [principal_id] = 1;'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27444401 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : SQL query field 'is_disabled' = 1\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all is_disabled must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT name, is_disabled FROM master.sys.sql_logins WHERE [principal_id] = 1;'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : !![ is_disabled = '0' ]!!\n\nResult Analysis         : is_disabled = '0' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \n","status":"open","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-274444","title":"SRG-APP-000033-DB-000084"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-016200","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Modify the enabled flag of SQL Server's [sa] (system administrator) account by running the following script:\nUSE master; \nGO \nALTER LOGIN [sa] DISABLE; \nGO","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Check SQL Server settings to determine if the [sa] (system administrator) account has been disabled by executing the following query: \nUSE master;\nGO\nSELECT name, is_disabled\nFROM sys.sql_logins\nWHERE principal_id = 1;\nGO\n\nVerify that the \"name\" column contains the current name of the [sa] database server account.\n\nIf the \"is_disabled\" column is not set to \"1\", this is a finding.","group_id":"V-274444","rule_title":"The SQL Server default account [sa] must be disabled.","group_id_src":"V-274444","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:274444"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":"","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","mitigations":"","comments":null,"uuid":"F20456BA-6BF8-1014-BE72-9CDCC092C750","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"rule_id":"SV-274444r1137654","rule_id_src":"SV-274444r1137654_rule","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","security_override_guidance":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","severity":"medium","discussion":"SQL Server's [sa] account has special privileges required to administer the database. The [sa] account is a well-known SQL Server account and is likely to be targeted by attackers and thus more prone to providing unauthorized access to the database. \n\nThis [sa] default account is administrative and could lead to catastrophic consequences, including the complete loss of control over SQL Server. If the [sa] default account is not disabled, an attacker might be able to gain access through the account. SQL Server by default disables the [sa] account at installation. \n\nSome applications that run on SQL Server require the [sa] account to be enabled for the application to function properly. These applications that require the [sa] account to be enabled are usually legacy systems.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000033-DB-000084"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Check if the SQL Server default [sa] (system administrator) account name has been changed.)\nResult Analysis         :        Existence requirement is 'none_exists' and 1 collected item exists, so result is false\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27444501 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Check if the SQL Server default [sa] (system administrator) account name has been changed.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27444501 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name FROM master.sys.sql_logins WHERE [name] = 'sa';'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT name FROM master.sys.sql_logins WHERE [name] = 'sa';'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n\nResult Analysis         : Existence requirement is 'none_exists' and 1 collected item exists, so result is false\n","weight":"10.0","status":"open","rule_version":"SQLI-22-016300","group_tree":{"id":"V-274445","title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000092"},"false_positives":"","fix_text":"Modify the SQL Server's [sa] (system administrator) account by running the following script:\n\nUSE master; \nGO \nALTER LOGIN [sa] WITH NAME = &lt;new name&gt; \nGO","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the SQL Server default [sa] (system administrator) account name has been changed by executing the following query:\nUSE master; \nGO \nSELECT * \nFROM sys.sql_logins \nWHERE [name] = 'sa' OR [principal_id] = 1; \nGO \n\nIf the login account name \"SA\" or \"sa\" appears in the query output, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-274445","rule_title":"The SQL Server default account [sa] must have its name changed.","group_id_src":"V-274445","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:274445"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":"","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","comments":null,"mitigations":"","uuid":"F204608C-6BF8-1014-AA13-EBE216B9FFED","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_id":"SV-274445r1111103","rule_id_src":"SV-274445r1111103_rule","third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","severity":"medium","discussion":"SQL Server's [sa] account has special privileges required to administer the database. The [sa] account is a well-known SQL Server account name and is likely to be targeted by attackers, and is thus more prone to providing unauthorized access to the database. \n\nSince the SQL Server [sa] is administrative in nature, the compromise of a default account can have catastrophic consequences, including the complete loss of control over SQL Server. Since SQL Server needs for this account to exist and it should not be removed, one way to mitigate this risk is to change the [sa] account name.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000092"},{"group_id_src":"V-274446","mitigation_control":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:274446"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-274446","check_content":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:var:27444604;;Instance;;stored_proc;;Array","rule_title":"Execution of startup stored procedures must be restricted to necessary cases only.","ia_controls":"","false_positives":"","fix_text":"To disable startup stored procedure(s), run the following in Master for each undocumented procedure:\nsp_procoption @procname = '&lt;procedure name&gt;', @OptionName = 'Startup', @optionValue = 'Off'","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (If no stored procedures are returned, or if all stored procedures are returned that are documented, this is not a finding.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27444602 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If no stored procedures are returned, or if all stored procedures are returned that are documented, this is not a finding.\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27444601 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'Select [name] as stored_proc\n                        : From sys.procedures\n                        : Where OBJECTPROPERTY(OBJECT_ID, 'ExecIsStartup') = 1\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27444601 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : If all stored procedures are returned are documented, this is not a finding.\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : Field Requirement       : for at least one stored_proc, at least one of the following must be true:\n                        : Field Requirement       : stored_proc must be equal to  the value(s) in End user provided list of documented and approved stored procedures\n                        : Field Requirement       :     stored_proc must be equal to ''\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql does not exist\n","rule_version":"SQLI-22-016400","group_tree":{"id":"V-274446","title":"SRG-APP-000342-DB-000302"},"weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","severity":"medium","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5677","group_title":"SRG-APP-000342-DB-000302","discussion":"In certain situations, to provide required functionality, a DBMS needs to execute internal logic (stored procedures, functions, triggers, etc.) and/or external code modules with elevated privileges. However, if the privileges required for execution are at a higher level than the privileges assigned to organizational users invoking the functionality applications/programs, those users are indirectly provided with greater privileges than assigned by organizations.\n\nWhen \"Scan for startup procs\" is enabled, SQL Server scans for and runs all automatically run stored procedures defined on the server. The execution of start-up stored procedures will be done under a high privileged context; therefore, it is a commonly used post-exploitation vector.","rule_id_src":"SV-274446r1111106_rule","security_override_guidance":"","third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-002233"],"rule_id":"SV-274446r1111106","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","uuid":"F2046AAA-6BF8-1014-8EF6-E237CA785657"},{"ia_controls":"","fix_text":"Run the following to enable encryption on the mirroring endpoint:\nALTER ENDPOINT &lt;Endpoint Name&gt;\nFOR DATABASE_MIRRORING\n(ENCRYPTION = REQUIRED ALGORITHM AES)","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (If any records are returned, this is a finding.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27444701 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If any records are returned, this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27444701 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name, type_desc, encryption_algorithm_desc\n                        : FROM sys.database_mirroring_endpoints\n                        : WHERE encryption_algorithm != 2\n                        : \t\t\t\t\t'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql does not exist\n","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000516-DB-000363","id":"V-274447"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-016500","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-274447","mitigation_control":"","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:274447","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"group_id":"V-274447","check_content":"If the data owner does not have a strict requirement for ensuring data integrity and confidentiality is maintained at every step of the data transfer and handling process, and the requirement is documented and authorized, this is not a finding.\n\nIf Database Mirroring is in use, run the following to check for encrypted transmissions:\nSELECT name, type_desc, encryption_algorithm_desc\nFROM sys.database_mirroring_endpoints\nWHERE encryption_algorithm != 2\n\nIf any records are returned, this is a finding.","rule_title":"The SQL Server Mirroring endpoint must use AES encryption.","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_id":"SV-274447r1111109","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"uuid":"F204779B-6BF8-1014-99AF-988611A262EF","mitigations":"","comments":null,"severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516-DB-000363","discussion":"Information can be unintentionally or maliciously disclosed or modified during preparation for transmission, including, for example, during aggregation, at protocol transformation points, and during packing/unpacking. These unauthorized disclosures or modifications compromise the confidentiality or integrity of the information.\n\nUse of this requirement will be limited to situations where the data owner has a strict requirement for ensuring data integrity and confidentiality is maintained at every step of the data transfer and handling process. \n\nSQL Mirroring endpoints support different encryption algorithms, including no-encryption. Using a weak encryption algorithm or plaintext in communication protocols can lead to data loss, data manipulation, and/or connection hijacking.","rule_id_src":"SV-274447r1111109_rule","security_override_guidance":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":""},{"group_title":"SRG-APP-000516-DB-000363","discussion":"Information can be unintentionally or maliciously disclosed or modified during preparation for transmission, including, for example, during aggregation, at protocol transformation points, and during packing/unpacking. These unauthorized disclosures or modifications compromise the confidentiality or integrity of the information.\n\nUse of this requirement will be limited to situations where the data owner has a strict requirement for ensuring that data integrity and confidentiality is maintained at every step of the data transfer and handling process. \n\nSQL Server Service Broker endpoints support different encryption algorithms, including no-encryption. Using a weak encryption algorithm or plaintext in communication protocols can lead to data loss, data manipulation, and/or connection hijacking.","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-274448r1111112_rule","rule_id":"SV-274448r1111112","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"uuid":"F204835D-6BF8-1014-BB4B-8C4520788722","comments":null,"mitigations":"","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"mitigation_control":"","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:274448"},"group_id_src":"V-274448","rule_title":"The SQL Server Service Broker endpoint must use AES encryption.","group_id":"V-274448","check_content":"If the data owner does not have a strict requirement for ensuring data integrity and confidentiality is maintained at every step of the data transfer and handling process, and the requirement is documented and authorized, this is not a finding.\n\nIf SQL Service Broker is in use, run the following to check for encrypted transmissions:\nSELECT name, type_desc, encryption_algorithm_desc\nFROM sys.service_broker_endpoints\nWHERE encryption_algorithm != 2\n\nIf any records are returned, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","fix_text":"Run the following to enable encryption on the Service Broker endpoint:\nALTER ENDPOINT &lt;EndpointName&gt;\nFOR SERVICE_BROKER\n(ENCRYPTION = REQUIRED ALGORITHM AES)","false_positives":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-274448","title":"SRG-APP-000516-DB-000363"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-016600","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (If any records are returned, this is a finding.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27444801 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If any records are returned, this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27444801 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name, type_desc, encryption_algorithm_desc\n                        : FROM sys.service_broker_endpoints\n                        : WHERE encryption_algorithm != 2\n                        : \t\t\t\t'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql does not exist\n"},{"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_id":"SV-274449r1111115","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","comments":null,"uuid":"F2048E55-6BF8-1014-8750-E368BB738853","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093","discussion":"Information systems are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the functions and services, provided by default, may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n\nIt is detrimental for applications to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. \n\nApplications must adhere to the principles of least functionality by providing only essential capabilities.\n\nSQL Server may spawn additional external processes to execute procedures that are defined in the SQL Server but stored in external host files (external procedures). The spawned process used to execute the external procedure may operate within a different operating system security context than SQL Server and provide unauthorized access to the host system.\n\nThe registry contains sensitive information, including password hashes and clear text passwords. Registry extended stored procedures allow Microsoft SQL Server to access the machine's registry. The sensitivity of these procedures is exacerbated if Microsoft SQL Server is run under the Windows account LocalSystem. LocalSystem can read and write nearly all values in the registry, even those not accessible by the administrator. Unlike the xp_cmdshell extended stored procedure, which runs under a separate context if executed by a login not in the sysadmin role, the registry extended stored procedures always execute under the security context of the MSSQLServer service. Because the sensitive information is stored in the registry, it is essential that access to that information be properly guarded.","rule_id_src":"SV-274449r1111115_rule","security_override_guidance":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","ia_controls":"","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Remove execute permissions to any registry extended stored procedure from all users (other than dbo):\nUSE master\nGO\nREVOKE EXECUTE ON [&lt;procedureName&gt;] FROM [&lt;principal&gt;]\nGO","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Registry extended stored procedures have been revoked from all users)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27444901 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Registry extended stored procedures have been revoked from all users\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27444901 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT OBJECT_NAME(major_id) AS [Stored Procedure]\n                        : ,dpr.NAME AS [Principal]\n                        : FROM sys.database_permissions AS dp\n                        : INNER JOIN sys.database_principals AS dpr ON dp.grantee_principal_id = dpr.principal_id\n                        : WHERE major_id IN (\n                        :  OBJECT_ID('xp_regaddmultistring')\n                        : ,OBJECT_ID('xp_regdeletekey')\n                        : ,OBJECT_ID('xp_regdeletevalue')\n                        : ,OBJECT_ID('xp_regenumvalues')\n                        : ,OBJECT_ID('xp_regenumkeys')\n                        : ,OBJECT_ID('xp_regremovemultistring')\n                        : ,OBJECT_ID('xp_regwrite')\n                        : ,OBJECT_ID('xp_instance_regaddmultistring')\n                        : ,OBJECT_ID('xp_instance_regdeletekey')\n                        : ,OBJECT_ID('xp_instance_regdeletevalue')\n                        : ,OBJECT_ID('xp_instance_regenumkeys')\n                        : ,OBJECT_ID('xp_instance_regenumvalues')\n                        : ,OBJECT_ID('xp_instance_regremovemultistring')\n                        : ,OBJECT_ID('xp_instance_regwrite')\n                        : )\n                        : AND dp.[type] = 'EX'\n                        : ORDER BY dpr.NAME;'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql does not exist\n","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093","id":"V-274449"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-016700","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-274449","mitigation_control":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:274449"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-274449","check_content":"To determine if permissions to execute registry extended stored procedures have been revoked from all users (other than dbo), execute the following command:\nSELECT OBJECT_NAME(major_id) AS [Stored Procedure]\n,dpr.NAME AS [Principal]\nFROM sys.database_permissions AS dp\nINNER JOIN sys.database_principals AS dpr ON dp.grantee_principal_id = dpr.principal_id\nWHERE major_id IN (\n OBJECT_ID('xp_regaddmultistring')\n,OBJECT_ID('xp_regdeletekey')\n,OBJECT_ID('xp_regdeletevalue')\n,OBJECT_ID('xp_regenumvalues')\n,OBJECT_ID('xp_regenumkeys')\n,OBJECT_ID('xp_regremovemultistring')\n,OBJECT_ID('xp_regwrite')\n,OBJECT_ID('xp_instance_regaddmultistring')\n,OBJECT_ID('xp_instance_regdeletekey')\n,OBJECT_ID('xp_instance_regdeletevalue')\n,OBJECT_ID('xp_instance_regenumkeys')\n,OBJECT_ID('xp_instance_regenumvalues')\n,OBJECT_ID('xp_instance_regremovemultistring')\n,OBJECT_ID('xp_instance_regwrite')\n)\nAND dp.[type] = 'EX'\nORDER BY dpr.NAME;\n\nIf any records are returned, review the system documentation to determine if accessing the registry via extended stored procedures is required and authorized. If it is not authorized, this is a finding.","rule_title":"SQL Server execute permissions to access the registry must be revoked unless specifically required and approved."},{"third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-274450r1111117_rule","discussion":"Information systems are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the functions and services, provided by default, may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n\nIt is detrimental for applications to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. \n\nApplications must adhere to the principles of least functionality by providing only essential capabilities.\n\nThe most significant potential for attacking an instance is through the use of features that expose an external interface or ad hoc execution capability. FILESTREAM integrates the SQL Server Database Engine with an NTFS file system by storing varbinary(max) binary large object (BLOB) data as files on the file system. Transact-SQL statements can insert, update, query, search, and back up FILESTREAM data.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","comments":null,"mitigations":"","uuid":"F204991F-6BF8-1014-AE26-B83827B46E89","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","rule_id":"SV-274450r1111117","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_title":"Filestream must be disabled unless specifically required and approved.","check_content":"Review the system documentation to determine if FileStream is in use. If in use and authorized, this is not a finding.   \n\nIf FileStream is not documented as being authorized, execute the following query:\nEXEC sp_configure 'filestream access level'\n\nIf \"run_value\" is greater than \"0\", this is a finding.\n\nThis rule checks that the Filestream SQL-specific option is disabled.\nSELECT CASE \n        WHEN EXISTS (SELECT * \n                     FROM sys.configurations \n                     WHERE Name = 'filestream access level' \n                            AND Cast(value AS INT) = 0) THEN 'No' \n        ELSE 'Yes'\n      END AS TSQLFileStreamAccess;\n\nIf the above query returns \"Yes\" in the \"FileStreamEnabled\" field, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-274450","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:274450"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-274450","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"SQLI-22-016800","group_tree":{"id":"V-274450","title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true ('filestream access level' must be = 0)\nTest                    :   true ('FileStreamEnabled' must be = 'No')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27445001 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'filestream access level' must be = 0\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27445001 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'filestream access level''\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27445001 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : If for name 'filestream access level, and 'value_in_use' is not '0', this is a finding.\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all name must be equal (case insensitive) to 'filestream access level'\n                        : all value_in_use must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'filestream access level''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : name = 'filestream access level'\n                        : value = '0'\n                        : value_in_use = '0'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27445002 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'FileStreamEnabled' must be = 'No'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27445002 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT CASE \n                        : WHEN EXISTS (SELECT * \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE Name = 'filestream access level' \n                        : \tAND Cast(value AS INT) = 0) THEN 'No' \n                        : ELSE 'Yes'\n                        : END AS tsql_file_stream_access;'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27445002 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : If 'run_value' is greater than '0', this is a finding.\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all tsql_file_stream_access must not be equal to 'Yes'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT CASE \n                        : WHEN EXISTS (SELECT * \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE Name = 'filestream access level' \n                        : \tAND Cast(value AS INT) = 0) THEN 'No' \n                        : ELSE 'Yes'\n                        : END AS tsql_file_stream_access;'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : tsql_file_stream_access = 'No'\n","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Disable the use of Filestream.\n\n1. Delete all FILESTREAM columns from all tables. ALTER TABLE &lt;name&gt; DROP COLUMN &lt;column name&gt;\n2. Disassociate tables from the FILESTREAM filegroups. ALTER TABLE &lt;name&gt; SET (FILESTREAM_ON = 'NULL'\n3. Remove all FILESTREAM data containers. ALTER DATABASE &lt;name&gt; REMOVE FILE &lt;file name&gt;\n4. Remove all FILESTREAM filegroups. ALTER DATABASE &lt;name&gt; REMOVE FILEGROUP &lt;file name&gt;\n5. Disable FILESTREAM.\nEXEC sp_configure filestream_access_level, 0 \n    RECONFIGURE \n6. Restart the SQL Service.","ia_controls":""},{"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_id":"SV-274451r1111120","legacy_ids":[],"documentable":"false","uuid":"F204A4A8-6BF8-1014-80A1-D9545606D829","comments":null,"mitigations":"","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","discussion":"Information systems are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the functions and services, provided by default, may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n\nIt is detrimental for applications to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. \n\nApplications must adhere to the principles of least functionality by providing only essential capabilities.\n\nSQL Server may spawn additional external processes to execute procedures that are defined in the SQL Server but stored in external host files (external procedures). The spawned process used to execute the external procedure may operate within a different operating system security context than SQL Server and provide unauthorized access to the host system.\n\nSQL Server is capable of providing a wide range of features and services. Some of the features and services, provided by default, may not be necessary, and enabling them could adversely affect system security.\n\nThe \"Ole Automation Procedures\" option controls whether OLE Automation objects can be instantiated within Transact-SQL batches. These are extended stored procedures that allow SQL Server users to execute functions external to SQL Server in the security context of SQL Server.\n\nThe \"Ole Automation Procedures\" extended stored procedure allows execution of host executables outside the controls of database access permissions. This access may be exploited by malicious users who have compromised the integrity of the SQL Server database process to control the host operating system to perpetrate additional malicious activity.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093","rule_id_src":"SV-274451r1111120_rule","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","security_override_guidance":"","fix_text":"Disable use of or remove any external application executable object definitions that are not authorized. To disable the use of \"Ole Automation Procedures\" option, from the query prompt:\nsp_configure 'show advanced options', 1;  \nGO  \nRECONFIGURE;  \nGO  \nsp_configure 'Ole Automation Procedures', 0;  \nGO  \nRECONFIGURE;  \nGO","false_positives":"","ia_controls":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (If the value of 'config_value' is '0', this is not a finding.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27445101 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If the value of 'config_value' is '0', this is not a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27445101 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'Ole Automation Procedures''\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27445101 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : SQL query result field 'name' = 'Ole Automation Procedures' and config_value = 0\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all name must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Ole Automation Procedures'\n                        : all value_in_use must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'Ole Automation Procedures''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : value_in_use = '0'\n                        : value = '0'\n                        : name = 'Ole Automation Procedures'\n","weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093","id":"V-274451"},"rule_version":"SQLI-22-017000","group_id_src":"V-274451","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:274451"},"mitigation_control":"","check_content":"To determine if the \"Ole Automation Procedures\" option is enabled, execute the following query: \nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'show advanced options', '1'; \nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE; \nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'Ole Automation Procedures'; \n\nIf the value of \"config_value\" is \"0\", this is not a finding. \n\nIf the value of \"config_value\" is \"1\", review the system documentation to determine whether the use of \"Ole Automation Procedures\" is required and authorized. If it is not authorized, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-274451","rule_title":"The Ole Automation Procedures feature must be disabled unless specifically required and approved."},{"security_override_guidance":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-274452r1111123_rule","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093","discussion":"SQL Server is capable of providing a wide range of features and services. Some of the features and services, provided by default, may not be necessary, and enabling them could adversely affect system security.\n\nThe \"user options\" option specifies global defaults for all users. A list of default query processing options is established for the duration of a user's work session. The \"user options\" option enables changing the default values of the SET options (if the server's default settings are not appropriate).","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5677","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","comments":null,"uuid":"F204AEFC-6BF8-1014-BD29-8189D0F92140","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"rule_id":"SV-274452r1111123","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_title":"The SQL Server User Options feature must be disabled unless specifically required and approved.","group_id":"V-274452","check_content":"To determine if \"User Options\" option is enabled, execute the following query:\nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'show advanced options', '1'; \nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE; \nEXEC SP_CONFIGURE 'user options'; \n\nIf the value of \"config_value\" is \"0\", this is not a finding. \n\nIf the value of \"config_value\" is \"1\", review the system documentation to determine whether the use of \"user options\" is required and authorized. If it is not authorized, this is a finding.","mitigation_control":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:def:274452","href":"U_MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_V1R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV7-oval2.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-274452","rule_version":"SQLI-22-017100","group_tree":{"id":"V-274452","title":"SRG-APP-000141-DB-000093"},"status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:10:14\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (If the value of 'config_value' is '0', this is not a finding.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:tst:27445201 (sqlext_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If the value of 'config_value' is '0', this is not a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:obj:27445201 (sqlext_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  context = instance\nObject Requirement      : for engine, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     engine must be equal to 'sqlserver'\nObject Requirement      : for version, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     version must match the pattern '2016|2017|2019|2022'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'sql' must be equal to 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'user options''\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.sql.server.inst:ste:27445201 (sqlext_state)\nState Comment           : SQL query result field 'name' = 'user options' and config_value = 0\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all name must be equal (case insensitive) to 'user options'\n                        : all value_in_use must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : engine equals 'sqlserver'\n                        : version equals '2022'\n                        : instance equals 'SQLEXPRESS'\n                        : database equals ''\n                        : sql equals 'SELECT name, value, value_in_use \n                        : FROM sys.configurations \n                        : WHERE name = 'user options''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : name = 'user options'\n                        : value_in_use = '0'\n                        : value = '0'\n","ia_controls":"","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Disable use of or remove any external application executable object definitions that are not authorized. To disable the use of the \"User Options\" option, from the query prompt:\nsp_configure 'show advanced options', 1;  \nGO  \nRECONFIGURE;  \nGO  \nsp_configure 'user options', 0;  \nGO  \nRECONFIGURE;  \nGO"}],"stig_id":"MS_SQL_Server_2022_Instance_STIG","version":"1","uuid":"F1F6F2AD-6BF8-1014-BF14-B6E959F636E6","size":79}],"id":"F20C876C-6BF8-1014-90DB-861F169CE9B1","title":"SCC Generated CKLB at: 2026-09-05T13:11:24"}